--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- zz_probe_ui_text.lua - RUNTIME PROBE: ARE A UNIT'S STAT VALUES READABLE
--                        FROM THE UI LAYER?  (separate from the main mod AND
--                        from zz_probe_unit_reads.lua)
--
-- WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--   Hovering a unit card in battle shows the stat values (screenshot:
--   "Melee Defence ... Base value: 53 / Hold the Line!: 5"). Those numbers are
--   therefore RENDERED BY THE UI. The engine renders a component's text from
--   the component's own state; if the engine can draw the value, script should
--   be able to READ the value back through the same component API - the same
--   access class our badge code already uses (it creates components on
--   hud_battle and writes text on them with SetText).
--
--   The UIC API dump (C:\Users\vlady\AppData\Local\Temp\wh3\uicomponent.lua,
--   141 methods) has NO GetText, but it DOES have the reads this probe uses:
--     GetStateText, GetTooltipText, CurrentState, Id,
--     Visible, VisibleFromRoot, Position
--   The published API doc documents the SAME set (and also has no GetText):
--   GetStateText "Returns the text on the current state ... This text will be
--   localised", GetTooltipText "Returns the tooltip text of the current state
--   ... as a localised string".
--
-- ROUND-3 REDESIGN - MOUSE-ARMED CAPTURE (why the timed windows came second)
--   Round 1 read only from the Lua console: moving the mouse off the stat line
--   to reach the console made the tooltip DISAPPEAR first, so every read hit a
--   dead tooltip. Round 2 fixed that by reading CONTINUOUSLY inside a few
--   bounded timer windows - and it captured the HUD walk (141 components with
--   text, hud_battle children=24) but STILL MISSED the tooltip, because the
--   tooltip only exists while the mouse is over the card and the user's hover
--   fell outside the timed windows. The lesson is the TRIGGER, not the reader:
--   the capture must be armed BY THE HOVER ITSELF.
--
--   So round 3 listens for the component mouse events (ComponentMouseOn /
--   ComponentMouseOff) - the event class the main mod's own reporter chain
--   proved reaches script in battle - and arms a SHORT 5 s / 200 ms capture the
--   moment the mouse lands on a UNIT CARD. The tooltip's components are NEW
--   when they appear, so the unchanged change-only reader catches them exactly
--   as they arrive. ROUND 7: the two 60 s auto windows are GONE - a capture
--   starts ONLY on a hover (or the manual hook zz_probe_ui_arm(seconds)).
--
--   ENGINE FACT (measured here, not guessed - README round 24, the main mod's
--   own log, and the API doc): a component only fires the 'spammy' mouse events
--   AFTER AddScriptEventReporter() has been called on it. The doc says the
--   reporter is what "cause[s] it to begin firing all events", and lists
--   ComponentMouseOn/ComponentMouseOff among them; the main mod called it on the
--   ability button and then heard the mouse. A bare listener hears NOTHING. So,
--   on every HUD walk, a component whose id looks like a unit card (its id
--   contains 'card', or carries a local unit's ui id) gets the reporter ONCE,
--   and the cards panel (card_panel_docker / cards_panel) gets it too via a
--   light sweep that also runs outside a window. The reporter is a SUBSCRIPTION,
--   not a UI-state write: no setter (SetText/SetState/...) is ever called.
--
-- ROUND 4 - TARGETED STAT DUMP (see section 7b; round 3 below is unchanged)
--   Round 3 proved the stat panel components are reachable and NAMED, each
--   carrying its OWN description as GetTooltipText (CcoUnitStat5755085424 melee
--   attack, ...4448 melee defence, ...1344 weapon damage, ...4112 armour,
--   ...5328 leadership, ...4128 charge bonus) - but EVERY CcoUnitStat* returned
--   stext="" (EMPTY), so the NUMBER is rendered somewhere round 3 did not read.
--   Round 4 therefore ADDS a targeted dump of the whole stat subtree (ROUND 7:
--   slimmed to depth 12 / 200 visits TOTAL / text-and-stat rows only), triggered
--   (a) automatically when a stat component becomes visible
--   (the unit-details panel was opened - it can be PINNED, so no mouse needed)
--   and (b) by the console hook zz_probe_stat_dump().
--   Seed roots: id starts with CcoUnitStat* | dynamic_stats | template_stat |
--   health_and_stats_parent | row_header_stats | stats_toggle; fallback = the
--   unit card subtree. ROUND 7 SLIM: depth 12, 200 visits TOTAL per dump, only
--   components with text or in the stat structure are logged, with
--   id/state/stext/tip/vis/vfr/pos and any digit flagged ***STAT-LIKE***.
--   Manual: zz_probe_stat_dump() (rescan + dump) / zz_probe_stat_dump('root id')
--   with the panel pinned open. Status: zz_probe_stat_status().
--
-- ROUND 5 - THE CROSS-UNIT EXPERIMENT (see section 10; rounds 1-4 unchanged)
--   Round 4 answered "where is a unit's stat value in the UI": the unit-info
--   panel's stat rows are dynamic_stats -> template_stat rows, each carrying a
--   stat_name child (the stat's NAME, GetStateText, e.g. "Range") and a
--   value_holder -> dy_value child (THE VALUE as text, e.g. "42"). The panel is
--   bound to the SELECTED unit. Round 5 asks the follow-up question: can the
--   panel be pointed at ANOTHER (non-selected) unit? Four labelled experiments
--   (R5.1 .. R5.4), all gated on the stat panel being visible:
--     R5.1 READ-ONLY: GetContextObjectId/GetContextObject("CcoUnitDetails" /
--          "CcoUnitStat") on dynamic_stats, a template_stat row and a dy_value
--          (the layout binds those two context types; the values are rendered
--          from CcoUnitStat.DisplayedValue / Name.RemoveTextTags).
--     R5.2 SetContextObject on dynamic_stats with each candidate in order: the
--          selected unit's script_unit, its battle_unit, the ui id as number,
--          the ui id as text, then cco("CcoUnitDetails", id) (the shape vanilla
--          battle script uses: lib_bsu.lua's ping icon) - then the same five
--          for a unit the cards say is NOT selected. After each set every
--          dy_value is re-read and compared; a detected change is logged
--          loudly and the original context object (if readable) is set back.
--     R5.3 select_in_ui: battle_unit:select_in_ui() on ONE non-selected unit,
--          with the selection set (read from the cards, the lib_bm.lua way)
--          logged before and after, and the panel re-read.
--     R5.4 SimulateMouseOn on another unit's card (cards_panel/review_DY),
--          label_compare re-read while hovered (deltas = the hovered unit),
--          then SimulateMouseOff - the doc says a simulated mouse-on STICKS
--          unless off is called, so the off call always follows.
--   Gate: the automatic run queues ONCE when the visible-stat signature
--   carries dynamic_stats (the panel opened); every test stage re-checks the
--   panel and aborts BEFORE any write if it is not there. Every write is
--   logged immediately BEFORE it happens, so a crash names its last write.
--   Caps (hard, per battle): R5.max_runs / max_sets / max_selects / max_sims.
--
-- ROUND 6 - ONE-WRITE-PER-PASS CONTEXT LADDER (see section 11; R5's AUTO ladder
--   is DISARMED - r5.auto_done = true below - because round 5's ladder died at
--   set #1/8). Offline research (all 901 shipped scripts, all layouts):
--     * cco( ) has 30 CALL SITES and ZERO Lua definitions - it is an
--       engine-registered global (same class as UIComponent,
--       also never defined in Lua). The ONLY battle-side vanilla call is the
--       ping icon: lib_battle_script_unit.lua:1872
--         uic_ping_marker:SetContextObject(cco("CcoBattleUnit",
--                                             unit:unique_ui_id()))
--       all 29 other call sites are campaign. So R6 re-checks cco at USE TIME.
--     * The REAL type ids (declared in unit_information.twui.xml):
--         "CcoUnitDetails" - dynamic_stats: ContextList CcoUnitDetails.StatList
--           (update_constant 2000 ms); the panel root unit_information carries
--           the CcoUnitDetails ContextPropagator (~line 11050), i.e. the
--           context lives on/above the root and PROPAGATES DOWN - which is why
--           a direct GetContextObjectId on dynamic_stats answered nil in R5.
--         "CcoUnitStat"    - the value component (ContextNumberFormatter
--           CcoUnitStat.DisplayedValue).
--         "CcoBattleUnit"  - unit cards; proven read in battle by
--           wh3_battle_prologue_values.lua: uic_unit_panel:GetContextObjectId(
--           "CcoBattleUnit") -> common.get_context_value("CcoBattleUnit", id, ..).
--   R6 runs THREE passes, ONE SetContextObject write per pass, target
--   dynamic_stats, and NEVER auto-advances past pass 1:
--     pass 1 (auto ONCE, CONTROL): the selected unit's own cco, built the
--            vanilla way (global cco -> core.cco/core:cco -> live read off the
--            parent chain) - if it lands and the same numbers render, the
--            mechanism is CONFIRMED; if nothing changes, STOP.
--     pass 2 (zz_probe_r6_next()): the non-selected unit's cco.
--     pass 3 (zz_probe_r6_next() again): the raw battle_unit userdata.
--   Every pass logs GetContextObjectId + GetContextObject for the real type
--   ids on dynamic_stats / unit_information / the first dy_value BEFORE and
--   AFTER the write, plus the value signature and a verdict line. The write
--   itself is logged IMMEDIATELY BEFORE it happens (a fatal candidate names
--   itself). A failed build performs NO write. Any manual arm cancels the
--   auto pass-1 arm (after a crash: relaunch, then zz_probe_r6_next(2) BEFORE
--   opening the panel to skip a fatal candidate).
--
-- ROUND 8 - THE DECISIVE EXPERIMENT (section 13): CAN THE MOD READ A UNIT'S
--   UNIT-CARD STAT NUMBERS FOR A UNIT THE PLAYER HAS NOT SELECTED - with no
--   player hover and no gameplay interruption? Four labelled parts:
--     PART 1 GROUND TRUTH: pin the stat panel; click each unit once; each
--       becomes 'R8 TRUTH <id> <stat>=<value> ...' (the comparison baseline).
--     PART 2 SIMULATED-HOVER LADDER: for every NON-selected card, SimulateMouseOn
--       / SimulateMouseOff at 50 / 150 / 300 / 1500 ms holds, polling the panel
--       every 50 ms for the comparison fields (CcoUnitStat.ComparisonValue /
--       CcoUnitDetails.ComparisonContext / label_compare text) and recording
--       whether they appear and how long they persist - one 'R8 SIMHOVER
--       card=.. hold=..' verdict per pass. The player does NOTHING.
--     PART 3 INVISIBILITY: the layouts' tooltip timings (panel_sticky_tooltips
--       default_appear_val 0.25 s; special_unit_tooltip expand_delay_ms 2500;
--       tooltip_default expand_delay 0.8 s) -> holds under 250 ms are invisible.
--     PART 4 THE FAKE-SELECTION ROUTE: ONE hand-armed select_in_ui pass
--       ('R8 DESELECT-TEST', OFF by default; zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test()).
--   ZERO SetContextObject calls; every SimulateMouseOn is paired with an Off.
--   GATE OBSERVABILITY (this build): about once a second (and on a forced run)
--   ONE cheap line is logged even when the gate is CLOSED, naming the condition
--   that did (or did not) fire and the panel's tab state when no stat rows are
--   seen: 'R8 GATE panel_seen=.. stat_rows=.. stat_names=[..] selected_card=..
--   ladder_state=<idle/armed/running/done> fired=<panel|selection|none>
--   [tab={..}]'. The gate now OPENS on EITHER the stat panel showing rows OR a
--   unit being selected while the cards panel is up.
--   Hooks: zz_probe_r8() (FORCE - runs even when the auto-gate never opened;
--   it logs 'R8 FORCE' + the gate line) / zz_probe_r8_status()
--   (reports the cached gate state) / zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test().

-- WHAT THIS PROBE DOES (per poll, while a capture window is armed)
--   1. Resolve hud_battle and require it to report children; otherwise the poll
--      is skipped SILENTLY and retried next poll - an empty tree is never
--      logged as if it were a result (round-1 lesson).
--   2. Walk the subtree (depth <= MAX_DEPTH, <= MAX_VISITS visits, every engine
--      touch pcall-walled) using the SAME pattern the main mod proved reaches
--      612-632 components of this exact root: ChildCount()/Find(i) descending.
--   3. For every component that HAS TEXT (GetStateText / GetTooltipText) - or
--      whose id names a stat/tooltip - build a signature and log ONE line ONLY
--      when that signature is NEW or CHANGED since the previous poll. Switched
--      to changed-only because a full HUD is 600+ components and a poll every
--      200 ms would otherwise flood the log; unchanged polls write NOTHING.
--   4. Flag any text containing a digit or "Base value" (or "Hold the Line")
--      as ***STAT-LIKE*** - grep the log for exactly that.
--   Round-1 lesson applied: GetProperty is CONFIRMED DEAD (it echoed property
--   names back empty), so it is NOT probed any more.
--
-- ARMING (the mouse is the trigger; no console needed for the normal run)
--   PRIMARY: hover a UNIT CARD. ComponentMouseOn arms a 5 s / 200 ms capture
--   (ComponentMouseOff closes it early). Just hover and read.
--   NO AUTOMATIC WINDOWS (round 7): a capture starts ONLY on a card hover
--   (the mouse is the trigger; the manual hook is the other way in).
--   MANUAL (re-run): zz_probe_ui_arm(seconds) from the Lua console (shift+F3)
--   BEFORE you hover.
--
-- WHERE THIS FILE GOES
--   script/battle/mod/zz_probe_ui_text.lua inside the .pack. The game's mod
--   loader executes every *.lua under /script/battle/mod/ in a battle, so the
--   top-level code below runs at load. It proves it ran by writing its log.
--
-- WHERE THE OUTPUT GOES
--   zz_probe_ui_text_log.txt, in the game's install folder (next to
--   Warhammer3.exe) - a THIRD file, different from the main mod's log and from
--   zz_probe_unit_reads_log.txt, so no two concerns can mix. Every load appends
--   a clearly marked new round header. Grep it for "[zz_probe_ui_text]" and for
--   "***STAT-LIKE***".
--
-- HOW TO DRIVE IT
--   1. Play a battle and just HOVER a unit card for a few seconds. The hover
--      arms the capture and the tooltip's numbers are caught as they appear.
--   2. Read zz_probe_ui_text_log.txt and grep for ***STAT-LIKE***.
--   Manual re-run: zz_probe_ui_arm(60) BEFORE hovering (no auto windows anymore).
--
-- CONSOLE HOOKS (all globals are prefixed zz_probe_ui_ - no clash with the
-- main mod's zz_* or with the other probe's zz_probe_*):
--   zz_probe_ui_arm(seconds)   arm a capture window now (default 60 s) - call
--                              this BEFORE hovering
--   zz_probe_ui()              one immediate walk of the default root
--   zz_probe_ui('hud_battle')  one immediate walk of a named root
--   zz_probe_ui_status()       windows used, polls run, log path
--   zz_probe_ui_help()         these instructions as a string
--   zz_probe_stat_dump()       ROUND 4: rescan + full dump of every stat seed
--                              root (with the unit-details panel PINNED open)
--   zz_probe_stat_dump('id')   ROUND 4: full dump of one named root
--   zz_probe_stat_status()     ROUND 4: dump count, seeds found, log path
--   zz_probe_stat_help()       ROUND 4: the one instruction, as a string
--   ROUND 5 hooks (open AND PIN the unit-details panel first):
--   zz_probe_r5()              queue a full R5 run (all four experiments)
--   zz_probe_r5_context()      R5.1 only (read-only: GetContextObject)
--   zz_probe_r5_setctx()       R5.2 only (SetContextObject candidates)
--   zz_probe_r5_select()       R5.3 only (select_in_ui on a non-selected unit)
--   zz_probe_r5_hover()        R5.4 only (SimulateMouseOn on another card)
--   zz_probe_r5_status()       runs / caps / phase / log path
--   zz_probe_r5_help()         the R5 instructions, as a string
--   ROUND 6 hooks (open AND PIN the unit-details panel first; select one
--   unit; the auto-run does pass 1 only):
--   zz_probe_r6()              arm pass 1 now (cancels the auto pass-1 arm)
--   zz_probe_r6_next()         advance: arm the next pass (1 -> 2 -> 3)
--   zz_probe_r6_next(k)        arm pass k explicitly (skip a fatal candidate)
--   zz_probe_r6_status()       passes / sets / phase / panel-seen
--   ROUND 8 hooks (battle -> pin the panel -> click each unit once):
--   zz_probe_r8()              FORCE the simulated-hover ladder NOW - it runs
--                              even when the auto-gate never opened and logs
--                              'R8 FORCE' + one R8 GATE line (the auto ladder
--                              also starts ~6 s after the last truth click)
--   zz_probe_r8_status()       phase / truth entries / passes / sim on+off /
--                              owed Off / select-test state / cached gate
--                              (panel_seen, stat_rows, selected_card, fired) /
--                              force count / log path
--   zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test()  ARM or DISARM the ONE select_in_ui test
--   zz_probe_r8_help()         the round-8 instructions, as a string
--   zz_probe_r6_help()         the ladder, as a string
--   ROUND 11 hooks (battle -> open AND PIN the unit-info panel -> keep the
--   cards panel up with >=2 units):
--   zz_probe_r11()             start/restart the run (step 0)
--   zz_probe_r11_step()        run EXACTLY ONE step (1-2 are proven safe)
--   zz_probe_r11_auto()        run every step to the cap
--   zz_probe_r11_status()      step / budgets / located / rows / ctx ids
--   zz_probe_r11_help()        the round-11 instructions, as a string
--   ROUND 12 hooks (R12 TOTAL STEPS 6 - you are done after step 6; battle ->
--   open AND PIN the unit-info panel -> keep the cards panel up with >=2 units):
--   zz_probe_r12()             start/restart the run (step 0)
--   zz_probe_r12_step()        run EXACTLY ONE step (SIX total; stop after 6)
--   zz_probe_r12_auto()        run every step to the cap
--   zz_probe_r12_status()      step / budgets / seeds / located / rows / ctx ids
--   zz_probe_r12_help()        the round-12 instructions, as a string
--   ROUND 13 hooks (R13 TOTAL STEPS 7 - you are done after step 7; battle ->
--   open AND PIN the unit-info panel -> keep the cards panel up with >=2 units):
--   zz_probe_r13()             start/restart the run (step 0)
--   zz_probe_r13_step()        run EXACTLY ONE step (SEVEN total; stop after 7)
--   zz_probe_r13_auto()        run every step to the cap
--   zz_probe_r13_status()      step / budgets / roots / hits / located / rows / ctx ids
--   zz_probe_r13_help()        the round-13 instructions, as a string
--
-- REMOVAL: delete this one file and rebuild. Nothing else refers to it.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


-- ============================================================================
-- 1. THE PROBE'S OWN LOG (a third file - never the main mod's, never the other
--    probe's) - written append-only, flushed after every line
-- ============================================================================

local PROBE_TAG = "[zz_probe_ui_text] "
local LOG_FILE  = "zz_probe_ui_text_log.txt"
local POLL_NAME = "zz_probe_ui_text_poll"

local POLL_MS        = 200     -- poll cadence inside a capture window (the main
                               -- mod's own HUD walk runs 600+ components fast
                               -- with no reported lag, so 5 Hz is tolerated)
local MOUSE_SECONDS  = 5       -- a mouse-armed capture lasts this long
-- ROUND 7: the automatic safety windows are GONE. A capture starts ONLY on
-- a hover (ComponentMouseOn on a card) or the manual console hook; no timed
-- window ever arms by itself.
local MAX_MOUSE_CAPTURES = 60  -- HARD CAP on mouse-armed captures (log bound)
local MOUSE_OFF_GRACE_TICKS = 2  -- a MouseOff closes a mouse window after this
                                 -- many ticks, so the tooltip's first poll lands
local UNIT_ID_REFRESH_TICKS = 25 -- re-read the local unit ids at most every 5 s
local PANEL_SWEEP_TICKS = 25     -- outside a window, keep card reporters fresh

local MAX_DEPTH  = 9           -- subtree depth cap
local MAX_VISITS = 1500        -- component visit cap per poll (bounds the work)

-- Round 1 proved that four of the five hard-coded root names do NOT exist in
-- the battle context (unit_information, tooltip_ai_stats_modifier,
-- tooltip_ai_stats, tooltip_unit_health, tooltip_entity_info were all absent);
-- only hud_battle was found, and the main mod's walk of that SAME root reaches
-- 612-632 components. So the continuous capture walks hud_battle; the alternate
-- finders are still tried for a caller-supplied name in the one-shot hook.
local DEFAULT_ROOT = "hud_battle"

-- The cards panel (the main mod's own names) - its reporter makes a hover
-- ANYWHERE over the cards fire a ComponentMouseOn, which is the net for a card
-- whose own id we could not classify.
local CARD_PANELS = { "card_panel_docker", "cards_panel" }

-- Component ids whose own name says "this is a tooltip / a stat" are treated as
-- interesting even when their text reads empty, because they are the likely
-- home of the rendered numbers. Cheap: no engine call, id only.
local NAME_HINTS = { "tooltip", "stat", "unit_card", "card" }

local log_handle = nil
local file_logging_off = false

local function write_to_file(line)
	if file_logging_off then return end
	if log_handle == nil then
		local ok, handle = pcall(io.open, LOG_FILE, "a")
		if not ok or handle == nil then
			file_logging_off = true
			return
		end
		log_handle = handle
		pcall(function()
			log_handle:write("\n======== zz_probe_ui_text session "
				.. "(round 13: all-roots descent + CcoUnitStat prefix hunt | rounds 12-3 below) ========\n")
			log_handle:flush()
		end)
	end
	pcall(function()
		log_handle:write(line .. "\n")
		log_handle:flush()
	end)
end

local function log(message)
	local line = PROBE_TAG .. tostring(message)
	write_to_file(line)
	if ModLog ~= nil then pcall(ModLog, line) end
	pcall(out, line)
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 2. SMALL SAFE HELPERS (every engine touch is pcall'd; no string.find/match is
--    ever run on an engine value - the round-1 crash hunt proved the engine can
--    die inside a find on a dressed string, so the contains/digit tests here are
--    plain string.sub / string.byte scans on a fresh tostring copy)
-- ============================================================================

local lua_type = type

local function safe_text(v)
	if v == nil then return nil end
	-- Copy first: the engine can dress a value as a string (round-1 lesson),
	-- so string ops must never touch the raw value. `v .. ""` forces a fresh
	-- plain copy and the pcall contains a hostile concat; tostring is the
	-- fallback for a value that refuses concat but has a tostring.
	local ok, s = pcall(function() return v .. "" end)
	if ok and s ~= nil then return s end
	local ok2, s2 = pcall(tostring, v)
	if ok2 and s2 ~= nil then return s2 end
	return nil
end

-- Turn a read's (raw, ok) pair into a log-safe text value. A raising read and a
-- value with no tostring become explicit sentinels, never nil-as-silence.
local function text_of(raw, ok)
	if not ok then return "<ERR>" end
	if raw == nil then return nil end
	local s = safe_text(raw)
	if s ~= nil then return s end
	return "<opaque>"
end

-- Quoted, truncated string for the log (safe against a hostile tostring).
local function q(v)
	if v == nil then return "nil" end
	local s = safe_text(v)
	if s == nil then return "<unreadable>" end
	if #s > 90 then s = string.sub(s, 1, 90) .. "..." end
	return "\"" .. s .. "\""
end

local function truncate(s, n)
	local str = safe_text(s)
	if str == nil then return "<unreadable>" end
	if #str > n then return string.sub(str, 1, n) .. "..." end
	return str
end

-- A substring test with NO string.find (see the section note above).
local function contains_str(haystack, needle)
	local h = tostring(haystack or "")
	local n = tostring(needle or "")
	local hlen = string.len(h)
	local nlen = string.len(n)
	if nlen == 0 or nlen > hlen then return false end
	for i = 1, hlen - nlen + 1 do
		if string.sub(h, i, i + nlen - 1) == n then return true end
	end
	return false
end

local function has_digit(s)
	local h = tostring(s or "")
	local hlen = string.len(h)
	for i = 1, hlen do
		local c = string.byte(h, i)
		if c ~= nil and c >= 48 and c <= 57 then return true end
	end
	return false
end

-- Read one engine value under pcall -> value, okflag.
local function read1(fn)
	local ok, v = pcall(fn)
	if not ok then return nil, false end
	return v, true
end

-- Read a two-return engine value under pcall -> a, b, okflag (Position()).
local function read2(fn)
	local ok, a, b = pcall(fn)
	if not ok then return nil, nil, false end
	return a, b, true
end

-- Read one boolean-ish engine value under pcall -> text, okflag.
local function readb(fn)
	local ok, v = pcall(fn)
	if not ok then return "ERR", false end
	if v == nil then return "nil", true end
	return tostring(v), true
end

-- A string is "stat-like" if it contains a digit or the words the tooltip
-- shows. Returns the matched reason, or nil.
local function stat_like(s)
	if s == nil then return nil end
	local str = safe_text(s)
	if str == nil or str == "" then return nil end
	local low = string.lower(str)
	if contains_str(low, "base value") then return "contains 'Base value'" end
	if contains_str(low, "hold the line") then return "contains 'Hold the Line'" end
	if has_digit(str) then return "contains a digit" end
	return nil
end

-- A component id "names a tooltip/stat" -> flagged so it is findable by grep.
local function name_hint(id)
	if id == nil then return nil end
	local str = safe_text(id)
	if str == nil then return nil end
	local low = string.lower(str)
	for i = 1, #NAME_HINTS do
		if contains_str(low, NAME_HINTS[i]) then return NAME_HINTS[i] end
	end
	return nil
end

local function has_text(v)
	return v ~= nil and v ~= ""
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 3. UI ACCESS (root lookup + Find/FindByScriptTag/SequentialFind)
-- ============================================================================

local function get_ui_root()
	local ok, r = pcall(function() return core:get_ui_root() end)
	if ok then return r end
	return nil
end

local function wrap(raw)
	-- R11 FIX: a boolean is NOT a component. The engine's name-lookup helper
	-- returns FALSE on a miss and UIComponent(false) hard-crashes the engine.
	if raw == nil or raw == false then return nil end
	local ok_w, wrapped = pcall(UIComponent, raw)
	if ok_w and wrapped ~= nil then return wrapped end
	return raw
end

-- root:Find(name,false) -> the engine's own recursive search by id, exactly as
-- the main mod does it.
local function find_by_name(name)
	local root = get_ui_root()
	if root == nil then return nil end
	local ok, raw = pcall(function() return root:Find(name, false) end)
	if not ok or raw == nil then return nil end
	return wrap(raw)
end

local function find_by_script_tag(tag)
	local root = get_ui_root()
	if root == nil then return nil end
	local ok, raw = pcall(function() return root:FindByScriptTag(tag) end)
	if not ok or raw == nil then return nil end
	return wrap(raw)
end

local function sequential_find(a, b)
	local root = get_ui_root()
	if root == nil then return nil end
	local ok, raw = pcall(function() return root:SequentialFind(a, b) end)
	if not ok or raw == nil then return nil end
	return wrap(raw)
end

-- Resolve a caller-supplied root name; records which finder answered.
local function resolve_root(name)
	local c = find_by_name(name)
	if c ~= nil then return c, "Find" end
	local t = find_by_script_tag(name)
	if t ~= nil then return t, "FindByScriptTag" end
	local s = sequential_find(name)
	if s ~= nil then return s, "SequentialFind" end
	return nil, nil
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 4. THE CHANGE TRACKER + CAPTURE STATE
--    prev[path_key] = { sig, stext, tip } - the last-seen signature of every
--    component that carried text. path_key is a positional key (root + child
--    indices), which stays stable even when Id() answers a function or raises
--    (round-1 lesson: Id() on a real component can be a function or fail).
-- ============================================================================

local prev = {}
local tick_count = 0               -- polls since load (the probe's own clock)
local window_active = false        -- true while a capture window is running
local window_index = 0             -- how many windows have ever been armed
local window_ends_tick = 0         -- tick at which the active window ends
local window_why = nil             -- "mouse" / "manual" (round 7: no auto windows)
local window_hover_id = nil        -- the hovered component id (mouse windows)
local window_hover_reason = nil    -- why it was taken for a card
local window_arm_addr = nil        -- the event's component address (mouse windows)
local window_header_pending = false -- the window header has not been written yet
local manual_arm_seconds = nil     -- set by zz_probe_ui_arm, consumed by the tick
local polls_in_window = 0          -- polls that actually walked in this window
local lines_in_window = 0          -- log lines this window produced
local walk_visits = 0              -- visits in the current walk
local cap_spoken = false           -- the visit cap has spoken this window

local mouse_captures_started = 0   -- mouse-armed captures armed
local mouse_cap_spoken = false     -- the mouse-capture cap has spoken
local manual_windows_started = 0   -- manual (console) windows armed

local mouse_arm_pending = false    -- a hover landed on a card (set by listener)
local mouse_arm_id = nil           -- the hovered component id
local mouse_arm_reason = nil       -- the card test that matched
local mouse_arm_addr = nil         -- the event's component address
local mouse_off_tick = nil         -- tick a matching MouseOff arrived (close)

local SEP = "\30"                  -- record separator inside a signature

local function sig_of(state, st, tip)
	return tostring(state) .. SEP .. tostring(st) .. SEP .. tostring(tip)
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 5. ONE COMPONENT (every read pcall'd; logs ONLY when NEW or CHANGED)
--    The id is read by the walk (section 6) and passed in, so a component's
--    Id() is touched exactly once per visit.
-- ============================================================================

local function log_component(uic, depth, path_key, id_text)
	local state_raw, state_ok = read1(function() return uic:CurrentState() end)
	local st_raw, st_ok = read1(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
	local tip_raw, tip_ok = read1(function() return uic:GetTooltipText() end)
	local vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end)
	local vfr = readb(function() return uic:VisibleFromRoot() end)
	local px, py = read2(function() return uic:Position() end)

	local id = id_text
	local state = text_of(state_raw, state_ok)
	local st = text_of(st_raw, st_ok)
	local tip = text_of(tip_raw, tip_ok)

	local hint = name_hint(id)
	-- A component matters only if it carries text or its name says stat/tooltip.
	if not (has_text(st) or has_text(tip) or hint ~= nil) then
		return false
	end

	local sig = sig_of(state, st, tip)
	local entry = prev[path_key]

	if entry ~= nil and entry.sig == sig then
		return false                     -- unchanged: write nothing at all
	end

	local is_new = (entry == nil)
	local flags = ""
	if hint ~= nil then flags = flags .. "  <<NAME~" .. hint .. ">>" end
	local sl_st = stat_like(st)
	local sl_tip = stat_like(tip)
	if sl_st ~= nil then flags = flags .. "  ***STAT-LIKE stext (" .. sl_st .. ")***" end
	if sl_tip ~= nil then flags = flags .. "  ***STAT-LIKE tip (" .. sl_tip .. ")***" end

	local old_part = ""
	if not is_new then
		old_part = "  (was stext=" .. q(entry.stext) .. " tip=" .. q(entry.tip) .. ")"
	end

	local line = (is_new and "NEW  " or "CHG  ")
		.. "id=" .. q(id)
		.. " state=" .. q(state)
		.. " stext=" .. q(st)
		.. " tip=" .. q(tip)
		.. " vis=" .. tostring(vis) .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr)
		.. " pos=(" .. tostring(safe_text(px)) .. "," .. tostring(safe_text(py)) .. ")"
		.. flags .. old_part

	log(line)
	lines_in_window = lines_in_window + 1

	prev[path_key] = { sig = sig, stext = st, tip = tip }
	return true
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 5b. THE CARD TEST + THE REPORTER SUBSCRIPTION (the mouse trigger's front end)
--     The engine only fires ComponentMouseOn/Off for a component that has called
--     AddScriptEventReporter() (README round 24 / the API doc / the main mod's
--     own log). So a card-like component must be subscribed before its hover can
--     be heard. This is a SUBSCRIPTION, not a UI-state write - no SetText /
--     SetState / SetProperty / Layout / CreateComponent / Destroy is ever called.
-- ============================================================================

local unit_id_set = {}             -- local unit unique_ui_id (as text) -> true
local unit_id_set_at = -100000     -- tick of the last unit-id refresh

local reporter_addrs = {}          -- Address() text -> true: already subscribed
local reporter_calls = 0           -- subscriptions that succeeded (diagnostic)
local reporter_armed_ids = {}      -- id text -> true: card-like ids subscribed

-- Read the local player's units and remember their ui ids. Called at most once
-- every UNIT_ID_REFRESH_TICKS (section 6 gates it), so the walk does not hammer
-- the engine.
local function refresh_unit_ids()
	unit_id_set = {}
	local ok = pcall(function()
		local sunits = bm:get_scriptunits_for_local_players_army()
		if sunits == nil then return end
		local total = sunits:count()
		if lua_type(total) ~= "number" then return end
		for i = 1, total do
			local su = sunits:item(i)
			local u = su and su.unit
			if u ~= nil then
				local ok_id, uid = pcall(function() return u:unique_ui_id() end)
				if ok_id and uid ~= nil then
					local t = safe_text(uid)
					if t ~= nil then unit_id_set[t] = true end
				end
			end
		end
	end)
	unit_id_set_at = tick_count
	-- `ok` is deliberately unused: a failed read leaves an EMPTY set, and an
	-- empty set simply means no id matched this pass.
	return ok
end

local function ensure_unit_ids()
	if (tick_count - unit_id_set_at) >= UNIT_ID_REFRESH_TICKS then
		pcall(refresh_unit_ids)
	end
end

-- The arming rule (the task's own words): the component's id equals a local
-- unit's unique_ui_id as text, OR its id/name contains 'card' / the unit's id.
-- Returns a short reason, or nil.
local function card_like_reason(id_text)
	if id_text == nil or id_text == "" then return nil end
	local low = string.lower(id_text)
	if contains_str(low, "card") then return "id names a card" end
	ensure_unit_ids()
	if unit_id_set[id_text] then return "id is a local unit's ui id" end
	for uid in pairs(unit_id_set) do
		if contains_str(id_text, uid) then
			return "id carries a local unit's ui id (" .. tostring(uid) .. ")"
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- Subscribe a component (once, keyed by its Address() when readable). A
-- subscription that fails is simply retried on the next walk.
local function arm_reporter_on(uic, label)
	local ok_a, addr = pcall(function() return uic:Address() end)
	local key = nil
	if ok_a and addr ~= nil then key = safe_text(addr) end
	if key == nil then key = "id:" .. tostring(label) end
	if reporter_addrs[key] then return end
	reporter_addrs[key] = true
	local ok = pcall(function() uic:AddScriptEventReporter() end)
	if ok then
		reporter_calls = reporter_calls + 1
		if label ~= nil then reporter_armed_ids[tostring(label)] = true end
	end
end

-- The light sweep that keeps card reporters fresh OUTSIDE a window: subscribe
-- the cards panel itself, so a hover anywhere over the cards is heard even if
-- no individual card id could be classified.
local function arm_panel_reporters()
	for i = 1, #CARD_PANELS do
		local p = find_by_name(CARD_PANELS[i])
		if p ~= nil then
			pcall(arm_reporter_on, p, CARD_PANELS[i])
		end
	end
end

-- Is this mouse event about a unit card? The id carries the arming rule; the
-- address is the fallback for a card/panel whose id could not be classified.
local function mouse_event_is_card(id_text, addr_text)
	local reason = card_like_reason(id_text)
	if reason ~= nil then return reason end
	if addr_text ~= nil and reporter_addrs[addr_text] then
		return "event address is a known card/panel reporter"
	end
	return nil
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 6. THE WALK (recursive; depth-capped, visit-capped, every touch pcall-walled -
--    the main mod's proven ChildCount()/Find(i) descent). It also subscribes the
--    reporter on any card-like component it meets, which is what makes the
--    hover audible.
-- ============================================================================

local function capture_component(uic, depth, path_key)
	if uic == nil then return end
	if walk_visits >= MAX_VISITS then
		if not cap_spoken then
			cap_spoken = true
			log("VISIT CAP reached (" .. tostring(MAX_VISITS) .. " components) - subtree truncated here")
			lines_in_window = lines_in_window + 1
		end
		return
	end
	walk_visits = walk_visits + 1

	-- The component's id, read ONCE and shared by the logger and the card test.
	local id_raw, id_ok = read1(function() return uic:Id() end)
	local id_text = text_of(id_raw, id_ok)

	-- The component's whole read set, in its own pcall wall: a hostile component
	-- cannot abort the walk.
	local ok_one = pcall(log_component, uic, depth, path_key, id_text)
	if not ok_one then
		-- swallowed on purpose; the walk must survive it
	end

	-- Subscribe the reporter on a card-like component (section 5b), so its hover
	-- can be heard. pcall'd: a hostile component must not stop the walk.
	if id_text ~= nil and id_text ~= "" then
		if card_like_reason(id_text) ~= nil then
			pcall(arm_reporter_on, uic, id_text)
		end
	end

	if depth >= MAX_DEPTH then return end

	local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
	if lua_type(n) == "number" and n > 0 then
		for i = 0, n - 1 do
			local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
			if ok_c and child ~= nil then
				-- each recursion is pcall'd too, so one bad child cannot stop
				-- its siblings
				pcall(capture_component, wrap(child), depth + 1, path_key .. "/" .. i)
			end
		end
	end
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 7. ONE POLL / ONE-SHOT (requires children; never logs an empty tree)
-- ============================================================================

local function capture_poll(root_label, root)
	if root == nil then return false end

	local n = read1(function() return root:ChildCount() end)
	if lua_type(n) ~= "number" or n <= 0 then
		return false        -- HUD not populated yet: silent retry next poll
	end

	if window_header_pending then
		window_header_pending = false
		lines_in_window = lines_in_window + 1
		local hover_part = ""
		if window_hover_id ~= nil then
			hover_part = " hover=" .. q(window_hover_id)
				.. " (" .. tostring(window_hover_reason or "?") .. ")"
		end
		log("===== CAPTURE WINDOW " .. tostring(window_index) .. " (" .. tostring(window_why) .. ")"
			.. " t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. hover_part
			.. " root='" .. tostring(root_label) .. "' children=" .. tostring(n) .. " =====")
	end

	walk_visits = 0
	capture_component(root, 0, root_label)
	return true
end

local function one_shot(root_name)
	local name = (root_name ~= nil and root_name ~= "") and tostring(root_name) or DEFAULT_ROOT
	local root, how = resolve_root(name)
	if root == nil then
		log("one-shot: root '" .. name .. "' NOT FOUND by Find / FindByScriptTag / SequentialFind")
		return false
	end
	local n = read1(function() return root:ChildCount() end)
	if lua_type(n) ~= "number" or n <= 0 then
		log("one-shot: root '" .. name .. "' has no children yet - nothing walked"
			.. " (no empty pass logged, by design)")
		return false
	end
	log("===== ONE-SHOT WALK root='" .. name .. "' (" .. tostring(how) .. ") t="
		.. tostring(tick_count) .. " children=" .. tostring(n) .. " =====")
	walk_visits = 0
	capture_component(root, 0, name)
	return true
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 7b. ROUND-4 TARGETED STAT DUMP (the unit-stat subtree, walked FULLY, with NO
--     change-filtering) - the answer to round 3's finding that the stat
--     components are reachable and NAMED but their own text reads empty.
--
--     Round 3 reached CcoUnitStat5755085424 (melee attack), ...4448 (melee
--     defence), ...1344 (weapon damage), ...4112 (armour), ...5328 (leadership),
--     ...4128 (charge bonus) and read each one's OWN description as
--     GetTooltipText - but EVERY CcoUnitStat* returned stext="" (empty), so the
--     NUMBER is rendered somewhere round 4 has not read yet: a child text
--     component, a state of a child, a number-sprite image path, or a property.
--     This section walks the whole stat subtree and logs EVERY component with its
--     id / state / GetStateText / GetTooltipText / Visible / VisibleFromRoot /
--     Position / Bounds / GetImagePath, so the row structure beneath a stat is
--     visible in the log and the number's home can be located by reading it.
--
--     TRIGGERS
--       (a) AUTOMATIC: a light watch walk (every STAT_WATCH_EVERY polls) finds
--           every stat-named component under hud_battle and reads its
--           Visible/VisibleFromRoot. When the SET of visible stat ids changes
--           AND is non-empty - i.e. the unit-details panel was opened, or a
--           different stat became visible - ONE full dump runs. A later change
--           of the set re-dumps. The panel can be PINNED, so the watch keeps
--           working with the mouse parked off the game.
--       (b) MANUAL: zz_probe_stat_dump() (rescan + dump every seed) or
--           zz_probe_stat_dump('root id') (dump one named root), from the Lua
--           console (shift+F3) with the panel pinned open.
--
--     CAPS (round 7 slim): depth <= 12, <= 200 visits TOTAL per dump (ONE
--     shared budget across seeds), STAT_DUMP_MAX (40) dumps per session,
--     STAT_SEED_MAX (12) seed roots. Only components WITH TEXT or inside the
--     stat structure are logged.
--     Every read is pcall-walled. NO setter is ever called (the only engine
--     WRITE anywhere in this file is the reporter SUBSCRIPTION).
-- ============================================================================

-- ROUND 7 SLIM (the 6 s stall fix): the targeted dump is capped at depth 12
-- and 200 visits TOTAL per dump (shared across every seed root), and the
-- watch walk at 250 visits - the round-4 values (20 / 3000 / 2000 x one ref
-- per seed) walked the whole subtree repeatedly.
local STAT_MAX_DEPTH    = 12      -- round-7 slim (was 20)
local STAT_MAX_VISITS   = 200     -- round-7 slim: TOTAL per dump (was 3000 per seed)
local STAT_WATCH_VISITS = 250     -- round-7 slim (was 2000)
local STAT_WATCH_EVERY  = 3       -- watch cadence: every 3rd poll (~600 ms)
local STAT_DUMP_MAX     = 40      -- HARD CAP on full stat dumps (log bound)
local STAT_SEED_MAX     = 12      -- round-7 slim (was 60)
local STAT_CARD_MAX     = 2       -- round-7 slim (was 4)

-- Seed id tests (the task's own list). The CcoUnitStat* test is a
-- case-insensitive PREFIX (the engine appends a numeric instance suffix); the
-- rest are substrings.
local STAT_SEED_PREFIX = "ccounitstat"
local STAT_SEED_HINTS  = { "dynamic_stats", "template_stat",
                           "health_and_stats_parent", "row_header_stats",
                           "stats_toggle" }

local stat_dump_count      = 0
local stat_dump_cap_spoken = false
local stat_visible_sig     = nil    -- last visible-stat-id signature (nil=never)
local stat_scan_seeds      = {}     -- seed components the last watch found
local stat_scan_cards      = {}     -- fallback card roots the last watch found

-- Does this component id name a stat subtree root? -> short reason, or nil.
local function stat_root_reason(id_text)
	if id_text == nil or id_text == "" then return nil end
	local low = string.lower(id_text)
	if string.sub(low, 1, #STAT_SEED_PREFIX) == STAT_SEED_PREFIX then
		return "id starts with CcoUnitStat"
	end
	for i = 1, #STAT_SEED_HINTS do
		if contains_str(low, STAT_SEED_HINTS[i]) then
			return "id names " .. STAT_SEED_HINTS[i]
		end
	end
	return nil
end

-- One component of a FULL stat dump: EVERY field, NO change-filtering, EVERY
-- component logged. Recurses to STAT_MAX_DEPTH; visit_ref bounds the work.
local function stat_dump_visit(uic, depth, path, visit_ref)
	if uic == nil then return end
	if visit_ref[1] >= STAT_MAX_VISITS then
		if not visit_ref.spoken then
			visit_ref.spoken = true
			log("STAT DUMP visit budget reached (" .. tostring(STAT_MAX_VISITS)
				.. " components total) - subtree truncated here")
		end
		return
	end
	visit_ref[1] = visit_ref[1] + 1

	-- ROUND 7: a SMALL read set (the bounds/images/state-name probes of round 4
	-- are gone) and a filter: only components WITH TEXT (stext/tip) or inside
	-- the stat structure (CcoUnitStat* / dynamic_stats / template_stat /
	-- dy_value / stat_name) produce a line. The point is the stat_name ->
	-- dy_value pairing, which the text test catches.
	local id_raw, id_ok = read1(function() return uic:Id() end)
	local id      = text_of(id_raw, id_ok)
	local st_raw, st_ok     = read1(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
	local tip_raw, tip_ok   = read1(function() return uic:GetTooltipText() end)
	local st  = text_of(st_raw, st_ok)
	local tip = text_of(tip_raw, tip_ok)

	local id_low = ""
	if id ~= nil and id ~= "" then id_low = string.lower(id) end
	local in_stat_structure = (id_low ~= "" and (stat_root_reason(id) ~= nil
		or contains_str(id_low, "dy_value") or contains_str(id_low, "stat_name")))
	local interesting = in_stat_structure or has_text(st) or has_text(tip)

	if interesting then
		local state_raw, state_ok = read1(function() return uic:CurrentState() end)
		local state = text_of(state_raw, state_ok)
		local vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end)
		local vfr = readb(function() return uic:VisibleFromRoot() end)
		local px, py = read2(function() return uic:Position() end)
		local why = {}
		if has_digit(state) then why[#why + 1] = "digit in state" end
		if has_digit(st)    then why[#why + 1] = "digit in stext" end
		if has_digit(tip)   then why[#why + 1] = "digit in tip" end
		local sl_st  = stat_like(st)
		local sl_tip = stat_like(tip)
		if sl_st ~= nil then why[#why + 1] = "stext:" .. sl_st end
		if sl_tip ~= nil then why[#why + 1] = "tip:" .. sl_tip end
		local flags = ""
		if #why > 0 then flags = "  ***STAT-LIKE (" .. table.concat(why, ", ") .. ")***" end

		log(string.rep("  ", depth) .. "[" .. tostring(depth) .. "] "
			.. "id=" .. q(id)
			.. " state=" .. q(state)
			.. " stext=" .. q(st)
			.. " tip=" .. q(tip)
			.. " vis=" .. tostring(vis) .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr)
			.. " pos=(" .. tostring(safe_text(px)) .. "," .. tostring(safe_text(py)) .. ")"
			.. flags)
	end

	if depth >= STAT_MAX_DEPTH then return end
	local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
	if lua_type(n) == "number" and n > 0 then
		for ci = 0, n - 1 do
			if visit_ref[1] >= STAT_MAX_VISITS then
				if not visit_ref.spoken then
					visit_ref.spoken = true
					log("STAT DUMP visit budget reached (" .. tostring(STAT_MAX_VISITS)
						.. " components total) - subtree truncated here")
				end
				return
			end
			local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(ci) end)
			if ok_c and child ~= nil then
				pcall(stat_dump_visit, wrap(child), depth + 1, path .. "/" .. ci, visit_ref)
			end
		end
	end
end

-- Run one full dump over the given seed roots + fallback card roots.
local function stat_do_dump(trigger, seeds, cards)
	if stat_dump_count >= STAT_DUMP_MAX then
		if not stat_dump_cap_spoken then
			stat_dump_cap_spoken = true
			log("STAT DUMP cap reached (" .. tostring(STAT_DUMP_MAX)
				.. ") - no more dumps; manual: zz_probe_stat_dump()")
		end
		return
	end
	stat_dump_count = stat_dump_count + 1
	local nseeds = seeds and #seeds or 0
	local ncards = cards and #cards or 0
	log("")
	log("===== STAT DUMP #" .. tostring(stat_dump_count) .. " (trigger: "
		.. tostring(trigger) .. ") stat roots=" .. tostring(nseeds)
		.. " fallback card roots=" .. tostring(ncards)
		.. " t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. " =====")
	log("seed roots tried: id starts with CcoUnitStat | id names dynamic_stats /"
		.. " template_stat / health_and_stats_parent / row_header_stats / stats_toggle")
	if nseeds == 0 and ncards == 0 then
		log("STAT DUMP: no stat/card root found under hud_battle - nothing to dump"
			.. " (pin the unit-details panel open and retry zz_probe_stat_dump())")
		return
	end
	-- ROUND 7: ONE shared visit budget for the WHOLE dump (the old shape made
	-- a fresh ref per seed, so every seed could walk STAT_MAX_VISITS again).
	local ref = { [1] = 0 }
	local i = 0
	while i < nseeds and i < STAT_SEED_MAX do
		i = i + 1
		local seed = seeds[i]
		log("--- stat root " .. tostring(i) .. "/" .. tostring(nseeds)
			.. " (" .. tostring(seed.reason or "?") .. ") id=" .. q(seed.id) .. " ---")
		pcall(stat_dump_visit, seed.uic, 0, seed.id or ("seed" .. i), ref)
		log("--- stat root " .. tostring(i) .. " done: budget used "
			.. tostring(ref[1]) .. "/" .. tostring(STAT_MAX_VISITS) .. " ---")
	end
	i = 0
	while i < ncards and i < STAT_CARD_MAX do
		i = i + 1
		local cr = cards[i]
		log("--- fallback card root " .. tostring(i) .. "/" .. tostring(ncards)
			.. " id=" .. q(cr.id) .. " ---")
		pcall(stat_dump_visit, cr.uic, 0, cr.id or ("card" .. i), ref)
		log("--- fallback card root " .. tostring(i) .. " done: budget used "
			.. tostring(ref[1]) .. "/" .. tostring(STAT_MAX_VISITS) .. " ---")
	end
end

-- The light watch: walk hud_battle (bounded), collect stat-named seeds, their
-- visibility, and card-like fallback roots. Returns the visible-stat-id
-- signature (possibly ""), or nil when there is nothing to scan.
local function stat_watch_scan()
	local hud = find_by_name(DEFAULT_ROOT)
	if hud == nil then return nil end
	local hn = read1(function() return hud:ChildCount() end)
	if lua_type(hn) ~= "number" or hn <= 0 then return nil end

	local seeds = {}
	local cards = {}
	local visible = {}
	local visits = { [1] = 0 }

	local function visit(uic, depth)
		if uic == nil or visits[1] >= STAT_WATCH_VISITS then return end
		visits[1] = visits[1] + 1
		local id_raw, id_ok = read1(function() return uic:Id() end)
		local id = text_of(id_raw, id_ok)
		if id ~= nil and id ~= "" then
			local reason = stat_root_reason(id)
			if reason ~= nil then
				if #seeds < STAT_SEED_MAX then
					seeds[#seeds + 1] = { uic = uic, id = id, reason = reason }
				end
				local vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end)
				local vfr = readb(function() return uic:VisibleFromRoot() end)
				if vis == "true" or vfr == "true" then visible[id] = true end
			elseif card_like_reason(id) ~= nil and #cards < STAT_CARD_MAX then
				cards[#cards + 1] = { uic = uic, id = id }
			end
		end
		if depth >= STAT_MAX_DEPTH then return end
		local cn = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
		if lua_type(cn) == "number" and cn > 0 then
			for i = 0, cn - 1 do
				if visits[1] >= STAT_WATCH_VISITS then return end
				local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
				if ok_c and child ~= nil then
					pcall(visit, wrap(child), depth + 1)
				end
			end
		end
	end

	pcall(visit, hud, 0)
	stat_scan_seeds = seeds
	stat_scan_cards = cards
	local keys = {}
	for k in pairs(visible) do keys[#keys + 1] = k end
	table.sort(keys)
	return table.concat(keys, ",")
end

-- Find a component by its id anywhere under hud_battle (the fallback for a
-- dynamic CcoUnitStat* id that root:Find may not resolve). Bounded.
local function find_by_id_under_hud(want)
	if want == nil or want == "" then return nil, nil end
	local hud = find_by_name(DEFAULT_ROOT)
	if hud == nil then return nil, nil end
	local found = nil
	local visits = { [1] = 0 }
	local function visit(uic, depth)
		if uic == nil or found ~= nil or visits[1] >= STAT_WATCH_VISITS then return end
		visits[1] = visits[1] + 1
		local id_raw, id_ok = read1(function() return uic:Id() end)
		local id = text_of(id_raw, id_ok)
		if id == want then found = uic; return end
		if depth >= STAT_MAX_DEPTH then return end
		local cn = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
		if lua_type(cn) == "number" and cn > 0 then
			for i = 0, cn - 1 do
				if found ~= nil or visits[1] >= STAT_WATCH_VISITS then return end
				local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
				if ok_c and child ~= nil then
					pcall(visit, wrap(child), depth + 1)
				end
			end
		end
	end
	pcall(visit, hud, 0)
	if found ~= nil then return found, "hud id-search" end
	return nil, nil
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 10. ROUND 5 - THE CROSS-UNIT EXPERIMENT (can the stat panel show ANOTHER
--     unit's stats? See the ROUND 5 header block at the top of the file.)
--
--     Four labelled tests, R5.1 .. R5.4. EVERY test runs ONLY while the stat
--     panel is visible; every stage re-checks the panel and aborts BEFORE any
--     write if it is not there; every engine touch is pcall'd; every write is
--     logged IMMEDIATELY BEFORE it happens (a crash names its last write).
--     Caps are hard and per battle; the automatic run queues once when the
--     panel first shows up (dynamic_stats in the visible-stat signature).
-- ============================================================================

-- ROUND 7 - THE ZERO-WRITE HELPER. Every former write site in this file
-- (R5.2 set + restore, R5.3 select_in_ui, R5.4 SimulateMouseOn/Off, R6's one
-- write) calls THIS instead. It logs what would have been written and returns
-- the same (ok, err) shape the old call returned - with ok = false. No setter
-- is ever invoked: this build performs ZERO UI writes.
local function r7_skip_write(what)
	log("R7-SKIP: " .. tostring(what) .. " - writes are deprecated (round 7 zero-write build)")
	return false, "R7-SKIP: writes deprecated (round 7 zero-write build)"
end

local R5 = {
	max_depth = 12,        -- the panel scan's own walk caps
	max_visits = 800,
	settle = 15,           -- ticks (~3 s): the stat list refreshes up to every
	                       -- 2000 ms (the layout's update_constant), so every
	                       -- write waits this long before its re-read
	max_runs = 8,          -- HARD CAP: runs per battle (automatic + manual)
	max_sets = 20,         -- HARD CAP: SetContextObject calls (incl. the restore)
	max_selects = 6,       -- HARD CAP: select_in_ui calls
	max_sims = 6,          -- HARD CAP: SimulateMouseOn calls (MouseOff paired)
	max_cards = 40,        -- HARD CAP: cards read per pass
	max_units = 40,        -- HARD CAP: local units read per pass
	max_rows = 60,         -- HARD CAP: stat rows in a value signature
	auto_attempts = 3,     -- HARD CAP: automatic-run attempts
	ctx_types = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoUnitStat" },
}

local r5 = {
	active = false, phase = "idle", next_at = 0,
	runs = 0, sets = 0, selects = 0, sims = 0,
	auto_done = false, auto_attempts = 0,
	origin = nil, mode = "full", run_no = 0,
	panel = nil,
	baseline = nil, cur_sig = nil,
	orig_cco = nil,
	cand_i = 0, candidates = nil, cur_cand_name = nil,
	sel_unit = nil, sel_before = nil,
	sim_card = nil,
	sig_now = nil,
}

-- ROUND 6: THE R5 AUTO LADDER IS DISARMED. Round 5 proved that a candidate
-- can kill the probe's callbacks (set #1/8 was rejected, then silence).
-- Round 6's own one-write-per-pass ladder is the ONLY automatic experiment
-- now; the manual R5 hooks below remain for reference, but they are NOT
-- part of round 6.
r5.auto_done = true

-- The global cco() constructor (vanilla battle script: lib_bsu.lua's ping icon
-- does uic:SetContextObject(cco("CcoBattleUnit", unit:unique_ui_id()))).
-- Captured once; if the runtime has no cco() the cco candidates are skipped.
local r5_cco = nil
pcall(function() r5_cco = cco end)

local function r5_out(msg)
	log("R5 " .. tostring(msg))
end

-- Read a text value through r5_read_text (raising -> "<ERR>", nil -> nil).
local function r5_read_text(fn)
	local ok, v = pcall(fn)
	if not ok then return "<ERR>" end
	if v == nil then return nil end
	local s = safe_text(v)
	if s ~= nil then return s end
	return "<opaque>"
end

-- --------------------------------------------------------------- signatures
-- The panel's value signature: one "<name>=<value>" per stat row (the round-4
-- dy_value/stat_name route), falling back to the raw dy_value texts. Compared
-- raw; displayed truncated.
local function r5_sig(parts)
	if parts == nil then return nil end
	local items = {}
	local i = 0
	while i < #parts.rows and #items < R5.max_rows do
		i = i + 1
		local r = parts.rows[i]
		local name = r.name or ""
		local value = r.value or ""
		if name ~= "" or value ~= "" then
			items[#items + 1] = name .. "=" .. value
		end
	end
	if #items == 0 then
		i = 0
		while i < #parts.dys and #items < R5.max_rows do
			i = i + 1
			local v = parts.dys[i].stext
			if v ~= nil and v ~= "" then items[#items + 1] = v end
		end
	end
	return table.concat(items, "|")
end

local function r5_sig_text(s)
	if s == nil then return "nil" end
	local t = safe_text(s)
	if t == nil then return "<unreadable>" end
	t = string.gsub(t, "\n", " ")
	if #t > 300 then t = string.sub(t, 1, 300) .. "..." end
	return "\"" .. t .. "\""
end

-- ------------------------------------------------------------- panel scan
-- Find dynamic_stats under hud_battle, then walk ITS subtree (bounded) and
-- collect: the panel handle, its visibility, the template_stat rows (each with
-- its stat_name and dy_value texts), every dy_value, every label_compare.
local function r5_panel_parts()
	local ds = find_by_id_under_hud("dynamic_stats")
	if ds == nil then return nil end
	local vis = readb(function() return ds:Visible() end)
	local vfr = readb(function() return ds:VisibleFromRoot() end)
	local rows, dys, compares = {}, {}, {}
	local cur = nil
	local visits = 0
	local function visit(uic, depth)
		if uic == nil or visits >= R5.max_visits then return end
		visits = visits + 1
		local id = r5_read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
		if id == "template_stat" then
			if #rows < R5.max_rows then
				cur = { uic = uic, name = nil, value = nil }
				rows[#rows + 1] = cur
			else
				cur = nil
			end
		elseif id == "stat_name" and cur ~= nil and cur.name == nil then
			cur.name = r5_read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
		elseif id == "dy_value" then
			local st = r5_read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
			if cur ~= nil and cur.value == nil then cur.value = st end
			if #dys < R5.max_rows * 2 then
				dys[#dys + 1] = { uic = uic, stext = st }
			end
		elseif id == "label_compare" then
			if #compares < 60 then
				compares[#compares + 1] = {
					uic = uic,
					stext = r5_read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end),
					state = r5_read_text(function() return uic:CurrentState() end),
					vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end),
				}
			end
		end
		if depth >= R5.max_depth then return end
		local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
		if lua_type(n) == "number" and n > 0 then
			for i = 0, n - 1 do
				if visits >= R5.max_visits then return end
				local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
				if ok_c and child ~= nil then
					pcall(visit, wrap(child), depth + 1)
				end
			end
		end
	end
	pcall(visit, ds, 0)
	return { ds = ds, vis = vis, vfr = vfr, rows = rows, dys = dys, compares = compares }
end

-- --------------------------------------------------------------- the cards
-- The cards live under cards_panel/review_DY (lib_bm.lua's path); a card is a
-- review_DY child whose CallbackId answers "UnitCard". The card id IS the
-- unit's unique_ui_id as text (round-1 finding) and its CurrentState starts
-- with "selected" when selected (lib_bm does exactly this read).
local function r5_read_cards()
	local cards = {}
	local review = find_by_name("review_DY")
	if review == nil then review = find_by_id_under_hud("review_DY") end
	if review ~= nil then
		local n = read1(function() return review:ChildCount() end)
		if lua_type(n) == "number" and n > 0 then
			for i = 0, n - 1 do
				if #cards >= R5.max_cards then break end
				local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return review:Find(i) end)
				if ok_c and child ~= nil then
					local uic = wrap(child)
					if r5_read_text(function() return uic:CallbackId() end) == "UnitCard" then
						cards[#cards + 1] = {
							uic = uic,
							id = r5_read_text(function() return uic:Id() end),
							state = r5_read_text(function() return uic:CurrentState() end),
							vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end),
						}
					end
				end
			end
		end
	end
	if #cards == 0 then
		-- fallback: any UnitCard-CallbackId component under hud_battle
		local hud = find_by_name(DEFAULT_ROOT)
		if hud ~= nil then
			local visits = 0
			local function visit(uic, depth)
				if uic == nil or visits >= R5.max_visits or #cards >= R5.max_cards then return end
				visits = visits + 1
				if r5_read_text(function() return uic:CallbackId() end) == "UnitCard" then
					cards[#cards + 1] = {
						uic = uic,
						id = r5_read_text(function() return uic:Id() end),
						state = r5_read_text(function() return uic:CurrentState() end),
						vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end),
					}
					return
				end
				if depth >= R5.max_depth then return end
				local cn = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
				if lua_type(cn) == "number" and cn > 0 then
					for i = 0, cn - 1 do
						if visits >= R5.max_visits or #cards >= R5.max_cards then return end
						local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
						if ok_c and child ~= nil then
							pcall(visit, wrap(child), depth + 1)
						end
					end
				end
			end
			pcall(visit, hud, 0)
		end
	end
	return cards
end

local function r5_cards_text(cards)
	if cards == nil or #cards == 0 then return "(no cards)" end
	local parts = {}
	local i = 0
	while i < #cards and #parts < 24 do
		i = i + 1
		local c = cards[i]
		parts[#parts + 1] = "id=" .. q(c.id) .. " state=" .. q(c.state) .. " vis=" .. tostring(c.vis)
	end
	return table.concat(parts, "; ")
end

-- The selected set, derived from the card states (substring compare on a safe
-- copy: "selected" / "selected_hover" both count; string.find is never used).
local function r5_selected_set(cards)
	local sel = {}
	if cards == nil then return sel end
	for i = 1, #cards do
		local c = cards[i]
		local st = c.state
		if st ~= nil and c.vis == "true" and string.sub(st, 1, 8) == "selected" and c.id ~= nil then
			sel[c.id] = true
		end
	end
	return sel
end

local function r5_compares_text(compares)
	if compares == nil or #compares == 0 then return "(none)" end
	local parts = {}
	local i = 0
	while i < #compares and #parts < 8 do
		i = i + 1
		local c = compares[i]
		parts[#parts + 1] = "state=" .. q(c.state) .. " stext=" .. q(c.stext) .. " vis=" .. tostring(c.vis)
	end
	return table.concat(parts, "; ")
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the units
local function r5_read_units()
	local list = {}
	pcall(function()
		local sunits = bm:get_scriptunits_for_local_players_army()
		if sunits == nil then return end
		local total = sunits:count()
		if lua_type(total) ~= "number" then return end
		for i = 1, total do
			if #list >= R5.max_units then break end
			local su = sunits:item(i)
			if su ~= nil then
				local u = su.unit
				local uid, uid_ok = nil, false
				if u ~= nil then
					uid, uid_ok = read1(function() return u:unique_ui_id() end)
				end
				local uid_text = nil
				if uid_ok and uid ~= nil then uid_text = safe_text(uid) end
				list[#list + 1] = { su = su, unit = u, uid = uid, uid_text = uid_text }
			end
		end
	end)
	return list
end

-- The selected-unit guess and the non-selected candidate, from the cards.
-- Returns sel_su, sel_why, nonsel, nonsel_why. The two never share an entry.
local function r5_pick_units(units, sel)
	local sel_su, sel_why = nil, nil
	local nonsel, nonsel_why = nil, nil
	for i = 1, #units do
		local e = units[i]
		if e.uid_text ~= nil and sel[e.uid_text] == true then
			if sel_su == nil then
				sel_su = e
				sel_why = "card state says selected"
			end
		elseif nonsel == nil and e.uid_text ~= nil then
			nonsel = e
			nonsel_why = "card state says NOT selected"
		end
	end
	if sel_su == nil and #units > 0 then
		sel_su = units[1]
		sel_why = "fallback: first unit in the army list (no card matched)"
	end
	if nonsel == sel_su then
		nonsel, nonsel_why = nil, nil
	end
	if nonsel == nil then
		for i = 1, #units do
			local e = units[i]
			if e ~= sel_su and e.uid_text ~= nil then
				nonsel = e
				nonsel_why = "fallback: another army unit (selection could not be read)"
				break
			end
		end
	end
	return sel_su, sel_why, nonsel, nonsel_why
end

-- ------------------------------------------------------------ context reads
local function r5_ctx_line(uic, label, type_id)
	local o_ok, o_raw = pcall(function() return uic:GetContextObject(type_id) end)
	local o_type = nil
	local o_text = "<ERR>"
	if o_ok then
		o_type = lua_type(o_raw)
		o_text = q(text_of(o_raw, true))
	end
	r5_out("ctx " .. label .. " GetContextObject(" .. q(type_id) .. ") -> type="
		.. tostring(o_type) .. " value=" .. o_text)
end

local function r5_ctx_probe(uic, label)
	for t = 1, #R5.ctx_types do
		local type_id = R5.ctx_types[t]
		local id_ok, id_raw = pcall(function() return uic:GetContextObjectId(type_id) end)
		local id_text = nil
		if id_ok then id_text = safe_text(id_raw) end
		r5_out("ctx " .. label .. " GetContextObjectId(" .. q(type_id) .. ") = "
			.. (id_ok and q(id_text) or "<ERR>"))
		r5_ctx_line(uic, label, type_id)
	end
end

-- ------------------------------------------------------------- candidates
-- The task's four, plus the vanilla-proven cco("CcoUnitDetails", id) shape,
-- for the selected-unit guess; then the same five for a NON-selected unit.
local function r5_build_candidates(sel_su, nonsel)
	local cands = {}
	local function add(name, kind, value)
		if value == nil then return end
		cands[#cands + 1] = { name = name, kind = kind, value = value }
	end
	local function add_unit_five(tag, e)
		if e == nil or e.uid_text == nil then return end
		add(tag .. " script_unit", "su", e.su)
		add(tag .. " battle_unit (su.unit)", "unit", e.unit)
		add(tag .. " ui id (number)", "number", e.uid)
		add(tag .. " ui id (text)", "text", e.uid_text)
		if lua_type(r5_cco) == "function" then
			local arg = e.uid
			local slot = "number"
			if arg == nil then
				arg = e.uid_text
				slot = "text"
			end
			local ok, obj = pcall(r5_cco, "CcoUnitDetails", arg)
			if ok and obj ~= nil then
				add("cco('CcoUnitDetails', " .. tag .. " id " .. slot .. ")", "cco", obj)
			end
		end
	end
	if sel_su ~= nil then add_unit_five("sel", sel_su) end
	if nonsel ~= nil then add_unit_five("nonsel", nonsel) end
	return cands
end

-- ------------------------------------------------------------ run lifecycle
local function r5_abort(msg)
	r5_out("===== R5 RUN #" .. tostring(r5.run_no) .. " ABORTED: " .. msg .. " =====")
	r5.active = false
	r5.phase = "idle"
end

local function r5_phase_after(test_id)
	if r5.mode == "full" then
		if test_id == "1" then return "t2_prep" end
		if test_id == "2" then return "t3_prep" end
		if test_id == "3" then return "t4_prep" end
	end
	return "done"
end

local function r5_start(origin, mode)
	if r5.active then return false end
	if r5.runs >= R5.max_runs then
		r5_out("run refused: the run cap (" .. tostring(R5.max_runs)
			.. ") is reached - restart the battle for a fresh budget")
		return false
	end
	r5.runs = r5.runs + 1
	r5.run_no = r5.runs
	r5.active = true
	r5.origin = origin or "manual"
	r5.mode = mode or "full"
	r5.cand_i = 0
	r5.candidates = nil
	r5.cur_cand_name = nil
	r5.sel_unit = nil
	r5.sim_card = nil
	r5.baseline = nil
	r5.cur_sig = nil
	r5.orig_cco = nil
	if r5.mode == "full" or r5.mode == "1" then
		r5.phase = "t1_read"
	elseif r5.mode == "2" then
		r5.phase = "t2_prep"
	elseif r5.mode == "3" then
		r5.phase = "t3_prep"
	else
		r5.phase = "t4_prep"
	end
	r5.next_at = tick_count
	r5_out("")
	r5_out("===== R5 RUN #" .. tostring(r5.run_no) .. " (" .. tostring(r5.origin)
		.. ", mode " .. tostring(r5.mode) .. ") =====")
	return true
end

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------ stages
local r5_stages = {}

r5_stages["t1_read"] = function()
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	if parts == nil then
		r5_abort("the stat panel (dynamic_stats) was not found under hud_battle - open AND pin the unit-details panel, then retry")
		return
	end
	local sig = r5_sig(parts)
	if sig == nil or sig == "" then
		r5_abort("dynamic_stats found but no stat values are rendered (no unit selected? panel collapsed?)")
		return
	end
	r5_out("===== R5 RUN #" .. tostring(r5.run_no) .. " TEST 1: GetContextObject reads (READ-ONLY) =====")
	r5_out("R5.1 panel via dynamic_stats vis=" .. tostring(parts.vis) .. " vfr=" .. tostring(parts.vfr)
		.. " values=" .. r5_sig_text(sig))
	r5_ctx_probe(parts.ds, "dynamic_stats")
	local row = parts.rows[1]
	if row ~= nil and row.uic ~= nil then
		r5_ctx_probe(row.uic, "template_stat row 1 (name=" .. q(row.name) .. ")")
	else
		r5_out("R5.1 no template_stat row was found under the panel")
	end
	local dy = parts.dys[1]
	if dy ~= nil and dy.uic ~= nil then
		r5_ctx_probe(dy.uic, "dy_value 1 (stext=" .. q(dy.stext) .. ")")
	else
		r5_out("R5.1 no dy_value was found under the panel")
	end
	r5_out("R5.1 TEST 1 done (this test performs NO writes)")
	r5.phase = r5_phase_after("1")
	r5.next_at = tick_count
end

r5_stages["t2_prep"] = function()
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	if parts == nil then
		r5_abort("the stat panel (dynamic_stats) was not found under hud_battle - open AND pin the unit-details panel, then retry")
		return
	end
	local sig = r5_sig(parts)
	if sig == nil or sig == "" then
		r5_abort("dynamic_stats found but no stat values are rendered (no unit selected? panel collapsed?)")
		return
	end
	r5.panel = parts.ds
	r5.baseline = sig
	r5.cur_sig = sig
	local o_ok, o_raw = pcall(function() return parts.ds:GetContextObject(R5.ctx_types[1]) end)
	r5.orig_cco = nil
	if o_ok and o_raw ~= nil then r5.orig_cco = o_raw end
	r5_out("===== R5 RUN #" .. tostring(r5.run_no) .. " TEST 2: SetContextObject candidates =====")
	r5_out("R5.2 baseline values " .. r5_sig_text(r5.baseline))
	r5_out("R5.2 original GetContextObject(" .. q(R5.ctx_types[1]) .. ") read="
		.. (o_ok and "ok" or "ERR") .. " restore object="
		.. (r5.orig_cco ~= nil and "readable" or "none"))
	if lua_type(r5_cco) ~= "function" then
		r5_out("R5.2 note: the global cco() is NOT available here - the cco candidates are skipped")
	end
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
	r5_out("R5.2 cards: " .. r5_cards_text(cards))
	local units = r5_read_units()
	local sel_su, sel_why, nonsel, nonsel_why = r5_pick_units(units, sel)
	r5_out("R5.2 selected-unit guess: "
		.. (sel_su ~= nil and (q(sel_su.uid_text) .. " (" .. tostring(sel_why) .. ")") or "NONE"))
	r5_out("R5.2 non-selected candidate: "
		.. (nonsel ~= nil and (q(nonsel.uid_text) .. " (" .. tostring(nonsel_why) .. ")") or "NONE"))
	r5.candidates = r5_build_candidates(sel_su, nonsel)
	r5_out("R5.2 " .. tostring(#r5.candidates) .. " candidate(s) will be tried in order")
	r5.phase = "t2_set"
	r5.next_at = tick_count
end

r5_stages["t2_set"] = function()
	if r5.candidates == nil or r5.cand_i >= #r5.candidates then
		r5_out("R5.2 TEST 2 done (" .. tostring(r5.cand_i) .. " candidate(s) tried)")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("2")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	if r5.sets >= R5.max_sets then
		r5_out("R5.2 set cap reached (" .. tostring(R5.max_sets) .. ") - no more SetContextObject writes")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("2")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	r5.cand_i = r5.cand_i + 1
	local c = r5.candidates[r5.cand_i]
	r5.cur_cand_name = c.name
	-- log BEFORE the write: if the engine dies here, this names the candidate
	r5_out("R5.2 set #" .. tostring(r5.cand_i) .. "/" .. tostring(#r5.candidates)
		.. " candidate: " .. c.name .. " [" .. c.kind .. "] -> dynamic_stats:SetContextObject")
	r5.sets = r5.sets + 1
	local ok, err = r7_skip_write("R5.2 set #" .. tostring(r5.cand_i) .. "/" .. tostring(#r5.candidates)
		.. " candidate " .. c.name .. " -> dynamic_stats")
	local err_text = nil
	if not ok then err_text = truncate(err, 140) end
	r5.phase = "t2_check"
	r5.next_at = tick_count + R5.settle
	if err_text == nil then
		r5_out("R5.2 set #" .. tostring(r5.cand_i) .. " accepted (no Lua error)")
	else
		r5_out("R5.2 set #" .. tostring(r5.cand_i) .. " not performed: " .. err_text)
	end
end

r5_stages["t2_check"] = function()
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	local sig = r5_sig(parts)
	local changed = (parts ~= nil) and (sig ~= r5.cur_sig)
	local cand_name = r5.cur_cand_name
	if parts ~= nil then
		r5_ctx_line(parts.ds, "dynamic_stats", R5.ctx_types[1])
		r5_ctx_line(parts.ds, "dynamic_stats", R5.ctx_types[2])
		local dy = parts.dys[1]
		if dy ~= nil and dy.uic ~= nil then
			r5_ctx_line(dy.uic, "dy_value 1", R5.ctx_types[2])
		end
	end
	if changed and r5.orig_cco ~= nil then
		r5_out("R5.2 after candidate #" .. tostring(r5.cand_i) .. " (" .. tostring(cand_name)
			.. "): values CHANGED *** | now " .. r5_sig_text(sig))
		r5_out("R5.2 CHANGE detected - restoring the original context object")
		r5.sets = r5.sets + 1
		local ok_r, err_r = r7_skip_write("R5.2 restore of the original context object")
		r5.phase = "t2_restore"
		r5.next_at = tick_count + R5.settle
		if not ok_r then
			r5_out("R5.2 restore not performed: " .. truncate(err_r, 140))
		end
		return
	end
	r5.cur_sig = sig
	r5.phase = "t2_set"
	r5.next_at = tick_count
	if changed then
		r5_out("R5.2 after candidate #" .. tostring(r5.cand_i) .. " (" .. tostring(cand_name)
			.. "): values CHANGED *** | now " .. r5_sig_text(sig))
		r5_out("R5.2 CHANGE detected - no restore object was readable; re-select a unit to restore the panel")
	else
		r5_out("R5.2 after candidate #" .. tostring(r5.cand_i) .. " (" .. tostring(cand_name)
			.. "): values unchanged | " .. r5_sig_text(sig))
	end
end

r5_stages["t2_restore"] = function()
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	local sig = r5_sig(parts)
	local back = (parts ~= nil) and (sig == r5.baseline)
	r5.cur_sig = sig
	r5_out("R5.2 restore result: values now "
		.. (back and "back at the original baseline" or "NOT back at the baseline")
		.. " | " .. r5_sig_text(sig))
	r5.phase = "t2_set"
	r5.next_at = tick_count
end

r5_stages["t3_prep"] = function()
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	if parts == nil then
		r5_abort("the stat panel (dynamic_stats) was not found under hud_battle - open AND pin the unit-details panel, then retry")
		return
	end
	local sig = r5_sig(parts)
	if sig == nil or sig == "" then
		r5_abort("dynamic_stats found but no stat values are rendered (no unit selected? panel collapsed?)")
		return
	end
	r5.cur_sig = sig
	r5_out("===== R5 RUN #" .. tostring(r5.run_no) .. " TEST 3: select_in_ui on a non-selected unit =====")
	r5_out("R5.3 panel values before: " .. r5_sig_text(sig))
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
	r5.sel_before = sel
	r5_out("R5.3 cards before: " .. r5_cards_text(cards))
	local units = r5_read_units()
	local sel_su, sel_why, nonsel, nonsel_why = r5_pick_units(units, sel)
	local i = 0
	while i < #units and i < 20 do
		i = i + 1
		local e = units[i]
		r5_out("R5.3 unit " .. q(e.uid_text) .. " selected="
			.. tostring(e.uid_text ~= nil and sel[e.uid_text] == true))
	end
	if nonsel == nil then
		r5_out("R5.3 TEST 3 skipped: no non-selected unit available")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("3")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	if r5.selects >= R5.max_selects then
		r5_out("R5.3 select cap reached (" .. tostring(R5.max_selects) .. ") - no more select_in_ui writes")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("3")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	r5.sel_unit = nonsel
	r5.phase = "t3_do"
	r5.next_at = tick_count
end

r5_stages["t3_do"] = function()
	local e = r5.sel_unit
	if e == nil or e.unit == nil then
		r5_out("R5.3 TEST 3 skipped: the chosen unit handle is gone")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("3")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	r5_out("R5.3 would call battle_unit:select_in_ui() on unit " .. q(e.uid_text)
		.. " (NOT in the selected set) - round 7: REMOVED (zero-write build)")
	r5.selects = r5.selects + 1
	local ok, err = r7_skip_write("R5.3 select_in_ui on unit " .. q(e.uid_text))
	local err_text = nil
	if not ok then err_text = truncate(err, 140) end
	r5.phase = "t3_wait"
	r5.next_at = tick_count + R5.settle
	if err_text == nil then
		r5_out("R5.3 select_in_ui accepted (no Lua error) - watch the screen: the selection may visibly jump")
	else
		r5_out("R5.3 select_in_ui not performed: " .. err_text)
	end
end

r5_stages["t3_wait"] = function()
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
	local same = true
	for id in pairs(sel) do
		if r5.sel_before == nil or r5.sel_before[id] ~= true then same = false end
	end
	if r5.sel_before ~= nil then
		for id in pairs(r5.sel_before) do
			if sel[id] ~= true then same = false end
		end
	end
	r5_out("R5.3 cards after: " .. r5_cards_text(cards))
	r5_out("R5.3 selection " .. (same and "unchanged" or "DID change"))
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	local sig = r5_sig(parts)
	local pchg = (parts ~= nil) and (sig ~= r5.cur_sig)
	r5_out("R5.3 panel after: values " .. (pchg and "CHANGED ***" or "unchanged")
		.. " | now " .. r5_sig_text(sig))
	r5.cur_sig = sig
	r5_out("R5.3 TEST 3 done")
	r5.phase = r5_phase_after("3")
	r5.next_at = tick_count + R5.settle
end

r5_stages["t4_prep"] = function()
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	if parts == nil then
		r5_abort("the stat panel (dynamic_stats) was not found under hud_battle - open AND pin the unit-details panel, then retry")
		return
	end
	r5.cur_sig = r5_sig(parts)
	r5_out("===== R5 RUN #" .. tostring(r5.run_no) .. " TEST 4: SimulateMouseOn on another card =====")
	r5_out("R5.4 label_compare before: " .. r5_compares_text(parts.compares))
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
	local chosen, why = nil, nil
	local i = 0
	while i < #cards do
		i = i + 1
		local c = cards[i]
		if c.vis == "true" and not (c.id ~= nil and sel[c.id] == true) then
			chosen = c
			why = "visible card whose id is NOT in the selected set"
			break
		end
	end
	if chosen == nil then
		i = 0
		while i < #cards do
			i = i + 1
			if cards[i].vis == "true" then
				chosen = cards[i]
				why = "fallback: first visible card"
				break
			end
		end
	end
	if chosen == nil then
		r5_out("R5.4 TEST 4 skipped: no unit card found (cards_panel / review_DY)")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("4")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	if #parts.compares == 0 then
		r5_out("R5.4 TEST 4 skipped: no label_compare components under the panel (nothing to observe)")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("4")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	if r5.sims >= R5.max_sims then
		r5_out("R5.4 simulation cap reached (" .. tostring(R5.max_sims) .. ") - no more SimulateMouseOn writes")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("4")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	r5.sim_card = chosen
	r5_out("R5.4 chosen card id=" .. q(chosen.id) .. " state=" .. q(chosen.state)
		.. " (" .. tostring(why) .. ")")
	r5.phase = "t4_do"
	r5.next_at = tick_count
end

r5_stages["t4_do"] = function()
	local c = r5.sim_card
	if c == nil then
		r5_out("R5.4 TEST 4 skipped: the card handle is gone")
		r5.phase = r5_phase_after("4")
		r5.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	r5_out("R5.4 would call SimulateMouseOn() on card " .. q(c.id) .. " - round 7: REMOVED (zero-write build)")
	r5.sims = r5.sims + 1
	local ok, err = r7_skip_write("R5.4 SimulateMouseOn on card " .. q(c.id))
	local err_text = nil
	if not ok then err_text = truncate(err, 140) end
	r5.phase = "t4_wait"
	r5.next_at = tick_count + R5.settle
	if err_text == nil then
		r5_out("R5.4 SimulateMouseOn accepted (no Lua error)")
	else
		r5_out("R5.4 SimulateMouseOn not performed: " .. err_text)
	end
end

r5_stages["t4_wait"] = function()
	pcall(function()
		local parts = r5_panel_parts()
		if parts ~= nil then
			r5_out("R5.4 while hovered: label_compare " .. r5_compares_text(parts.compares)
				.. " | panel values " .. r5_sig_text(r5_sig(parts)))
		else
			r5_out("R5.4 while hovered: the panel could not be re-read")
		end
	end)
	-- the doc: a simulated mouse-on STICKS unless SimulateMouseOff is called
	local ok_off, err_off = r7_skip_write("R5.4 SimulateMouseOff (the release)")
	r5.phase = "t4_off"
	r5.next_at = tick_count + R5.settle
	if ok_off then
		r5_out("R5.4 SimulateMouseOff called (the mouse-on is released)")
	else
		r5_out("R5.4 SimulateMouseOff not performed: " .. truncate(err_off, 140))
	end
end

r5_stages["t4_off"] = function()
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	if parts ~= nil then
		r5_out("R5.4 after MouseOff: label_compare " .. r5_compares_text(parts.compares)
			.. " | panel values " .. r5_sig_text(r5_sig(parts)))
	end
	r5_out("R5.4 TEST 4 done")
	r5.phase = r5_phase_after("4")
	r5.next_at = tick_count
end

r5_stages["done"] = function()
	r5_out("===== R5 RUN #" .. tostring(r5.run_no) .. " (" .. tostring(r5.origin)
		.. ", mode " .. tostring(r5.mode) .. ") DONE =====")
	if r5.origin == "auto" then r5.auto_done = true end
	r5.active = false
	r5.phase = "idle"
end

local function r5_step()
	local fn = r5_stages[r5.phase]
	if fn ~= nil then fn() end
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the hooks
local function r5_queue(origin, mode, what)
	local ok, started = pcall(r5_start, origin, mode)
	if not ok then return PROBE_TAG .. "r5 error: " .. tostring(started) end
	if not started then return PROBE_TAG .. "r5 not started (see the log: " .. LOG_FILE .. ")" end
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R5 " .. what .. " queued - the stat panel must be open (and pinned); log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r5()
	return r5_queue("manual", "full", "full run (tests 1-4)")
end

function zz_probe_r5_context()
	return r5_queue("manual", "1", "test 1 only (GetContextObject, read-only)")
end

function zz_probe_r5_setctx()
	return r5_queue("manual", "2", "test 2 only (SetContextObject candidates)")
end

function zz_probe_r5_select()
	return r5_queue("manual", "3", "test 3 only (select_in_ui)")
end

function zz_probe_r5_hover()
	return r5_queue("manual", "4", "test 4 only (SimulateMouseOn)")
end

function zz_probe_r5_status()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "r5 active=" .. tostring(r5.active) .. " phase=" .. tostring(r5.phase)
		.. " runs=" .. tostring(r5.runs) .. "/" .. tostring(R5.max_runs)
		.. " sets=" .. tostring(r5.sets) .. "/" .. tostring(R5.max_sets)
		.. " selects=" .. tostring(r5.selects) .. "/" .. tostring(R5.max_selects)
		.. " sims=" .. tostring(r5.sims) .. "/" .. tostring(R5.max_sims)
		.. " auto_done=" .. tostring(r5.auto_done)
		.. " | manual: zz_probe_r5() / zz_probe_r5_context() / zz_probe_r5_setctx() /"
		.. " zz_probe_r5_select() / zz_probe_r5_hover() | log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r5_help()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R5 CROSS-UNIT EXPERIMENT: open AND PIN the unit-details panel"
		.. " (select one unit first). When the panel becomes visible ONE automatic run"
		.. " queues; it tries GetContextObject (read-only), then SetContextObject on"
		.. " dynamic_stats with the selected unit's script_unit / battle_unit / ui id"
		.. " (number and text) / cco('CcoUnitDetails', id), then the same five for a"
		.. " NON-selected unit, then select_in_ui on a non-selected unit, then"
		.. " SimulateMouseOn on another card (released with SimulateMouseOff)."
		.. " Each test is its own labelled block (grep 'R5.1' .. 'R5.4'). Caps:"
		.. " " .. tostring(R5.max_runs) .. " runs / " .. tostring(R5.max_sets) .. " sets / "
		.. tostring(R5.max_selects) .. " selects / " .. tostring(R5.max_sims) .. " sims."
		.. " Manual: zz_probe_r5() (full) or the per-test hooks. Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

-- ============================================================================
-- 11. ROUND 6 - ONE-WRITE-PER-PASS CONTEXT LADDER (the ONLY automatic
--     experiment; the R5 auto ladder is disarmed above). See the ROUND 6 block
--     at the top of the file for the research findings and the pass ladder.
-- ============================================================================

local R6 = {
	root_name = "unit_information",
	target_name = "dynamic_stats",
	types = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoUnitStat", "CcoBattleUnit" },
	max_pass = 3,     -- HARD CAP: the ladder (1 sel / 2 nonsel / 3 raw unit)
	settle = 15,      -- ticks (~3 s) after a write before the re-read
	max_sets = 3,     -- HARD CAP: SetContextObject writes (one per pass)
	walk_max = 10,    -- live-read parent-chain walk cap
}

local r6 = {
	active = false, phase = "idle", next_at = 0,
	armed_pass = 0, next_pass = 1, origin = nil,
	auto_done = true, auto_attempts = 0, wait_spoken = false,   -- ROUND 7: disarmed at load
	done = false, sets = 0,
	pass = 0, kind = nil, last = nil,
	write_ok = nil, write_err_text = nil, obj_tid = nil, obj_src = nil,
	sig_now = nil, target = nil, root = nil,
	sel = nil, nonsel = nil, before_sig = nil, cards = nil,
}

function R6.out(msg) log("R6 " .. tostring(msg)) end

function R6.pass_name(k)
	if k == 1 then return "the selected unit's own cco (CONTROL)" end
	if k == 2 then return "the non-selected unit's cco" end
	if k == 3 then return "the raw battle_unit userdata" end
	return "?"
end

function R6.cand_desc(kind)
	if kind == "sel" then return "the selected unit's own cco" end
	if kind == "nonsel" then return "the non-selected unit's cco" end
	return "the raw battle_unit userdata"
end

-- diag: GetContextObjectId / GetContextObject for the REAL type ids (layout).
function R6.diag(label, uic)
	if uic == nil then
		R6.out("diag " .. label .. ": component NOT FOUND")
		return
	end
	for i = 1, #R6.types do
		local tid = R6.types[i]
		local id_ok, id_raw = pcall(function() return uic:GetContextObjectId(tid) end)
		local id_txt = "<ERR>"
		if id_ok then
			if id_raw == nil then id_txt = "nil" else id_txt = q(text_of(id_raw, true)) end
		end
		local o_ok, o_raw = pcall(function() return uic:GetContextObject(tid) end)
		local o_txt = "<ERR>"
		if o_ok then
			if o_raw == nil then o_txt = "nil" else o_txt = "type=" .. lua_type(o_raw) .. " value=" .. q(text_of(o_raw, true)) end
		end
		R6.out("diag " .. label .. " GetContextObjectId(" .. q(tid) .. ")=" .. id_txt
			.. " | GetContextObject -> " .. o_txt)
	end
end

-- the vanilla-proven contrast: a unit CARD answers GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit")
-- (wh3_battle_prologue_values.lua performs exactly this read in battle).
function R6.contrast_reads(label)
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	r6.cards = cards
	local maxn = #cards
	if maxn > 4 then maxn = 4 end
	for i = 1, maxn do
		local c = cards[i]
		if c.uic ~= nil then
			local ok_id, raw = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit") end)
			local txt = "<ERR>"
			if ok_id then
				if raw == nil then txt = "nil" else txt = q(text_of(raw, true)) end
			end
			R6.out("contrast " .. label .. " card id=" .. q(c.id) .. " state=" .. q(c.state)
				.. " GetContextObjectId(\"CcoBattleUnit\")=" .. txt)
		end
	end
	return cards
end

-- the panel handle set: dynamic_stats + unit_information + first dy_value + signature
function R6.panel_bits()
	local parts = r5_panel_parts()
	if parts == nil then return nil end
	local root = find_by_name(R6.root_name)
	if root == nil then root = find_by_id_under_hud(R6.root_name) end
	local dy1 = nil
	if parts.dys ~= nil and parts.dys[1] ~= nil then dy1 = parts.dys[1].uic end
	return { ds = parts.ds, root = root, dy1 = dy1, parts = parts, sig = r5_sig(parts) }
end

-- one build attempt with one callable; type ids tried in order (never cached).
function R6.try_fn(label, fn, arg)
	local vars = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoBattleUnit" }
	for i = 1, #vars do
		local tid = vars[i]
		R6.out("build: " .. label .. "(" .. q(tid) .. ", " .. q(arg) .. ") attempting (log-before-call)")
		local ok, obj = pcall(fn, tid, arg)
		if not ok then
			R6.out("build: " .. label .. "(" .. q(tid) .. ") FAILED: " .. truncate(obj, 140))
		elseif obj == nil then
			R6.out("build: " .. label .. "(" .. q(tid) .. ") -> nil")
		else
			R6.out("build: " .. label .. "(" .. q(tid) .. ") -> object, type=" .. lua_type(obj))
			return obj, label .. "(" .. tid .. ", " .. tostring(arg) .. ")", tid
		end
	end
	return nil, nil, nil
end

-- live-read fallback: walk UP the parent chain, GetContextObject per level
-- (the object that is ALREADY rendering IS the unit's own cco).
function R6.live_read(seed, types)
	if seed == nil then
		R6.out("build source 3: live-read - no seed component available")
		return nil, nil, nil
	end
	local uic = seed
	local level = 0
	while uic ~= nil and level < R6.walk_max do
		level = level + 1
		local id = r5_read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
		for i = 1, #types do
			local tid = types[i]
			local ok_o, o = pcall(function() return uic:GetContextObject(tid) end)
			if ok_o and o ~= nil then
				R6.out("build source 3: live-read GetContextObject(" .. q(tid) .. ") @ level "
					.. tostring(level) .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " -> type=" .. lua_type(o))
				return o, "live-read GetContextObject(" .. tid .. ") @ level " .. tostring(level)
					.. " id=" .. tostring(id), tid
			end
		end
		R6.out("build source 3: live-read level " .. tostring(level) .. " id=" .. q(id)
			.. " -> no context object for " .. tostring(#types) .. " type(s)")
		local ok_p, p = pcall(function() return uic:Parent() end)
		if not ok_p or p == nil then break end
		local casted = wrap(p)
		if casted == nil then break end
		uic = casted
	end
	R6.out("build source 3: live-read walked " .. tostring(level) .. " level(s) - no context object found")
	return nil, nil, nil
end

-- build the pass's candidate: global cco -> core.cco / core:cco -> live-read.
function R6.build(arg, live_seed, live_types)
	local ok_g, g = pcall(function() return cco end)
	if ok_g and lua_type(g) == "function" then
		R6.out("build source 1: global cco -> function (re-checked at use time, never cached)")
		local obj, src, tid = R6.try_fn("global cco", g, arg)
		if obj ~= nil then return obj, src, tid end
	else
		R6.out("build source 1: global cco -> "
			.. (ok_g and ("type=" .. tostring(lua_type(g))) or "<ERR>"))
		R6.out("build *** the global cco() is NOT reachable from this battle mod script ***"
			.. " (re-checked at use time; no shipped Lua file defines it - 30 call sites,"
			.. " 0 definitions; it is an engine-registered global like UIComponent /"
			.. " UIComponent; the only vanilla battle call is the ping icon)")
	end
	local ok_c, cdot = pcall(function() return core.cco end)
	if ok_c and lua_type(cdot) == "function" then
		R6.out("build source 2: core.cco -> function")
		local obj, src, tid = R6.try_fn("core.cco", cdot, arg)
		if obj ~= nil then return obj, src, tid end
	else
		R6.out("build source 2: core.cco -> "
			.. (ok_c and ("type=" .. tostring(lua_type(cdot))) or "<ERR>"))
	end
	R6.out("build source 2b: core:cco(...) attempting (log-before-call)")
	local ok_col, col = pcall(function() return core:cco("CcoUnitDetails", arg) end)
	if ok_col and col ~= nil then
		R6.out("build source 2b: core:cco -> object, type=" .. lua_type(col))
		return col, "core:cco('CcoUnitDetails', " .. tostring(arg) .. ")", "CcoUnitDetails"
	end
	R6.out("build source 2b: core:cco -> "
		.. (ok_col and "nil" or ("<ERR: " .. truncate(col, 100) .. ">")))
	return R6.live_read(live_seed, live_types)
end

-- did the write LAND? (the real discriminator: after a successful
-- SetContextObject the target answers a truthy GetContextObjectId)
function R6.landed_check(bits)
	if bits == nil or bits.ds == nil then return false, "panel gone" end
	local tids = R6.types
	if r6.obj_tid ~= nil then tids = { r6.obj_tid } end
	for i = 1, #tids do
		local ok_l, l = pcall(function() return bits.ds:GetContextObjectId(tids[i]) end)
		if ok_l and l ~= nil then return true, tids[i] end
	end
	return false, "nil"
end

function R6.card_for(cards, uid_text)
	if cards == nil or uid_text == nil then return nil end
	for i = 1, #cards do
		if cards[i].id == uid_text then return cards[i].uic end
	end
	return nil
end

function R6.arm(k, origin)
	if k == nil or k < 1 or k > R6.max_pass then
		R6.out("arm refused: pass " .. tostring(k) .. " is outside 1.." .. tostring(R6.max_pass))
		return false
	end
	if r6.active then
		R6.out("arm refused: pass " .. tostring(r6.pass) .. " is still running")
		return false
	end
	if r6.sets >= R6.max_sets then
		R6.out("arm refused: the set cap (" .. tostring(R6.max_sets) .. "/" .. tostring(R6.max_sets)
			.. ") is reached - restart the game for a fresh budget")
		return false
	end
	if r6.armed_pass ~= 0 then
		R6.out("note: re-arming - pass " .. tostring(r6.armed_pass) .. " was pending, pass "
			.. tostring(k) .. " replaces it")
	end
	r6.armed_pass = k
	r6.origin = origin or "manual"
	r6.wait_spoken = false
	r6.auto_done = true      -- any arm (auto included) cancels the auto pass-1 arm
	R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. "/" .. tostring(R6.max_pass) .. " armed ("
		.. tostring(r6.origin) .. "): " .. R6.pass_name(k)
		.. " - ONE SetContextObject write, then the pass STOPS (advance: zz_probe_r6_next())")
	return true
end

function R6.hook_arm(k, origin, what)
	local ok, armed = pcall(R6.arm, k, origin)
	if not ok then return PROBE_TAG .. "r6 error: " .. tostring(armed) end
	if not armed then return PROBE_TAG .. "r6 not armed (see the log: " .. LOG_FILE .. ")" end
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R6 " .. what .. " armed - select one unit first, open AND PIN the"
		.. " unit-details panel; log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

function R6.try_begin()
	if r6.sig_now == nil or not contains_str(r6.sig_now, R6.target_name) then
		if not r6.wait_spoken then
			r6.wait_spoken = true
			R6.out("pass " .. tostring(r6.armed_pass) .. " is armed; waiting for the stat panel ("
				.. R6.target_name .. ") to become visible - select one unit, open AND PIN the unit-details panel")
		end
		return false
	end
	local k = r6.armed_pass
	r6.armed_pass = 0
	r6.active = true
	r6.phase = "prep"
	r6.pass = k
	r6.next_pass = k + 1
	if r6.next_pass > R6.max_pass then r6.next_pass = R6.max_pass + 1 end
	r6.write_ok = nil
	r6.write_err_text = nil
	r6.obj_tid = nil
	r6.obj_src = nil
	r6.last = nil
	r6.next_at = tick_count
	r6.wait_spoken = false
	return true
end

function R6.prep()
	local k = r6.pass
	R6.out("")
	R6.out("===== R6 PASS " .. tostring(k) .. "/" .. tostring(R6.max_pass) .. " (origin "
		.. tostring(r6.origin) .. "): " .. R6.pass_name(k) .. " =====")
	local bits = R6.panel_bits()
	if bits == nil then
		r6.last = "no-panel"
		R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " ABORTED before any write: dynamic_stats / stat values"
			.. " were not found - select one unit and open AND PIN the unit-details panel,"
			.. " then retry with zz_probe_r6_next()")
		r6.phase = "finish"
		r6.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	r6.target = bits.ds
	r6.root = bits.root
	r6.before_sig = bits.sig
	R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " BEFORE: panel vis=" .. tostring(bits.parts.vis)
		.. " vfr=" .. tostring(bits.parts.vfr) .. " values=" .. r5_sig_text(bits.sig))
	R6.diag("BEFORE dynamic_stats", bits.ds)
	R6.diag("BEFORE unit_information", bits.root)
	R6.diag("BEFORE dy_value 1", bits.dy1)
	local cards = R6.contrast_reads("BEFORE")
	local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
	R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " cards: " .. r5_cards_text(cards))
	local units = r5_read_units()
	local sel_e, sel_why, nonsel_e, nonsel_why = r5_pick_units(units, sel)
	r6.sel = sel_e
	r6.nonsel = nonsel_e
	R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " selected-unit guess: "
		.. (sel_e ~= nil and (q(sel_e.uid_text) .. " (" .. tostring(sel_why) .. ")") or "NONE"))
	R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " non-selected candidate: "
		.. (nonsel_e ~= nil and (q(nonsel_e.uid_text) .. " (" .. tostring(nonsel_why) .. ")") or "NONE"))
	local kind = (k == 1) and "sel" or ((k == 2) and "nonsel" or "raw")
	r6.kind = kind
	local obj, src, tid = nil, nil, nil
	local entry = nil
	if kind == "raw" then
		entry = nonsel_e or sel_e
		if entry ~= nil then obj = entry.unit end
		src = "raw battle_unit userdata (su.unit)"
		if obj ~= nil then
			R6.out("build: the raw candidate is a " .. lua_type(obj)
				.. " - the most dangerous candidate; this pass performs exactly ONE write")
		else
			R6.out("build: the raw candidate is nil (no readable unit handle) - no write")
		end
	else
		if kind == "sel" then entry = sel_e else entry = nonsel_e end
		if entry == nil or (entry.uid == nil and entry.uid_text == nil) then
			r6.last = "no-unit"
			R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " ABORTED before any write: no " .. tostring(kind)
				.. " unit handle available")
			r6.phase = "finish"
			r6.next_at = tick_count
			return
		end
		local arg = entry.uid
		if arg == nil then arg = entry.uid_text end
		local live_seed = bits.ds
		local live_types = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoUnitStat", "CcoBattleUnit" }
		if kind == "nonsel" then
			live_seed = R6.card_for(cards, entry.uid_text)
			if live_seed == nil then live_seed = bits.ds end
			live_types = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoBattleUnit", "CcoUnitStat" }
		end
		obj, src, tid = R6.build(arg, live_seed, live_types)
	end
	if obj == nil then
		r6.last = "no-obj"
		R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " *** NO object could be built - NO WRITE performed ***"
			.. " (one-write-per-pass: the pass ends here; see the build lines above)")
		r6.phase = "finish"
		r6.next_at = tick_count
		return
	end
	r6.obj_src = src
	r6.obj_tid = tid
	local uid_txt = "?"
	if entry ~= nil and entry.uid_text ~= nil then uid_txt = tostring(entry.uid_text) end
	R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. "/" .. tostring(R6.max_pass) .. " candidate: " .. R6.cand_desc(kind)
		.. " for unit " .. uid_txt .. " | source=" .. tostring(src) .. " | -> " .. R6.target_name
		.. ":SetContextObject (value type=" .. lua_type(obj) .. ") [THE ONE WRITE OF THIS PASS]")
	r6.sets = r6.sets + 1
	local ok, err = r7_skip_write("R6 pass " .. tostring(k) .. " write to " .. R6.target_name)
	if ok then
		r6.write_ok = true
		R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " write accepted (no Lua error)")
	else
		r6.write_ok = false
		r6.write_err_text = truncate(err, 160)
		R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " write not performed: " .. r6.write_err_text)
	end
	r6.phase = "check"
	r6.next_at = tick_count + R6.settle
end

function R6.check()
	local k = r6.pass
	local bits = R6.panel_bits()
	local changed = nil
	if bits ~= nil and r6.before_sig ~= nil then
		changed = (bits.sig ~= r6.before_sig)
	end
	if bits ~= nil then
		R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " AFTER: values=" .. r5_sig_text(bits.sig)
			.. " changed=" .. tostring(changed == true))
		R6.diag("AFTER dynamic_stats", bits.ds)
		R6.diag("AFTER unit_information", bits.root)
		R6.diag("AFTER dy_value 1", bits.dy1)
	else
		R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " AFTER: the panel could not be re-read")
	end
	local landed, which = false, "nil"
	if bits ~= nil and bits.ds ~= nil then
		landed, which = R6.landed_check(bits)
	end
	local verdict = nil
	if r6.write_ok == false then
		verdict = "write REJECTED: " .. tostring(r6.write_err_text)
	elseif landed then
		verdict = "write accepted and LANDED (GetContextObjectId(" .. tostring(which)
			.. ") is truthy on " .. R6.target_name .. ")"
	else
		verdict = "write accepted but NOT landed (GetContextObjectId is still nil on "
			.. R6.target_name .. ")"
	end
	R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. "/" .. tostring(R6.max_pass) .. " verdict: " .. verdict
		.. " | values changed=" .. tostring(changed == true))
	if k == 1 then
		if r6.write_ok == true and landed and changed == false then
			R6.out("pass 1 CONTROL: mechanism CONFIRMED - the write landed and the SAME numbers"
				.. " still render. NEXT: zz_probe_r6_next() for pass 2 (the non-selected unit's cco)")
		elseif r6.write_ok == true and not landed then
			R6.out("pass 1 CONTROL: accepted but NOT landed - the mechanism is WRONG; STOP"
				.. " (do not advance). Check the diag lines; the panel root unit_information"
				.. " carries the CcoUnitDetails ContextPropagator (layout ~11050)")
		elseif r6.write_ok == false then
			R6.out("pass 1 CONTROL: REJECTED - read the error text; no further pass should run"
				.. " until the object is right")
		elseif changed == true then
			R6.out("pass 1 CONTROL: the rendered values CHANGED - inspect the AFTER block before advancing")
		end
	elseif k == 2 and changed == true then
		R6.out("pass 2: *** THE PANEL RE-RENDERED ANOTHER UNIT'S NUMBERS *** - the cross-unit"
			.. " mechanism WORKS; see the AFTER values")
	end
	r6.phase = "finish"
	r6.next_at = tick_count
end

function R6.finish()
	local k = r6.pass
	if r6.last == "no-panel" or r6.last == "no-unit" or r6.last == "no-obj" then
		R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " ended with NO write (" .. tostring(r6.last)
			.. "). NEXT: zz_probe_r6_next() to arm pass "
			.. tostring(math.min(k + 1, R6.max_pass)) .. ", or stop")
	elseif k < R6.max_pass and r6.sets < R6.max_sets then
		R6.out("pass " .. tostring(k) .. " complete (" .. tostring(r6.sets) .. "/"
			.. tostring(R6.max_sets) .. " write(s) used). NEXT: zz_probe_r6_next() for pass "
			.. tostring(k + 1) .. " (" .. R6.pass_name(k + 1)
			.. "); STOP instead if the verdict above says the mechanism is wrong")
	else
		R6.out("R6 ladder complete: " .. tostring(r6.sets) .. " of " .. tostring(R6.max_sets)
			.. " write(s) used - no further passes; the log holds the full ladder")
	end
	if k >= R6.max_pass or r6.sets >= R6.max_sets then
		r6.done = true
	end
	r6.active = false
	r6.phase = "idle"
	r6.target = nil
	r6.root = nil
end

function R6.step()
	local fn = R6[r6.phase]
	if fn ~= nil then fn() end
end

function zz_probe_r6()
	if r6.sets == 0 and r6.next_pass == 1 and not r6.active then
		return R6.hook_arm(1, "manual", "pass 1 (single attempt)")
	end
	return zz_probe_r6_next()
end

function zz_probe_r6_next(k)
	local target = nil
	if k == nil then
		target = r6.next_pass
	else
		target = tonumber(k)
	end
	if target == nil then
		return PROBE_TAG .. "r6: supply a pass index 1.." .. tostring(R6.max_pass)
	end
	return R6.hook_arm(target, "manual", "pass " .. tostring(target) .. " (single attempt)")
end

function zz_probe_r6_status()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "r6 active=" .. tostring(r6.active) .. " phase=" .. tostring(r6.phase)
		.. " armed_pass=" .. tostring(r6.armed_pass) .. " next_pass=" .. tostring(r6.next_pass)
		.. " sets=" .. tostring(r6.sets) .. "/" .. tostring(R6.max_sets)
		.. " auto=" .. tostring(r6.auto_done) .. " done=" .. tostring(r6.done)
		.. " panel_seen=" .. tostring(r6.sig_now ~= nil and contains_str(r6.sig_now, R6.target_name))
		.. " | manual: zz_probe_r6() / zz_probe_r6_next() | log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r6_help()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R6 ONE-WRITE-PER-PASS CONTEXT LADDER: select one unit, open AND PIN"
		.. " the unit-details panel. Pass 1 (auto-runs ONCE when the panel first shows): the"
		.. " selected unit's own cco -> dynamic_stats (CONTROL). Pass 2 zz_probe_r6_next():"
		.. " the non-selected unit's cco. Pass 3 zz_probe_r6_next() again: the raw battle_unit"
		.. " userdata. ONE SetContextObject per pass; the probe STOPS after every pass - read"
		.. " the verdict in the log, then advance or stop. The cco() build re-checks the global"
		.. " at use time, then core.cco / core:cco, then a live GetContextObject read off the"
		.. " panel chain. Real type ids: CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit."
		.. " Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

-- ============================================================================
-- 12. ROUND 7 - ZERO-WRITE READ EXPERIMENT (the NON-selected unit's stats)
--     C1 - the layouts' exact binding fields (grepped from the shipped XML):
--       "ui/battle ui/special_unit_tooltip.twui.xml" (the card tooltip) binds
--       context_object_id="CcoBattleUnit" with context_function_id:
--         BarrierHpPercent, BarrierHp, BarrierCapPercent, MoraleState,
--         ActiveEffectList(true).Size, IsBuffedByHarmony
--       "ui/common ui/unit_information.twui.xml" (the stat panel) binds
--         CcoUnitDetails.{Name, Description, HitPoints, BarrierHp, NumEntities,
--         NumEntitiesInitial, KillCount, ExperienceLevel, UpkeepCost, ...},
--         CcoUnitStat.{DisplayedValue, Name.RemoveTextTags, Tooltip,
--         ComparisonValue, ComparisonStatContext} (rows cloned from the
--         template_stat), and the hover COMPARISON rows are "label_compare"
--         components rendered from
--           CcoUnitStat: ContextVisibilitySetter "ComparisonStatContext && ComparisonValue != Value"
--                        ContextTextLabel      "Format(\"%+d\", RoundFloat(Value - ComparisonValue))"
--                        ContextStateSetter    "GetIfElse(Value > ComparisonValue, \"positive\", \"negative\")"
--         plus the panel-level delta "Format(\"%+d\", RoundFloat(this.HitPoints - ComparisonContext.HitPoints))".
--         The stat-value field names the probe reads through batte_team's proven
--         CcoBattleUnit surface: Name, HealthValue, HealthMax, HealthPercent,
--         BarrierHp, BarrierMaxHp, BarrierHpPercent, BarrierCapPercent,
--         BarrierReplenishRate, BarrierSecsUntilRecharge, MoralePercent,
--         MoraleState, NumEntities, NumEntitiesInitial, FatigueName,
--         ExperiencePercent, ExperienceLevel, CharacterRank, IsSelected,
--         IsPlayerUnit, AbilityList.Size, ActiveEffectList(true).Size,
--         SecondsLeftToTeleport.
--     C2 - the read: for BOTH cards (selected + non-selected), every field is
--       read through the vanilla-proven call
--         common.get_context_value("CcoBattleUnit", <ui id>, <field>)
--       (exactly the shape wh3_battle_prologue_values.lua uses:
--        common.get_context_value("CcoBattleUnit", CCOBattleUnitObjectId,
--        "AbilityList.Size")). The <ui id> is the card's own
--       GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit") answer - proven working in battle
--       for BOTH cards in round 6 ("1001" / "1002").
--     C3 - the hover comparison: while a unit is selected and the user hovers
--       another card, the panel's label_compare rows render the deltas the
--       user saw; the probe reads their GetStateText/CurrentState/Visible
--       (change-only) and probes GetContextObjectId on them (read-only).
--     C4 - the cards' own context ids are logged for every card read.
--     ZERO WRITES: nothing in this section (and, after round 7, nothing in
--     this file) calls SetContextObject / select_in_ui / SimulateMouseOn.
--     Every read is pcall-walled; a failing field is logged ONCE by name.
-- ============================================================================

local R7 = {
	every = 10,                -- sweep cadence in ticks (~2.5 s at 250 ms)
	fields = {
		"Name", "HealthValue", "HealthMax", "HealthPercent",
		"BarrierHp", "BarrierMaxHp", "BarrierHpPercent", "BarrierCapPercent",
		"BarrierReplenishRate", "BarrierSecsUntilRecharge",
		"MoralePercent", "MoraleState", "NumEntities", "NumEntitiesInitial",
		"FatigueName", "ExperiencePercent", "ExperienceLevel", "CharacterRank",
		"IsSelected", "IsPlayerUnit",
		"AbilityList.Size", "ActiveEffectList(true).Size", "SecondsLeftToTeleport",
	},
	compare_fields = { "Value", "ValueBase", "ComparisonValue", "DisplayedValue" },
	compare_cap = 12,          -- label_compare rows read per sweep
	ctx_types = { "CcoUnitStat", "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoBattleUnit" },
	max_lines = 900,           -- HARD CAP on R7 log lines per session
}

local r7 = {
	last = {},                 -- key -> last logged text (change-only logging)
	lines = 0,
	sweeps = 0,
	card_reads = 0,
	gcv_calls = 0,
	line_cap_spoken = false,
	field_err = {},            -- "Type.field" -> true once its error was logged
	stat_ctx_id = nil,         -- a CcoUnitStat object id, if a compare read yields one
	ctx_probe_done = false,    -- the once-per-session compare-context probe ran
}

local function r7_out(msg)
	if r7.lines >= R7.max_lines then
		if not r7.line_cap_spoken then
			r7.line_cap_spoken = true
			log("R7 line cap reached (" .. tostring(R7.max_lines) .. ") - further R7 values are not logged")
		end
		return
	end
	r7.lines = r7.lines + 1
	log("R7 " .. tostring(msg))
end

-- Change-only value logging, keyed by the caller's string.
local function r7_note(key, text)
	if r7.last[key] == text then return end
	local prev = r7.last[key]
	r7.last[key] = text
	if prev == nil then
		r7_out("NEW  " .. key .. " = " .. text)
	else
		r7_out("CHG  " .. key .. " = " .. text .. "  (was " .. tostring(prev) .. ")")
	end
end

-- ONE common.get_context_value read, pcall'd; the error text is logged ONCE
-- per (type, field) - never per call.
local function r7_gcv(obj_type, obj_id, field)
	r7.gcv_calls = r7.gcv_calls + 1
	local ok, v = pcall(function() return common.get_context_value(obj_type, obj_id, field) end)
	if not ok then
		local k = obj_type .. "." .. field
		if not r7.field_err[k] then
			r7.field_err[k] = true
			r7_out("ERR  " .. k .. " -> " .. truncate(tostring(v), 120))
		end
		return nil, true
	end
	return v, false
end

-- ONE card: its CcoBattleUnit context id (the proven read) + every field value
-- through common.get_context_value. The id is re-read every sweep (cheap) and
-- logged change-only.
local function r7_card_read(card, label)
	if card == nil or card.uic == nil then return end
	r7.card_reads = r7.card_reads + 1
	local id_ok, id_raw = pcall(function() return card.uic:GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit") end)
	local ctx_id = nil
	if id_ok then ctx_id = safe_text(id_raw) end
	r7_note(label .. " card: GetContextObjectId(CcoBattleUnit)",
		(id_ok and q(ctx_id) or "<ERR>") .. " state=" .. q(card.state)
		.. " vis=" .. tostring(card.vis))

	if ctx_id == nil or ctx_id == "" then
		r7_note(label .. " fields", "(no CcoBattleUnit id - field reads skipped)")
		return
	end
	for i = 1, #R7.fields do
		local field = R7.fields[i]
		local v, err = r7_gcv("CcoBattleUnit", ctx_id, field)
		if not err then
			local text = text_of(v, true)
			if text == nil then text = "<nil>" end
			r7_note(label .. " " .. field, q(text))
		end
	end
end

-- THE HOVER COMPARISON: the rendered label_compare rows (the deltas the user
-- saw) + a once-per-session read-only context probe on the first row.
local function r7_compare_read(parts)
	local compares = parts.compares
	local n = #compares
	if n > R7.compare_cap then n = R7.compare_cap end
	for i = 1, n do
		local c = compares[i]
		local sig = q(c.stext) .. "|" .. q(c.state) .. "|" .. tostring(c.vis)
		local key = "compare#" .. tostring(i)
		if r7.last[key] ~= sig then
			local prev = r7.last[key]
			r7.last[key] = sig
			r7_out((prev == nil and "NEW  " or "CHG  ") .. key
				.. " stext=" .. q(c.stext) .. " state=" .. q(c.state)
				.. " vis=" .. tostring(c.vis)
				.. (prev ~= nil and ("  (was " .. tostring(prev) .. ")") or ""))
		end
	end
	if (not r7.ctx_probe_done) and n >= 1 then
		r7.ctx_probe_done = true
		local c = compares[1]
		for t = 1, #R7.ctx_types do
			local type_id = R7.ctx_types[t]
			local ok_id, id_raw = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObjectId(type_id) end)
			local id_text = nil
			if ok_id then id_text = safe_text(id_raw) end
			r7_out("compare#1 GetContextObjectId(" .. q(type_id) .. ") = "
				.. (ok_id and q(id_text) or "<ERR>"))
			local ok_obj, obj_raw = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObject(type_id) end)
			r7_out("compare#1 GetContextObject(" .. q(type_id) .. ") -> type="
				.. (ok_obj and lua_type(obj_raw) or "<ERR>"))
			if type_id == "CcoUnitStat" and id_text ~= nil and id_text ~= "" then
				r7.stat_ctx_id = id_text
			end
		end
		if r7.stat_ctx_id ~= nil then
			for f = 1, #R7.compare_fields do
				local field = R7.compare_fields[f]
				local v, err = r7_gcv("CcoUnitStat", r7.stat_ctx_id, field)
				if not err then
					local text = text_of(v, true)
					if text == nil then text = "<nil>" end
					r7_note("CcoUnitStat." .. field, q(text))
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

-- THE SWEEP (the tick calls this; the console hook calls it directly).
local function r7_tick_sweep()
	local panel_visible = (r5.sig_now ~= nil and contains_str(r5.sig_now, "dynamic_stats"))
	if (not panel_visible) and (not window_active) then return end
	r7.sweeps = r7.sweeps + 1

	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel_card, nonsel_card = nil, nil
	for i = 1, #cards do
		local c = cards[i]
		if c.vis == "true" and c.state ~= nil
			and string.sub(c.state, 1, 8) == "selected" then
			if sel_card == nil then sel_card = c end
		elseif nonsel_card == nil then
			nonsel_card = c
		end
	end
	if sel_card ~= nil then r7_card_read(sel_card, "sel") end
	if nonsel_card ~= nil then r7_card_read(nonsel_card, "nonsel") end
	if window_active and window_hover_id ~= nil then
		for i = 1, #cards do
			if tostring(cards[i].id) == tostring(window_hover_id) then
				r7_card_read(cards[i], "hover")
				break
			end
		end
	end

	if panel_visible then
		local ok_parts, parts = pcall(r5_panel_parts)
		if ok_parts and parts ~= nil and parts.compares ~= nil then
			r7_compare_read(parts)
		end
	end
end

function zz_probe_r7()
	local ok, res = pcall(r7_tick_sweep)
	if not ok then
		return PROBE_TAG .. "R7 sweep error (swallowed): " .. truncate(res, 140)
	end
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R7 sweep done (sweeps=" .. tostring(r7.sweeps)
		.. " card reads=" .. tostring(r7.card_reads)
		.. " get_context_value calls=" .. tostring(r7.gcv_calls) .. "). Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r7_status()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R7 zero-write read experiment: sweeps=" .. tostring(r7.sweeps)
		.. " card reads=" .. tostring(r7.card_reads)
		.. " get_context_value calls=" .. tostring(r7.gcv_calls)
		.. " lines=" .. tostring(r7.lines) .. "/" .. tostring(R7.max_lines)
		.. " | fields per card=" .. tostring(#R7.fields)
		.. " | stat ctx id=" .. q(r7.stat_ctx_id)
		.. " | log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r7_help()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R7 ZERO-WRITE READS: click one unit, open AND PIN the "
		.. "unit-details panel, then hover the OTHER unit's card for a few seconds. "
		.. "Every ~2.5 s (and during hover captures) the probe reads both cards' "
		.. "CcoBattleUnit contexts with common.get_context_value ("
		.. tostring(#R7.fields) .. " fields) and the panel's compared rows "
		.. "(label_compare) - change-only, no writes. Manual: zz_probe_r7(); "
		.. "status: zz_probe_r7_status(). Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end
-- ============================================================================
-- 13. ROUND 8 - THE DECISIVE EXPERIMENT: the UNIT-CARD STAT NUMBERS of a
--     NON-SELECTED unit, procedurally, invisibly.
--
--     THE QUESTION. The stat panel's rows are readable text for the SELECTED
--     unit (rounds 4-7, PROVEN). The comparison fields (CcoUnitStat.
--     ComparisonValue / CcoUnitDetails.ComparisonContext / the label_compare
--     delta text) are rendered from the OTHER unit only while a card is
--     hovered. Round 8 asks: can the mod obtain a NON-selected unit's real stat
--     numbers procedurally - no player hover, no gameplay interruption - by
--     SIMULATING the hover itself and reading the comparison fields while they
--     live?
--
--     THE FOUR PARTS (each its own labelled block; grep 'R8 TRUTH',
--     'R8 SIMHOVER', 'R8 DESELECT-TEST'):
--       PART 1 GROUND TRUTH - the user clicks each unit once (PROVEN-SAFE
--         reading); each new selected unit's row table is logged as
--         'R8 TRUTH <id> <stat>=<value> ...' - the comparison baseline.
--       PART 2 SIMULATED-HOVER LADDER - for every NON-selected card, and for
--         the hold durations 50 / 150 / 300 / 1500 ms: SimulateMouseOn (logged
--         BEFORE the call), a poll every 50 ms of the panel's row values + the
--         label_compare rows + the compare context fields (READ ONLY), then
--         SimulateMouseOff at the end of the hold (EVERY On is paired with an
--         Off), then a 2 s persistence watch, then one verdict line
--         'R8 SIMHOVER card=<id> hold=<ms> comparison_seen=.. panel_changed=..
--          persisted_ms=<n> delta_text=..'. The whole ladder runs with the
--         player's hands OFF the mouse.
--       PART 3 INVISIBILITY (offline; the shipped layouts were read) -
--         ui/common ui/panel_sticky_tooltips.twui.xml: default_appear_val =
--           0.25 s (the DEFAULT tooltip APPEAR delay - nothing is drawn for
--           the first 250 ms of a hover), default_stick_val 0.9 s,
--           default_removal_val 0.15 s;
--         ui/battle ui/special_unit_tooltip.twui.xml: expand_delay_ms = 2500
--           (the unit-card tooltip does not EXPAND for 2.5 s);
--         ui/common ui/tooltip_default.twui.xml: expand_delay = 0.8 s.
--         So a simulated hover shorter than R8.visible_ms (250 ms) cannot draw
--         anything: the 50 ms and 150 ms passes are labelled invisible=yes; the
--         300 ms and 1500 ms passes cross the appear delay and may show a
--         minimised tooltip briefly (1500 ms is still short of the 2500 ms
--         expand).
--       PART 4 THE FAKE-SELECTION ROUTE (R8 DESELECT-TEST) - ONCE, and ONLY
--         when armed by hand (zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test()): call
--         battle_unit:select_in_ui() on ONE non-selected unit, log the cards'
--         states and the panel's values before/after, and whether the selection
--         appears restored. DISARMED by default; the user reports what they SAW.
--
--     SAFETY. ZERO SetContextObject calls anywhere. The ONLY writes in round 8
--     are the SimulateMouseOn/Off pair in the SIMHOVER block, each logged BEFORE
--     the call and each On tracked so an Off ALWAYS follows (r8.owed; a stuck
--     hover is reported loudly). select_in_ui is a single hand-armed pass.
--     Every engine read is pcall-walled; every walk is depth/visit capped.
--
--     DRIVING. The ladder lives in its OWN 50 ms callback (zz_probe_r8_poll) so
--     the 50 ms hold is honoured; the truth capture is throttled inside it. The
--     truth phase runs while the panel is visible; once >= R8.min_truth units
--     are recorded and no new click has arrived for R8.truth_settle_ticks, the
--     ladder auto-starts. zz_probe_r8() starts it immediately.
--
--     HOOKS: zz_probe_r8() / zz_probe_r8_status() /
--            zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test() / zz_probe_r8_help()
-- ============================================================================

local R8_POLL_NAME = "zz_probe_r8_poll"

local R8 = {
	poll_ms = 50,               -- the ladder's own poll cadence
	truth_every = 10,           -- truth capture every N r8 ticks (~500 ms)
	truth_settle_ticks = 120,   -- 6 s without a new click -> auto-start the ladder
	min_truth = 2,              -- at least this many units clicked before the ladder
	holds = { 50, 150, 300, 1500 },  -- the SIMULATED-HOVER LADDER (ms)
	persist_ms = 2000,          -- how long after MouseOff we keep watching (ms)
	visible_ms = 250,           -- default tooltip APPEAR delay (layouts); a hold
	                            -- shorter than this is labelled invisible=yes
	snap_visits = 220,          -- the ladder snapshot's visit cap
	snap_depth = 12,
	max_passes = 48,            -- HARD CAP hover passes per session
	max_sim = 48,               -- HARD CAP SimulateMouseOn (each paired with an Off)
	truth_cap = 30,             -- HARD CAP distinct truth entries
	max_lines = 1600,           -- HARD CAP R8 log lines
	gate_every = 20,            -- log the R8 GATE line every N r8 ticks (~1 s)
	gate_visits = 400,          -- the gate probe's own bounded walk (cheap)
	gate_depth = 16,            -- the gate probe's depth cap
	gate_max_lines = 4000,      -- HARD CAP on the ~1 Hz GATE lines (own budget)
	ctx_types = { "CcoUnitStat", "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoBattleUnit" },
	compare_fields = { "Value", "ValueBase", "DisplayedValue", "ComparisonValue" },
	details_fields = { "ComparisonContext", "ComparisonValue", "HitPoints" },
}

local r8 = {
	tick = 0,
	lines = 0, line_cap_spoken = false,
	phase = "idle",             -- idle | truth | ladder | done
	truth = {}, truth_count = 0,
	truth_order = {},
	truth_last_key = nil,
	truth_last_new = 0,
	ladder_started = false,
	queue = {}, queue_i = 0, hold_i = 0,
	pass = nil, passes_done = 0, pass_rows = {},
	sim_on = 0, sim_off = 0,
	owed = nil,                 -- a component that still owes a SimulateMouseOff
	select_armed = false, select_done = false,
	sim_armed = false, sim_wait_spoken = false,   -- ROUND 9: simhover DISARMED by default
	select_after_at = nil, select_after_unit = nil,
	select_base_sig = nil, select_sel_before = nil,
	panel_seen = false,
	done = false,
	-- ROUND 8 GATE OBSERVABILITY (this build): the ~1 Hz gate-line cache +
	-- the force-path bookkeeping. gate_open is set the first time either the
	-- stat panel shows rows OR a unit is selected with the cards panel up.
	gate_open = false, gate_fired = "none", selection_gate = false,
	gate_seen = false, gate_rows = 0, gate_names = "", gate_sel = "none",
	gate_tab = nil, gate_lines = 0, gate_cap_spoken = false,
	force_pending = false, force_calls = 0,
}

local function r8_out(msg)
	if r8.lines >= R8.max_lines then
		if not r8.line_cap_spoken then
			r8.line_cap_spoken = true
			log("R8 line cap reached (" .. tostring(R8.max_lines) .. ") - further R8 lines are not logged")
		end
		return
	end
	r8.lines = r8.lines + 1
	log("R8 " .. tostring(msg))
end

-- ONE get_context_value read, pcall'd (READ ONLY).
local function r8_gcv(type_id, obj_id, field)
	local ok, v = pcall(function() return common.get_context_value(type_id, obj_id, field) end)
	if not ok then return nil, false end
	return v, true
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13a0. ROUND 8 GATE OBSERVABILITY (this build). The auto-gate used to be
--       SILENT when it was closed, so a battle that never triggered could not
--       say WHY. Now, about once a second (and on a forced run), ONE cheap line
--       is logged even when the gate is closed:
--         R8 GATE panel_seen=<yes/no> stat_rows=<n> stat_names=[..]
--                 selected_card=<id|none> ladder_state=<idle/armed/running/done>
--                 fired=<panel|selection|none> [tab={..} when no rows]
--       The gate OPENS when EITHER the stat panel shows rows OR a unit is
--       selected while the cards panel is up; the line names WHICH fired. When
--       no stat rows are found the panel's TAB STATE is logged too
--       (row_header_stats / row_header_abilities state + their dy_title texts +
--       abilities_listview visibility), so 'the Stats tab is not selected' is
--       tellable apart from 'the panel is not open'.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The ~1 Hz gate lines have their OWN budget so they cannot exhaust the R8
-- value-line cap (max_lines), which bounds the truth/simhover output.
local function r8_gate_out(msg)
	if r8.gate_lines >= R8.gate_max_lines then
		if not r8.gate_cap_spoken then
			r8.gate_cap_spoken = true
			log("R8 GATE line cap reached (" .. tostring(R8.gate_max_lines) .. ")")
		end
		return
	end
	r8.gate_lines = r8.gate_lines + 1
	log("R8 " .. tostring(msg))
end

local function r8_ladder_state()
	if r8.done then return "done" end
	if r8.pass ~= nil or r8.ladder_started then return "running" end
	if r8.force_pending then return "armed" end
	return "idle"
end

-- Read one named component's CurrentState + (its first child's, then its own)
-- GetStateText - the tab-header shape (row_header_stats -> dy_title).
local function r8_named_state_text(uic)
	if uic == nil then return "NOT FOUND" end
	local st = r5_read_text(function() return uic:CurrentState() end)
	local title = nil
	local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
	if lua_type(n) == "number" and n > 0 then
		local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(0) end)
		if ok_c and child ~= nil then
			local ch = wrap(child)
			title = r5_read_text(function() return ch:GetStateText() end)
		end
	end
	if title == nil then
		title = r5_read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
	end
	return "state=" .. q(st) .. " title=" .. q(title)
end

-- The panel's TAB STATE (from the handles the gate walk collected): tells
-- 'Stats tab not selected' apart from 'the panel is not open'.
local function r8_tab_state_text(g)
	local parts = {}
	parts[#parts + 1] = "row_header_stats(" .. r8_named_state_text(g.rh_stats) .. ")"
	parts[#parts + 1] = "row_header_abilities(" .. r8_named_state_text(g.rh_abil) .. ")"
	if g.abil_lv ~= nil then
		parts[#parts + 1] = "abilities_listview.vis="
			.. tostring(readb(function() return g.abil_lv:Visible() end))
	else
		parts[#parts + 1] = "abilities_listview=NOT FOUND"
	end
	parts[#parts + 1] = "unit_information=" .. (g.unit_info ~= nil and "found" or "NOT FOUND")
	return table.concat(parts, " ")
end

-- ONE bounded probe: does dynamic_stats exist, how many stat rows, which stat
-- names, which card is selected, and (always) the panel's tab state. It walks
-- hud_battle ONCE (<= gate_visits visits) and reads the cards once.
local function r8_gate_probe()
	local out = { panel = nil, rows = 0, names = "", sel = "none", fired = "none" }

	-- the selected card (reuse the proven card reader). #cards > 0 means the
	-- cards panel is up.
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	out.has_cards = (#cards > 0)
	if out.has_cards then
		local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
		for i = 1, #cards do
			local c = cards[i]
			if c.vis == "true" and c.id ~= nil and sel[c.id] == true then
				out.sel = c.id
				break
			end
		end
	end

	-- one bounded walk of hud_battle: dynamic_stats, its stat_name texts, and
	-- the panel's tab-state components (Id() per visit + the few interesting
	-- reads only).
	local hud = find_by_name(DEFAULT_ROOT)
	if hud == nil then
		out.tab = "hud_battle not found"
		return out
	end
	local names = {}
	local rh_stats, rh_abil, abil_lv, unit_info = nil, nil, nil, nil
	local visits = { [1] = 0 }
	local function visit(uic, depth)
		if uic == nil or visits[1] >= R8.gate_visits then return end
		visits[1] = visits[1] + 1
		local id = r5_read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
		if id == "dynamic_stats" then
			if out.panel == nil then out.panel = uic end
		elseif id == "stat_name" then
			if #names < 40 then
				local st = r5_read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
				if st ~= nil and st ~= "" then names[#names + 1] = st end
			end
		elseif id == "row_header_stats" then rh_stats = uic
		elseif id == "row_header_abilities" then rh_abil = uic
		elseif id == "abilities_listview" then abil_lv = uic
		elseif id == "unit_information" then unit_info = uic
		end
		if depth >= R8.gate_depth then return end
		local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
		if lua_type(n) == "number" and n > 0 then
			for i = 0, n - 1 do
				if visits[1] >= R8.gate_visits then return end
				local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
				if ok_c and child ~= nil then
					pcall(visit, wrap(child), depth + 1)
				end
			end
		end
	end
	pcall(visit, hud, 0)
	out.rh_stats, out.rh_abil, out.abil_lv, out.unit_info = rh_stats, rh_abil, abil_lv, unit_info
	out.rows = #names
	out.names = table.concat(names, ",")
	if out.rows > 0 then
		out.fired = "panel"
	elseif out.has_cards and out.sel ~= "none" then
		out.fired = "selection"
	end
	if out.rows == 0 then
		out.tab = r8_tab_state_text(out)
	end
	return out
end

-- Log the gate line (~1 Hz and on a forced run). Opens the gate on the first
-- firing condition and names it. Returns the firing condition string.
local function r8_log_gate()
	local g = r8_gate_probe()
	r8.gate_seen = (g.panel ~= nil)
	r8.gate_rows = g.rows
	r8.gate_names = g.names
	r8.gate_sel = g.sel
	r8.gate_fired = g.fired
	r8.gate_tab = g.tab
	if g.rows > 0 then r8.panel_seen = true end

	-- OPEN the gate (once) on EITHER condition.
	if r8.phase == "idle" and g.fired ~= "none" then
		r8.phase = "truth"
		if g.fired == "selection" then r8.selection_gate = true end
		if not r8.gate_open then
			r8.gate_open = true
			r8_out("GATE OPENED by " .. tostring(g.fired) .. ": "
				.. (g.fired == "panel"
					and ("the stat panel shows rows (" .. tostring(g.rows) .. ")")
					or ("a unit (" .. tostring(g.sel)
						.. ") is selected and the cards panel is up")))
		end
	end

	local line = "GATE panel_seen=" .. (g.panel ~= nil and "yes" or "no")
		.. " stat_rows=" .. tostring(g.rows)
		.. " stat_names=[" .. tostring(g.names) .. "]"
		.. " selected_card=" .. tostring(g.sel)
		.. " ladder_state=" .. r8_ladder_state()
		.. " fired=" .. tostring(g.fired)
	if g.rows == 0 then
		line = line .. " tab={" .. tostring(g.tab) .. "}"
	end
	r8_gate_out(line)
	return g.fired
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13a. THE PANEL SNAPSHOT (the ladder's light reader): the stat rows
--      (stat_name -> dy_value), the label_compare rows (the delta text) and the
--      panel's visibility. Every read pcall-walled; depth/visit capped.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function r8_snapshot()
	local ds = find_by_id_under_hud("dynamic_stats")
	if ds == nil then return nil end
	local vis = readb(function() return ds:Visible() end)
	local vfr = readb(function() return ds:VisibleFromRoot() end)
	local rows, compares = {}, {}
	local cur = nil
	local visits = { [1] = 0 }
	local function visit(uic, depth)
		if uic == nil or visits[1] >= R8.snap_visits then return end
		visits[1] = visits[1] + 1
		local id = r5_read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
		if id == "template_stat" then
			if #rows < 60 then
				cur = { uic = uic, name = nil, value = nil }
				rows[#rows + 1] = cur
			else
				cur = nil
			end
		elseif id == "stat_name" and cur ~= nil and cur.name == nil then
			cur.name = r5_read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
		elseif id == "dy_value" then
			local st = r5_read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
			if cur ~= nil and cur.value == nil then cur.value = st end
		elseif id == "label_compare" then
			if #compares < 24 then
				compares[#compares + 1] = {
					uic = uic,
					stext = r5_read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end),
					state = r5_read_text(function() return uic:CurrentState() end),
					vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end),
				}
			end
		end
		if depth >= R8.snap_depth then return end
		local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
		if lua_type(n) == "number" and n > 0 then
			for i = 0, n - 1 do
				if visits[1] >= R8.snap_visits then return end
				local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
				if ok_c and child ~= nil then
					pcall(visit, wrap(child), depth + 1)
				end
			end
		end
	end
	pcall(visit, ds, 0)
	local parts = {}
	for i = 1, #rows do
		local rn = rows[i].name or ""
		local rv = rows[i].value or ""
		if rn ~= "" or rv ~= "" then parts[#parts + 1] = rn .. "=" .. rv end
	end
	local sig = table.concat(parts, "|")
	local cparts = {}
	local compare_vis = false
	local delta_text = nil
	for i = 1, #compares do
		local c = compares[i]
		cparts[#cparts + 1] = tostring(c.stext) .. "/" .. tostring(c.vis)
		if c.vis == "true" and c.stext ~= nil and c.stext ~= "" then
			compare_vis = true
			if delta_text == nil then delta_text = c.stext end
		end
	end
	return { ds = ds, vis = vis, vfr = vfr, rows = rows, compares = compares,
		sig = sig, compare_sig = table.concat(cparts, "|"),
		compare_vis = compare_vis, delta_text = delta_text }
end

-- READ-ONLY probe of the compare rows' context objects. A CcoUnitStat /
-- CcoUnitDetails id surfaced here feeds get_context_value for the comparison
-- fields (ComparisonValue / ComparisonContext). Change-only per (row, type).
local function r8_compare_ctx_read(snap)
	if snap == nil or snap.compares == nil then return end
	for i = 1, #snap.compares do
		local c = snap.compares[i]
		for t = 1, #R8.ctx_types do
			local tid = R8.ctx_types[t]
			local ok_id, raw = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObjectId(tid) end)
			local id_text = nil
			if ok_id then id_text = safe_text(raw) end
			if id_text ~= nil and id_text ~= "" then
				local key = "rc:" .. tostring(i) .. ":" .. tid
				if r8.pass_rows[key] ~= id_text then
					r8.pass_rows[key] = id_text
					r8_out("SIMHOVER compare#" .. tostring(i) .. " GetContextObjectId("
						.. q(tid) .. ") = " .. q(id_text))
					if tid == "CcoUnitStat" then
						for f = 1, #R8.compare_fields do
							local field = R8.compare_fields[f]
							local v, okf = r8_gcv("CcoUnitStat", id_text, field)
							if okf then
								local tx = text_of(v, true)
								if tx == nil then tx = "<nil>" end
								r8_out("SIMHOVER compare#" .. tostring(i) .. " CcoUnitStat."
									.. field .. " = " .. q(tx))
							end
						end
						if i == 1 then
							local ok_o, o = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObject(tid) end)
							r8_out("SIMHOVER compare#1 GetContextObject(" .. q(tid) .. ") -> type="
								.. (ok_o and lua_type(o) or "<ERR>"))
						end
					elseif tid == "CcoUnitDetails" then
						for f = 1, #R8.details_fields do
							local field = R8.details_fields[f]
							local v, okf = r8_gcv("CcoUnitDetails", id_text, field)
							if okf then
								local tx = text_of(v, true)
								if tx == nil then tx = "<nil>" end
								r8_out("SIMHOVER compare#" .. tostring(i) .. " CcoUnitDetails."
									.. field .. " = " .. q(tx))
							end
						end
					end
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13b. THE SIMULATED HOVER (the ONLY writes in round 8; every On paired with Off)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function r8_sim_on(uic, card_id, hold)
	r8_out("SIMHOVER SimulateMouseOn card=" .. q(card_id) .. " hold=" .. tostring(hold)
		.. "ms (write " .. tostring(r8.sim_on + 1) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.max_sim)
		.. "; logged BEFORE the call)")
	r8.sim_on = r8.sim_on + 1
	local ok, err = pcall(function() return uic:SimulateMouseOn() end)
	if not ok then
		r8_out("SIMHOVER SimulateMouseOn error (swallowed): " .. truncate(err, 140))
		return false
	end
	return true
end

local function r8_sim_off(uic, card_id, why)
	r8_out("SIMHOVER SimulateMouseOff card=" .. q(card_id) .. " (" .. tostring(why)
		.. "; logged BEFORE the call)")
	r8.sim_off = r8.sim_off + 1
	local ok, err = pcall(function() return uic:SimulateMouseOff() end)
	if not ok then
		r8_out("SIMHOVER SimulateMouseOff error (swallowed): " .. truncate(err, 140))
		return false
	end
	return true
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13c. THE CARD QUEUE (the cards-panel components that answer a CcoBattleUnit
--      context id and are NOT in the selected set)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function r8_build_queue()
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
	local q = {}
	for i = 1, #cards do
		local c = cards[i]
		if c.uic ~= nil and c.vis == "true" then
			local ok_id, raw = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit") end)
			local ctx = nil
			if ok_id then ctx = safe_text(raw) end
			local is_sel = (c.id ~= nil and sel[c.id] == true)
			if ctx ~= nil and ctx ~= "" and not is_sel then
				q[#q + 1] = { id = c.id, ctx = ctx, uic = c.uic, state = c.state }
			end
		end
	end
	return q
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13d. PART 1 - GROUND TRUTH (the tone the probe reads as the user clicks)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function r8_capture_truth()
	local snap = r8_snapshot()
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
	local selcard = nil
	for i = 1, #cards do
		local c = cards[i]
		if c.vis == "true" and c.id ~= nil and sel[c.id] == true then selcard = c; break end
	end
	local id = nil
	if selcard ~= nil then
		local ok_id, raw = pcall(function() return selcard.uic:GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit") end)
		if ok_id then id = safe_text(raw) end
		if id == nil or id == "" then id = selcard.id end
	end

	-- NO STAT ROWS YET: log WHY once (the panel's tab state) instead of staying
	-- silent - this is what tells 'the Stats tab is not selected' apart from
	-- 'the panel is not open'.
	if snap == nil or snap.sig == "" then
		local key = "NOROWS|" .. tostring(id or "(no selected card)") .. "|"
			.. tostring(r8.gate_tab)
		if r8.truth_last_key ~= key then
			r8.truth_last_key = key
			local tab = r8.gate_tab
			if tab == nil then
				local g = r8_gate_probe()
				tab = g.tab
				r8.gate_tab = tab
			end
			r8_out("TRUTH " .. tostring(id or "(no selected card)")
				.. " (no stat rows visible) tab={" .. tostring(tab) .. "}")
		end
		return false
	end

	if selcard == nil then
		if not r8.panel_seen then
			r8.panel_seen = true
			r8_out("TRUTH: the stat panel is visible - click EACH unit in turn;"
				.. " the row table is logged per unit as 'R8 TRUTH <id> <stat>=<value> ...'")
		end
		return false
	end
	local key = tostring(id) .. "|" .. snap.sig
	if r8.truth_last_key == key then return false end
	r8.truth_last_key = key
	r8.truth_last_new = r8.tick
	if r8.truth[id] == nil and r8.truth_count < R8.truth_cap then
		r8.truth[id] = true
		r8.truth_order[#r8.truth_order + 1] = id
		r8.truth_count = r8.truth_count + 1
	end
	local parts = {}
	for i = 1, #snap.rows do
		local rn = snap.rows[i].name
		local rv = snap.rows[i].value
		if (rn ~= nil and rn ~= "") or (rv ~= nil and rv ~= "") then
			parts[#parts + 1] = tostring(rn or "?") .. "=" .. tostring(rv or "?")
		end
	end
	if #parts == 0 then
		r8_out("TRUTH " .. tostring(id) .. " (panel visible, no stat rows rendered yet)")
	else
		r8_out("TRUTH " .. tostring(id) .. " " .. table.concat(parts, " "))
	end
	return true
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13e. PART 2 - THE SIMULATED-HOVER LADDER (pass lifecycle)
--      finish -> begin is a small cycle, so the pass functions are forward
--      declared and assigned.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local r8_begin_next_pass, r8_finish_pass, r8_start_pass, r8_step_pass

local function r8_finish_ladder(why)
	if r8.owed ~= nil then
		r8_sim_off(r8.owed, "owed", "ladder cleanup")
		r8.owed = nil
	end
	r8.phase = "done"
	r8.done = true
	r8_out("LADDER done (" .. tostring(why) .. "): passes=" .. tostring(r8.passes_done)
		.. " sim_on=" .. tostring(r8.sim_on) .. " sim_off=" .. tostring(r8.sim_off)
		.. " truth_entries=" .. tostring(r8.truth_count))
	if r8.sim_on ~= r8.sim_off then
		r8_out("LADDER WARNING: SimulateMouseOn (" .. tostring(r8.sim_on)
			.. ") != SimulateMouseOff (" .. tostring(r8.sim_off) .. ") - a hover may be stuck")
	end
end

r8_start_pass = function(card, hold)
	local snap = r8_snapshot()          -- baseline BEFORE any write
	r8.pass_rows = {}
	local p = {
		card = card,
		hold = hold,
		hold_ticks = math.max(1, math.floor(hold / R8.poll_ms)),
		base_sig = (snap ~= nil) and snap.sig or nil,
		phase = "on",
		t_on = r8.tick, t_off = nil, last_compare_tick = nil,
		comparison_seen = false, panel_changed = false,
		delta_text = nil, on_ok = nil,
	}
	r8.pass = p
	r8_out("SIMHOVER start card=" .. q(card.id) .. " ctx=" .. q(card.ctx)
		.. " hold=" .. tostring(hold) .. "ms base_values=" .. r5_sig_text(p.base_sig))
	r8.phase = "ladder"
end

r8_begin_next_pass = function()
	if r8.passes_done >= R8.max_passes then
		r8_finish_ladder("pass cap " .. tostring(R8.max_passes))
		return
	end
	if r8.sim_on >= R8.max_sim then
		r8_finish_ladder("sim cap " .. tostring(R8.max_sim))
		return
	end
	local card = r8.queue[r8.queue_i]
	if card == nil then
		r8_finish_ladder("queue exhausted")
		return
	end
	local hold = R8.holds[r8.hold_i]
	if hold == nil then
		r8.queue_i = r8.queue_i + 1
		r8.hold_i = 1
		card = r8.queue[r8.queue_i]
		if card == nil then
			r8_finish_ladder("queue exhausted")
			return
		end
		hold = R8.holds[r8.hold_i]
	end
	r8_start_pass(card, hold)
end

r8_finish_pass = function()
	local p = r8.pass
	if p == nil then return end
	local persisted = 0
	if p.last_compare_tick ~= nil and p.t_off ~= nil and p.last_compare_tick > p.t_off then
		persisted = (p.last_compare_tick - p.t_off) * R8.poll_ms
	end
	local invisible = "no"
	if p.hold <= R8.visible_ms then invisible = "yes" end
	r8_out("SIMHOVER card=" .. q(p.card.id) .. " hold=" .. tostring(p.hold)
		.. " comparison_seen=" .. (p.comparison_seen and "yes" or "no")
		.. " panel_changed=" .. (p.panel_changed and "yes" or "no")
		.. " persisted_ms=" .. tostring(persisted)
		.. " delta_text=" .. q(p.delta_text or "")
		.. " invisible=" .. invisible
		.. " on_ok=" .. tostring(p.on_ok == true))
	r8.passes_done = r8.passes_done + 1
	r8.pass = nil
	r8.hold_i = r8.hold_i + 1
	r8_begin_next_pass()
end

r8_step_pass = function()
	local p = r8.pass
	if p == nil then return end
	if p.phase == "on" then
		p.on_ok = r8_sim_on(p.card.uic, p.card.id, p.hold)
		r8.owed = p.card.uic            -- this On now owes an Off
		p.t_on = r8.tick
		p.phase = "hold"
		return
	end
	local snap = r8_snapshot()
	if snap ~= nil then
		if p.base_sig ~= nil and snap.sig ~= p.base_sig then p.panel_changed = true end
		if snap.compare_vis then
			p.comparison_seen = true
			p.last_compare_tick = r8.tick
			if snap.delta_text ~= nil then p.delta_text = snap.delta_text end
		end
		if (r8.tick % 4) == 0 then pcall(r8_compare_ctx_read, snap) end
	end
	if p.phase == "hold" then
		if (r8.tick - p.t_on) >= p.hold_ticks then
			r8_sim_off(p.card.uic, p.card.id, "hold " .. tostring(p.hold) .. "ms ended")
			r8.owed = nil
			p.t_off = r8.tick
			p.phase = "persist"
		end
	elseif p.phase == "persist" then
		if (r8.tick - p.t_off) >= math.max(1, math.floor(R8.persist_ms / R8.poll_ms)) then
			r8_finish_pass()
		end
	end
end

local function r8_start_ladder(why, force)
	if r8.pass ~= nil then
		r8_out("LADDER start refused: a pass is already in flight")
		return false
	end
	local q = r8_build_queue()
	if #q == 0 and force then
		-- FORCE: accept ANY visible card (even the selected one), so the
		-- simulated-hover mechanism still gets exercised when the auto-gate
		-- never opened. The queue still prefers the non-selected cards.
		local cards = r5_read_cards()
		for i = 1, #cards do
			local c = cards[i]
			if c.uic ~= nil and c.vis == "true" then
				local ok_id, raw = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit") end)
				local ctx = nil
				if ok_id then ctx = safe_text(raw) end
				if ctx == nil or ctx == "" then ctx = c.id end
				q[#q + 1] = { id = c.id, ctx = ctx, uic = c.uic, state = c.state }
			end
		end
		if #q > 0 then
			r8_out("LADDER FORCE fallback: no NON-selected card was found; using "
				.. tostring(#q) .. " visible card(s) including the selected one")
		end
	end
	if #q == 0 then
		r8_out("LADDER start refused: no card found (cards_panel) - "
			.. (force
				and "even a FORCED run needs >=1 visible unit card; open the cards panel"
				or "select one unit and open the stat panel, then retry"))
		return false
	end
	r8.queue = q
	r8.queue_i = 1
	r8.hold_i = 1
	r8.ladder_started = true
	r8.phase = "ladder"
	r8_out("LADDER starting (" .. tostring(why) .. "): " .. tostring(#q)
		.. " non-selected card(s); holds " .. tostring(R8.holds[1]) .. "/"
		.. tostring(R8.holds[2]) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.holds[3]) .. "/"
		.. tostring(R8.holds[4]) .. " ms; tooltip appear delay "
		.. tostring(R8.visible_ms) .. " ms (holds below it are invisible=yes)")
	r8_begin_next_pass()
	return true
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13f. PART 4 - THE FAKE-SELECTION ROUTE (manual, single pass, default OFF)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local r8_select_after   -- forward

local function r8_run_select_test()
	r8.select_done = true
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST begin (manual single pass; the ONE select_in_ui write)")
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel_before = r5_selected_set(cards)
	r8.select_sel_before = sel_before
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST cards before: " .. r5_cards_text(cards))
	local snap_before = r8_snapshot()
	r8.select_base_sig = (snap_before ~= nil) and snap_before.sig or nil
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST panel values before: " .. r5_sig_text(r8.select_base_sig))
	local units = r5_read_units()
	local sel_su, sel_why, nonsel, nonsel_why = r5_pick_units(units, sel_before)
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST selected-unit guess: "
		.. (sel_su ~= nil and q(sel_su.uid_text) or "NONE"))
	if nonsel == nil or nonsel.unit == nil or nonsel.uid_text == nil then
		r8_out("DESELECT-TEST skipped: no non-selected unit handle could be read")
		r8_out("DESELECT-TEST end")
		return
	end
	r8.select_after_unit = nonsel.uid_text
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST calling battle_unit:select_in_ui() on unit " .. q(nonsel.uid_text)
		.. " (" .. tostring(nonsel_why) .. "; logged BEFORE the call)")
	local ok, err = pcall(function() return nonsel.unit:select_in_ui() end)
	if not ok then
		r8_out("DESELECT-TEST select_in_ui error (swallowed): " .. truncate(err, 140))
	else
		r8_out("DESELECT-TEST select_in_ui accepted (no Lua error)")
	end
	r8.select_after_at = r8.tick + math.max(1, math.floor(1000 / R8.poll_ms))
end

r8_select_after = function()
	r8.select_after_at = nil
	local cards = r5_read_cards()
	local sel_after = r5_selected_set(cards)
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST cards after: " .. r5_cards_text(cards))
	local changed = false
	for id in pairs(sel_after) do
		if not (r8.select_sel_before ~= nil and r8.select_sel_before[id] == true) then changed = true end
	end
	if r8.select_sel_before ~= nil then
		for id in pairs(r8.select_sel_before) do
			if not sel_after[id] then changed = true end
		end
	end
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST selection " .. (changed and "DID change" or "unchanged"))
	local snap_after = r8_snapshot()
	local now_sig = (snap_after ~= nil) and snap_after.sig or nil
	local pchg = (now_sig ~= r8.select_base_sig)
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST panel values after: " .. r5_sig_text(now_sig)
		.. " (changed=" .. tostring(pchg) .. ")")
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST restored=" .. tostring((not changed) and (not pchg))
		.. " - the user reports what they SAW on screen")
	r8_out("DESELECT-TEST end")
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 13g. THE 50 ms POLL (truth phase -> auto ladder -> manual select test) and
--      the console hooks.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
local function r8_poll()
	local ok, err = pcall(function()
		r8.tick = r8.tick + 1

		-- the deferred after-read of the select test
		if r8.select_after_at ~= nil and r8.tick >= r8.select_after_at then
			r8_select_after()
		end

		-- THE ~1 Hz GATE LINE (runs even when the gate is closed, so a battle
		-- that never triggers can say WHY). It also OPENS the gate on the
		-- selection condition and names whichever condition fired.
		if (r8.tick % R8.gate_every) == 0 or r8.force_pending then
			pcall(r8_log_gate)
		end

		-- a hover pass in flight always steps first (it owns the simulated mouse)
		if r8.pass ~= nil then
			r8_step_pass()
			return
		end

		-- the manual select test (single pass) - runs at the next idle moment once armed
		if r8.select_armed and not r8.select_done
			and (r8.phase == "done" or (r8.tick - r8.truth_last_new) >= R8.truth_settle_ticks) then
			r8_run_select_test()
			return
		end

		-- PART 1 CONDITION A (the stat panel) -> truth phase. This per-tick
		-- check is the fast tell; CONDITION B (a unit selected while the cards
		-- panel is up) is handled by the ~1 Hz gate line above, which OPENS the
		-- gate and NAMES the firing condition.
		if r8.phase == "idle" then
			local ds = find_by_id_under_hud("dynamic_stats")
			if ds ~= nil then
				r8.panel_seen = true
				r8.phase = "truth"
				if not r8.gate_open then
					r8.gate_open = true
					r8_out("GATE OPENED by panel: dynamic_stats is present")
				end
			end
		end

		-- PART 1 truth phase -> PART 2 auto ladder
		if r8.phase == "truth" then
			if (r8.tick % R8.truth_every) == 0 then
				pcall(r8_capture_truth)
			end
			if r8.sim_armed and r8.truth_count >= R8.min_truth
				and (r8.tick - r8.truth_last_new) >= R8.truth_settle_ticks then
				pcall(r8_start_ladder, "auto: truth stable for "
					.. tostring(math.floor(R8.truth_settle_ticks * R8.poll_ms / 1000)) .. " s")
			elseif (not r8.sim_armed) and (not r8.sim_wait_spoken)
				and r8.truth_count >= R8.min_truth
				and (r8.tick - r8.truth_last_new) >= R8.truth_settle_ticks then
				r8.sim_wait_spoken = true
				r8_out("SIMHOVER ladder DISARMED (round 9) - the simulated hover draws a"
					.. " FULL tooltip (not shippable); manual only: zz_probe_r8() or"
					.. " zz_probe_r8_toggle_sim()")
			end
		end
	end)
	if not ok then
		log("R8 poll error (swallowed): " .. truncate(err, 160))
	end
end

function zz_probe_r8()
	r8.force_calls = r8.force_calls + 1
	r8.force_pending = true
	r8.sim_armed = true
	-- log the FORCE banner + the gate line FIRST (unambiguous, and it shows the
	-- gate state this forced run is bypassing)
	r8_out("FORCE zz_probe_r8() called (force #" .. tostring(r8.force_calls)
		.. ") - the auto-gate is bypassed; the gate line follows")
	local ok_g, fired = pcall(r8_log_gate)
	r8.force_pending = false
	if r8.phase == "idle" then r8.phase = "truth" end
	local fired_s = ok_g and tostring(fired) or "?"
	local ok, started = pcall(r8_start_ladder, "manual FORCE: zz_probe_r8()", true)
	if not ok then return PROBE_TAG .. "R8 error: " .. tostring(started) end
	if not started then
		return PROBE_TAG .. "R8 FORCE did not start (see the log: " .. LOG_FILE
			.. ") - the cards panel must be up with >=1 visible unit card"
	end
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R8 simulated-hover ladder started (FORCED; gate fired="
		.. fired_s .. ") - KEEP YOUR HANDS OFF THE MOUSE until it finishes; log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r8_status()
	local owed = (r8.owed ~= nil) and "YES" or "no"
	local p = r8.pass
	local pass_s = "none"
	if p ~= nil then
		pass_s = tostring(p.card.id) .. " hold=" .. tostring(p.hold) .. " phase=" .. tostring(p.phase)
	end
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R8 phase=" .. tostring(r8.phase)
		.. " truth_entries=" .. tostring(r8.truth_count)
		.. " passes=" .. tostring(r8.passes_done) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.max_passes)
		.. " sim_on=" .. tostring(r8.sim_on) .. " sim_off=" .. tostring(r8.sim_off)
		.. " owed_off=" .. owed .. " pass=" .. pass_s
		.. " select_armed=" .. tostring(r8.select_armed)
		.. " select_done=" .. tostring(r8.select_done)
		.. " gate[panel_seen=" .. tostring(r8.gate_seen)
		.. " stat_rows=" .. tostring(r8.gate_rows)
		.. " selected_card=" .. tostring(r8.gate_sel)
		.. " fired=" .. tostring(r8.gate_fired)
		.. " ladder_state=" .. r8_ladder_state() .. "]"
		.. " force=" .. tostring(r8.force_calls)
		.. " | holds " .. tostring(R8.holds[1]) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.holds[2]) .. "/"
		.. tostring(R8.holds[3]) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.holds[4]) .. " ms"
		.. " | manual: zz_probe_r8() / zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test() | log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test()
	r8.select_armed = not r8.select_armed
	local st = r8.select_armed and "ARMED" or "DISARMED"
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R8 select test " .. st
		.. (r8.select_armed
			and " - it runs ONCE at the next idle moment (after the ladder), then stops;"
			or " - the select test will NOT run;")
		.. " log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r8_help()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R8 DECISIVE EXPERIMENT: (1) battle -> open AND PIN the unit-details"
		.. " panel -> click EACH of your units once in turn; each click logs"
		.. " 'R8 TRUTH <id> <stat>=<value> ...'. (2) After ~6 s of no new click the"
		.. " SIMULATED-HOVER LADDER auto-starts (or call zz_probe_r8() now): for every"
		.. " non-selected card it does SimulateMouseOn / SimulateMouseOff at holds "
		.. tostring(R8.holds[1]) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.holds[2]) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.holds[3]) .. "/"
		.. tostring(R8.holds[4]) .. " ms, polling every " .. tostring(R8.poll_ms)
		.. " ms, and writes one 'R8 SIMHOVER card=.. hold=.. comparison_seen=..' verdict"
		.. " per pass - KEEP YOUR HANDS OFF THE MOUSE while it runs. Holds below "
		.. tostring(R8.visible_ms) .. " ms are labelled invisible=yes (the layout's tooltip"
		.. " appear delay). (3) zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test() arms the ONE"
		.. " select_in_ui test (R8 DESELECT-TEST; OFF by default). status:"
		.. " zz_probe_r8_status(). log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r8_toggle_sim()
	r8.sim_armed = not r8.sim_armed
	local st = r8.sim_armed and "ARMED" or "DISARMED"
	return PROBE_TAG .. "R8 simulated-hover ladder " .. st
		.. (r8.sim_armed
			and " - zz_probe_r8() forces one ladder pass now (it draws a tooltip);"
			or " (default: it does NOT run - the tooltip route is not shippable);")
		.. " log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

-- ============================================================================
-- 14. ROUND 9 - RESOLVE THE STAT PANEL BY NAME FIRST, THEN READ ITS CONTEXT
--     OBJECTS (the last route to a NON-selected unit's stat numbers).
--
--     WHY. Round 8's gate walked the WHOLE HUD with a 400-visit budget while the
--     HUD holds ~630 components, so it never reached the panel and reported
--     `panel_seen=no stat_rows=0` while the panel was visibly open and pinned.
--     The user's criticism is right: stop scanning all the HUD - look the panel
--     UP BY NAME, then read the components it names. The simulated-hover route
--     is CONFIRMED DEAD (SimulateMouseOn works, `on_ok=true`, but it draws a
--     FULL TOOLTIP - not shippable) and the select_in_ui route is rejected too,
--     so the simhover ladder below is DISARMED by default (manual hook only).
--
--     THE PLAN (all READ-ONLY; ZERO SetContextObject):
--       (1) LOOKUP: resolve the known ids BY NAME from the UI root, in order -
--           unit_information, health_and_stats_parent, dynamic_stats,
--           template_stat, stats_toggle, row_header_stats - with the probe's
--           own root:Find (the engine's name-lookup helper is BANNED).
--           Every attempt logs
--             R9 LOOKUP <name> -> found=<yes/no> id="<actual id>" vis=<..> vfr=<..>
--       (2) WALK FALLBACK: only when a lookup fails, ONE bounded walk of
--           hud_battle (budget 2000 visits, depth 20) logs
--             R9 WALK started because <name> not found
--           and, when it stops,
--             R9 WALK stopped for <name>: reason=<budget|depth|complete> visits=<n> found=<yes/no>
--       (3) REAL IDS: under the panel, every component whose id matches
--           stat|dy_value|template|value_holder|bar_base|bar_mod|label_compare is
--           logged with its stext (so the ACTUAL id shapes in a live battle are
--           recorded, not the address-based ones round 4 saw):
--             R9 ID <id> stext="<..>" vis=<..> vfr=<..>
--       (4) CONTEXT READS on the components genuinely FOUND (unit_information,
--           health_and_stats_parent, dynamic_stats, the first template_stat row,
--           and that row's stat_name / value_holder / dy_value): for each of
--           CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit call GetContextObjectId
--           and GetContextObject and log every result:
--             R9 CTX <component id> <type_id> -> id="<..>"
--             R9 CTXOBJ <component id> <type_id> -> type=<..>
--       (5) THE DECISIVE QUERY: for every non-nil context id, call
--           common.get_context_value(<type_id>, <id>, <field>) for StatList.Size /
--           DisplayedValue / Name / Value / ValueBase / ComparisonValue; then
--           REPEAT the same calls with a NON-selected card's ui id - if any
--           non-selected query returns a plausible stat number, that is the win:
--             R9 QUERY selected=<id> field=<f> -> <value>
--             R9 QUERY nonsel=<id> field=<f> -> <value>
--       (6) GROUND TRUTH: if the panel's own stat rows are readable, log the
--           stat_name -> dy_value pairs (proves the panel path for the SELECTED
--           unit only):
--             R9 PANEL row <n> name="<..>" value="<..>"
--
--     DRIVING. ONE run, automatically when the stat panel (dynamic_stats) is
--     seen visible, and on demand with zz_probe_r9() from the console. The run
--     performs NO write of any kind; the simhover ladder from round 8 is
--     DISARMED at load (r8.sim_armed = false) and only runs via its manual hook.
-- ============================================================================

local R9 = {
  names = { "unit_information", "health_and_stats_parent", "dynamic_stats",
            "template_stat", "stats_toggle", "row_header_stats" },
  ctx_types = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoUnitStat", "CcoBattleUnit" },
  fields = { "StatList.Size", "DisplayedValue", "Name", "Value", "ValueBase", "ComparisonValue" },
  id_hints = { "stat", "dy_value", "template", "value_holder", "bar_base", "bar_mod", "label_compare" },
  walk_visits = 2000,      -- bounded fallback walk (the round-8 budget was 400)
  walk_depth  = 20,
  scan_visits = 1500,      -- the panel subtree scan (id logging + rows)
  scan_depth  = 20,
  max_rows    = 80,
  max_lines   = 2500,      -- HARD CAP on R9 log lines
  ran         = false,     -- the one automatic run has happened
  active      = false,     -- a run was requested, not yet performed
  origin      = nil,
  wait_spoken = false,
  lines       = 0,
  line_cap_spoken = false,
  auto_enabled = false,   -- ROUND 10: the R9 auto-run is DISARMED
}

function R9.out(msg)
  if R9.lines >= R9.max_lines then
    if not R9.line_cap_spoken then
      R9.line_cap_spoken = true
      log("R9 line cap reached (" .. tostring(R9.max_lines) .. ") - further R9 lines are not logged")
    end
    return
  end
  R9.lines = R9.lines + 1
  log("R9 " .. tostring(msg))
end

function R9.read_text(fn)
  local ok, v = pcall(fn)
  if not ok then return "<ERR>" end
  if v == nil then return nil end
  local s = safe_text(v)
  if s ~= nil then return s end
  return "<opaque>"
end

function R9.id_matches(low)
  for i = 1, #R9.id_hints do
    if contains_str(low, R9.id_hints[i]) then return R9.id_hints[i] end
  end
  return nil
end

-- (1) LOOKUP by name from the UI root with the probe's own root:Find ONLY. The
-- engine's name-lookup helper (the round-9/10 killer) is BANNED from this file.
-- Logs the attempt and the ACTUAL id/visibility of whatever answered.
function R9.find(name)
  local uic, how = nil, nil
  local c = find_by_name(name)
  if c ~= nil then uic = c; how = "root:Find" end
  -- root:FindByScriptTag / root:SequentialFind have ZERO call sites in any
  -- shipped script - unproven shapes, dropped.
  local id, vis, vfr = nil, nil, nil
  if uic ~= nil then
    id = R9.read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
    vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end)
    vfr = readb(function() return uic:VisibleFromRoot() end)
  end
  R9.out("LOOKUP " .. name .. " -> found=" .. (uic ~= nil and "yes" or "no")
    .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " vis=" .. tostring(vis) .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr)
    .. (how ~= nil and (" via=" .. how) or ""))
  return uic, how
end

-- (2) THE BOUNDED FALLBACK WALK: only for a name the lookup could not resolve.
function R9.walk_find(name)
  local hud = find_by_name(DEFAULT_ROOT)
  if hud == nil then return nil, "hud_battle-not-found", 0 end
  local found = nil
  local visits = 0
  local stop = "complete"
  local depth_hit = false
  local function visit(uic, depth)
    if uic == nil or found ~= nil then return end
    if visits >= R9.walk_visits then stop = "budget"; return end
    visits = visits + 1
    local id = R9.read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
    if id == name then found = uic; return end
    local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
    if lua_type(n) ~= "number" or n <= 0 then return end
    if depth >= R9.walk_depth then depth_hit = true; return end
    for i = 0, n - 1 do
      if found ~= nil then return end
      if visits >= R9.walk_visits then stop = "budget"; return end
      local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
      if ok_c and child ~= nil then
        pcall(visit, wrap(child), depth + 1)
      end
    end
  end
  pcall(visit, hud, 0)
  if found ~= nil then
    stop = "complete"
  elseif stop ~= "budget" and depth_hit then
    stop = "depth"
  end
  return found, stop, visits
end

-- (3) THE PANEL SCAN: walk the panel subtree (bounded), log every component id
-- that matches the id hints WITH its stext, and collect the first template_stat
-- row + its stat_name / value_holder / dy_value + the stat_name->dy_value pairs.
function R9.scan_panel(root)
  if root == nil then return nil end
  local first = {}
  local rows = {}
  local cur = nil
  local visits = 0
  local stop = "complete"
  local depth_hit = false
  local function visit(uic, depth)
    if uic == nil then return end
    if visits >= R9.scan_visits then stop = "budget"; return end
    visits = visits + 1
    local id = R9.read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
    local low = ""
    if id ~= nil and id ~= "" then low = string.lower(id) end
    if low ~= "" and R9.id_matches(low) ~= nil then
      local st = R9.read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
      local vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end)
      local vfr = readb(function() return uic:VisibleFromRoot() end)
      R9.out("ID " .. q(id) .. " stext=" .. q(st)
        .. " vis=" .. tostring(vis) .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr))
      if first[id] == nil then first[id] = uic end
      if id == "template_stat" then
        if #rows < R9.max_rows then
          cur = { uic = uic, name = nil, value = nil }
          rows[#rows + 1] = cur
        else
          cur = nil
        end
      elseif id == "stat_name" and cur ~= nil and cur.name == nil then
        cur.name = st
      elseif id == "dy_value" and cur ~= nil and cur.value == nil then
        cur.value = st
      end
    end
    local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
    if lua_type(n) ~= "number" or n <= 0 then return end
    if depth >= R9.scan_depth then depth_hit = true; return end
    for i = 0, n - 1 do
      if visits >= R9.scan_visits then stop = "budget"; return end
      local ok_c, child = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
      if ok_c and child ~= nil then
        pcall(visit, wrap(child), depth + 1)
      end
    end
  end
  pcall(visit, root, 0)
  if stop ~= "budget" and depth_hit then stop = "depth" end
  return { first = first, rows = rows, visits = visits, stop = stop }
end

-- (4) CONTEXT READS on ONE located component: both GetContextObjectId and
-- GetContextObject for every real type id; returns the non-nil ids by type.
function R9.ctx_probe(uic, label)
  if uic == nil then
    R9.out("CTX " .. label .. " -> component NOT FOUND")
    return nil
  end
  local ids = {}
  local comp_id = R9.read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
  for i = 1, #R9.ctx_types do
    local tid = R9.ctx_types[i]
    local ok_id, id_raw = pcall(function() return uic:GetContextObjectId(tid) end)
    local id_text = nil
    if ok_id then id_text = safe_text(id_raw) end
    if id_text ~= nil and id_text ~= "" then
      R9.out("CTX " .. q(comp_id) .. " " .. tid .. " -> id=" .. q(id_text))
      ids[tid] = id_text
    else
      R9.out("CTX " .. q(comp_id) .. " " .. tid .. " -> id=nil"
        .. (ok_id and "" or " <ERR>"))
    end
    local ok_o, o = pcall(function() return uic:GetContextObject(tid) end)
    R9.out("CTXOBJ " .. q(comp_id) .. " " .. tid .. " -> type="
      .. (ok_o and lua_type(o) or "<ERR>"))
  end
  return ids
end

-- (5) ONE decisive query: common.get_context_value for every field, tagged
-- selected / nonsel. READ ONLY.
function R9.query(type_id, obj_id, tag)
  if obj_id == nil or obj_id == "" then return end
  for i = 1, #R9.fields do
    local field = R9.fields[i]
    local ok, v = pcall(function() return common.get_context_value(type_id, obj_id, field) end)
    local text = nil
    if not ok then
      text = "<ERR>"
    else
      text = text_of(v, true)
      if text == nil then text = "<nil>" end
    end
    R9.out("QUERY " .. tag .. "=" .. q(obj_id) .. " field=" .. field .. " -> " .. q(text))
  end
end

function R9.run(origin)
  R9.lines = 0
  R9.line_cap_spoken = false
  R9.out("")
  R9.out("===== ROUND 9 RUN (" .. tostring(origin) .. ") t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. " =====")
  R9.out("LOOKUP FIRST by name; a " .. tostring(R9.walk_visits) .. "-visit / depth-"
    .. tostring(R9.walk_depth) .. " walk ONLY for a name that fails; ZERO SetContextObject;"
    .. " simhover DISARMED")

  -- (1) + (2) resolve every known id by name, walk only on a failure
  local resolved = {}
  for i = 1, #R9.names do
    local name = R9.names[i]
    local uic = R9.find(name)
    if uic ~= nil then
      resolved[name] = uic
    else
      R9.out("WALK started because " .. name .. " not found")
      local w, stop, visits = R9.walk_find(name)
      R9.out("WALK stopped for " .. name .. ": reason=" .. tostring(stop)
        .. " visits=" .. tostring(visits) .. " found=" .. (w ~= nil and "yes" or "no"))
      if w ~= nil then resolved[name] = w end
    end
  end

  -- (3) the panel scan (id logging) off dynamic_stats, else unit_information
  local panel_root = resolved["dynamic_stats"]
  if panel_root == nil then panel_root = resolved["unit_information"] end
  local scan = nil
  if panel_root ~= nil then
    local pid = R9.read_text(function() return panel_root:Id() end)
    R9.out("PANEL scan root id=" .. q(pid) .. " (budget " .. tostring(R9.scan_visits)
      .. " visits, depth " .. tostring(R9.scan_depth) .. ")")
    scan = R9.scan_panel(panel_root)
    if scan ~= nil then
      R9.out("PANEL scan done: visits=" .. tostring(scan.visits)
        .. " rows=" .. tostring(#scan.rows) .. " stop=" .. tostring(scan.stop))
    end
  else
    R9.out("PANEL scan skipped: neither dynamic_stats nor unit_information was resolved")
  end

  -- (4) the context reads on every component genuinely found
  local targets = {}
  if resolved["unit_information"] ~= nil then
    targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "unit_information", uic = resolved["unit_information"] }
  end
  if resolved["health_and_stats_parent"] ~= nil then
    targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "health_and_stats_parent", uic = resolved["health_and_stats_parent"] }
  end
  if resolved["dynamic_stats"] ~= nil then
    targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "dynamic_stats", uic = resolved["dynamic_stats"] }
  end
  if scan ~= nil then
    local f = scan.first
    if f["template_stat"] ~= nil then
      targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "template_stat row 1", uic = f["template_stat"] }
    end
    if f["stat_name"] ~= nil then
      targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "row 1 stat_name", uic = f["stat_name"] }
    end
    if f["value_holder"] ~= nil then
      targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "row 1 value_holder", uic = f["value_holder"] }
    end
    if f["dy_value"] ~= nil then
      targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "row 1 dy_value", uic = f["dy_value"] }
    end
  end
  if resolved["stats_toggle"] ~= nil then
    targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "stats_toggle", uic = resolved["stats_toggle"] }
  end
  if resolved["row_header_stats"] ~= nil then
    targets[#targets + 1] = { label = "row_header_stats", uic = resolved["row_header_stats"] }
  end

  R9.out("CTX targets: " .. tostring(#targets))
  local sel_ids = {}
  for i = 1, #targets do
    local t = targets[i]
    local ids = R9.ctx_probe(t.uic, t.label)
    if ids ~= nil then
      for tid, idv in pairs(ids) do
        if sel_ids[tid] == nil then sel_ids[tid] = idv end
      end
    end
  end

  -- (5) THE DECISIVE QUERY - selected unit's context ids first
  R9.out("--- decisive query with the SELECTED unit's context ids ---")
  local any_sel = false
  for tid, idv in pairs(sel_ids) do
    any_sel = true
    R9.query(tid, idv, "selected")
  end
  if not any_sel then
    R9.out("no non-nil context id was returned by the located components - nothing to query")
  end

  -- (5b) THE DECISIVE QUERY - a NON-selected card's ui id
  R9.out("--- decisive query with a NON-SELECTED card's ui id ---")
  local cards = r5_read_cards()
  local sel = r5_selected_set(cards)
  local nonsel_uiid = nil
  local nonsel_ctx = nil
  for i = 1, #cards do
    local c = cards[i]
    if c.uic ~= nil and c.vis == "true" and not (c.id ~= nil and sel[c.id] == true) then
      nonsel_uiid = c.id
      local ok_id, raw = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit") end)
      if ok_id then nonsel_ctx = safe_text(raw) end
      break
    end
  end
  if nonsel_uiid ~= nil then
    R9.out("non-selected card ui id=" .. q(nonsel_uiid)
      .. " (its CcoBattleUnit ctx id=" .. q(nonsel_ctx) .. ")")
    for i = 1, #R9.ctx_types do
      R9.query(R9.ctx_types[i], nonsel_uiid, "nonsel")
    end
    if nonsel_ctx ~= nil and nonsel_ctx ~= nonsel_uiid then
      R9.query("CcoBattleUnit", nonsel_ctx, "nonsel")
    end
  else
    R9.out("no visible NON-selected card was found - open the cards panel with >=2 units")
  end

  -- (6) the panel's own stat rows (ground truth for the SELECTED unit)
  if scan ~= nil and #scan.rows > 0 then
    local nrows = #scan.rows
    local printed = 0
    for i = 1, nrows do
      local r = scan.rows[i]
      if (r.name ~= nil and r.name ~= "") or (r.value ~= nil and r.value ~= "") then
        printed = printed + 1
        R9.out("PANEL row " .. tostring(printed) .. " name=" .. q(r.name) .. " value=" .. q(r.value))
      end
    end
    if printed == 0 then
      R9.out("PANEL: " .. tostring(nrows) .. " template_stat row(s) found but no stat_name/dy_value text")
    end
  else
    R9.out("PANEL: no stat_name/dy_value rows were readable under the panel")
  end

  R9.out("===== ROUND 9 RUN done (reads only; zero writes) =====")
end

function zz_probe_r9()
  R9.active = true
  R9.origin = "manual zz_probe_r9()"
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R9 run queued - the stat panel must be open and PINNED; the probe looks the"
    .. " panel up BY NAME and reads its context objects (zero writes). Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r9_status()
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R9 ran=" .. tostring(R9.ran) .. " active=" .. tostring(R9.active)
    .. " lines=" .. tostring(R9.lines) .. "/" .. tostring(R9.max_lines)
    .. " walk=" .. tostring(R9.walk_visits) .. " visits/depth " .. tostring(R9.walk_depth)
    .. " | names: " .. table.concat(R9.names, ", ")
    .. " | manual: zz_probe_r9() | log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r9_help()
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R9 NAME-LOOKUP: start a battle and open AND PIN the unit-details panel"
    .. " (no hovering needed - the probe does everything by itself). It resolves the panel"
    .. " BY NAME (unit_information / health_and_stats_parent / dynamic_stats / template_stat /"
    .. " stats_toggle / row_header_stats), logs the REAL component ids under the panel, reads"
    .. " GetContextObjectId/GetContextObject (CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit) on"
    .. " the components it FOUND, then runs common.get_context_value for StatList.Size /"
    .. " DisplayedValue / Name / Value / ValueBase / ComparisonValue with the selected unit's"
    .. " context id AND with a NON-selected card's ui id. ZERO writes. Manual: zz_probe_r9()."
    .. " Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end
-- ============================================================================
-- 15. ROUND 11 - COMPLETE UI-ROOT ENUMERATION, THEN DESCEND TO THE STAT PANEL
--     AND ASK ONE DECISIVE get_context_value (the round-10 post-mortem build).
--
--     WHY. Round 10's step 1 enumerated the 25 top-level children of
--     core:get_ui_root() perfectly (ChildCount + Find(i)) - that route is proven
--     SAFE. Step 2 (the children of a few roots) also ran safely but stopped
--     before covering the other 22 roots. Step 3 then called the engine's
--     name-lookup helper (the vanilla "find by name" shape) and THE GAME DIED on
--     that call. THAT HELPER IS BANNED FROM THIS FILE - there is no call site for
--     it anywhere below, and build_and_install.py asserts the token is absent
--     from the shipped probe. The two other name finders (the script-tag and the
--     sequential finder) stay deleted too - neither has a call site in any
--     shipped script.
--
--     THE PLAN (all READ-ONLY; ZERO SetContextObject; simhover DISARMED; one
--     native call per armed console step, each logged BEFORE it is made):
--       STEP 1 - enumerate the top-level roots (ChildCount + Find(i)).
--       STEP 2 - list EVERY root's children (budget 40 each), tagging any id
--                containing unit/panel/info/stat/card/left/right/tactical as a
--                HINT - the unit-info panel lives SOMEWHERE in this tree.
--       STEP 3 - descend TWO more levels below every hint-tagged root or child
--                (budget 400 visits TOTAL for the step, depth 4 from the UI
--                root), logging the full path of every node visited. This is how
--                the panel and its stat rows are FOUND:
--                dynamic_stats > template_stat > stat_name / value_holder > dy_value.
--       STEP 4 - log every located panel component (path + children), read the
--                stat rows (stat_name -> value_holder/dy_value via GetStateText)
--                and the CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit context ids
--                on the located components (GetContextObjectId only - a read).
--       STEP 5 - ONE decisive query, run twice with the SAME field: first with
--                the selected unit's context id (from step 4), then with a
--                NON-selected card's ui id: common.get_context_value(<type>,
--                <id>, "StatList.Size") - the vanilla call shape.
--
--     USE ONLY THE PROVEN-SAFE PRIMITIVES: ChildCount, Find, Id, Visible,
--     VisibleFromRoot, CurrentState, GetStateText. Every engine read is
--     pcall-walled, so a raising read can never take the walk down.
-- ============================================================================

local R11 = {
  run_no       = 0,
  step         = 0,          -- 0 = not started; +1 per armed step
  done         = false,
  lines        = 0,
  max_lines    = 6000,       -- HARD CAP on R11 log lines
  line_cap_spoken = false,
  -- hard enumeration budgets
  root_max       = 40,       -- top-level roots logged (step 1)
  child_max      = 40,       -- children per root (step 2) AND per child probe (step 4)
  descend_visits = 400,      -- step 3 TOTAL visits
  descend_depth  = 4,        -- step 3 max depth from the UI root
  -- hint substrings: an id containing ANY of these is tagged a HINT
  hints = { "unit", "panel", "info", "stat", "card", "left", "right", "tactical" },
  -- the panel components the descent is hunting (their ids)
  stat_ids = { ["dynamic_stats"] = true, ["template_stat"] = true,
               ["stat_name"] = true, ["value_holder"] = true, ["dy_value"] = true },
  -- step-1 output
  roots        = {},         -- { id, uic }
  -- step-2 output
  children     = {},         -- { id, uic, parent, root_id, hint }
  -- step-3 output
  located      = {},         -- id -> { uic, path }
  located_order = {},        -- ids in discovery order
  descend_count = 0,
  desc_best    = {},         -- path -> best `below` already descended (step 3 memo)
  -- step-4 output
  rows         = {},         -- { n, name, value }
  ctx          = {},         -- type_id -> context id (non-nil, first kept)
  ctx_from     = {},         -- type_id -> path the id came from
  -- step-5
  fields       = { "StatList.Size" },          -- THE single decisive field
  ctx_types    = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoUnitStat", "CcoBattleUnit" },
}

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- R11 logging
function R11.out(msg)
  if R11.lines >= R11.max_lines then
    if not R11.line_cap_spoken then
      R11.line_cap_spoken = true
      log("R11 line cap reached (" .. tostring(R11.max_lines) .. ") - further R11 lines are not logged")
    end
    return
  end
  R11.lines = R11.lines + 1
  log("R11 " .. tostring(msg))
end

-- ALWAYS call this IMMEDIATELY before a native call: it is the line that names
-- the fatal call if the engine dies on the next statement.
function R11.call(desc)
  R11.out("CALL " .. tostring(R11.step) .. " " .. tostring(desc))
end

function R11.read_text(fn)
  local ok, v = pcall(fn)
  if not ok then return "<ERR>" end
  if v == nil then return nil end
  local s = safe_text(v)
  if s ~= nil then return s end
  return "<opaque>"
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------- proven-shape primitives
function R11.ui_root()
  R11.call("core:get_ui_root()")
  local ok, r = pcall(function() return core:get_ui_root() end)
  if not ok or r == nil then return nil end
  return r
end

function R11.child_count(uic)
  if uic == nil then return 0 end
  local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
  if lua_type(n) == "number" then return n end
  return 0
end

-- uic:Find(i) -> a child, or nil. The result is TRUTHINESS-guarded (never wrap a
-- boolean: the round-9 crash).
function R11.child_at(uic, i)
  if uic == nil then return nil end
  local ok, raw = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
  if not ok or raw == nil or raw == false then return nil end
  return wrap(raw)
end

function R11.id_of(uic)
  if uic == nil then return nil end
  return R11.read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
end

function R11.vis_of(uic)
  if uic == nil then return nil, nil end
  local vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end)
  local vfr = readb(function() return uic:VisibleFromRoot() end)
  return tostring(vis), tostring(vfr)
end

-- the HINT test: does an id contain any of the hint substrings?
function R11.hint_of(id)
  if id == nil or id == "" then return nil end
  local low = string.lower(id)
  for i = 1, #R11.hints do
    if contains_str(low, R11.hints[i]) then return R11.hints[i] end
  end
  return nil
end

function R11.count_located()
  local n = 0
  for _ in pairs(R11.located) do n = n + 1 end
  return n
end

function R11.count_ctx()
  local n = 0
  for _ in pairs(R11.ctx) do n = n + 1 end
  return n
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the steps
R11.steps = {}

-- STEP 1 - enumerate the top-level children of the global UI root.
R11.steps[1] = function()
  R11.out("STEP 1 - enumerate the UI root's top-level children (budget "
    .. tostring(R11.root_max) .. ")")
  local root = R11.ui_root()
  if root == nil then
    R11.out("STEP 1 aborted: core:get_ui_root() returned nil")
    return
  end
  local n = R11.child_count(root)
  R11.out("ROOTCOUNT " .. tostring(n))
  if n <= 0 then
    R11.out("STEP 1: the UI root has no children yet (battle not up?)")
    return
  end
  R11.roots = {}
  local lim = n
  if lim > R11.root_max then lim = R11.root_max end
  for i = 0, lim - 1 do
    R11.call("ui_root:Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ") + Id/ChildCount/Visible/VisibleFromRoot")
    local uic = R11.child_at(root, i)
    local id = R11.id_of(uic)
    local vis, vfr = R11.vis_of(uic)
    local cn = tostring(R11.child_count(uic))
    R11.out("ROOT " .. tostring(i) .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " vis=" .. tostring(vis)
      .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr) .. " children=" .. cn)
    R11.roots[#R11.roots + 1] = { uic = uic, id = id }
  end
  if n > lim then
    R11.out("ROOT ... (" .. tostring(n - lim) .. " more root(s) not listed; cap "
      .. tostring(R11.root_max) .. ")")
  end
end

-- STEP 2 - EVERY root's children (~one level deeper), with the hint tag.
R11.steps[2] = function()
  R11.out("STEP 2 - every root's children (budget " .. tostring(R11.child_max) .. " each)")
  if R11.roots == nil or #R11.roots == 0 then
    R11.out("STEP 2 aborted: no roots recorded by step 1")
    return
  end
  R11.children = {}
  for ri = 1, #R11.roots do
    local r = R11.roots[ri]
    R11.call("root " .. q(r.id) .. ":ChildCount()")
    local cn = R11.child_count(r.uic)
    local lim = cn
    if lim > R11.child_max then lim = R11.child_max end
    R11.out("ROOTCHILD root=" .. q(r.id) .. " children=" .. tostring(cn)
      .. " listed=" .. tostring(lim))
    for j = 0, lim - 1 do
      R11.call("root " .. q(r.id) .. ":Find(" .. tostring(j) .. ")")
      local ch = R11.child_at(r.uic, j)
      local cid = R11.id_of(ch)
      local ccn = tostring(R11.child_count(ch))
      local hint = R11.hint_of(cid)
      R11.out("ROOTCHILD " .. q(r.id) .. " " .. tostring(j) .. " id=" .. q(cid)
        .. " children=" .. ccn .. " hint=" .. tostring(hint))
      R11.children[#R11.children + 1] =
        { id = cid, uic = ch, parent = ri, root_id = r.id, hint = hint }
    end
  end
  R11.out("STEP 2 done: " .. tostring(#R11.children) .. " child component(s) listed across "
    .. tostring(#R11.roots) .. " root(s)")
end

-- STEP 3 - descend two levels below every hint-tagged root/child, hunting the
-- panel components (dynamic_stats / template_stat / stat_name / value_holder /
-- dy_value). ONE shared 400-visit budget, depth 4 from the UI root.
R11.steps[3] = function()
  R11.out("STEP 3 - descend two levels below hint-tagged nodes (budget "
    .. tostring(R11.descend_visits) .. " visits, depth " .. tostring(R11.descend_depth) .. ")")
  R11.located = {}
  R11.located_order = {}
  R11.descend_count = 0
  R11.desc_best = {}
  if R11.roots == nil or #R11.roots == 0 then
    R11.out("STEP 3 aborted: no roots recorded by step 1")
    return
  end
  -- seeds: EVERY hint-tagged root AND EVERY hint-tagged child (two levels below
  -- each). The desc_best memo skips a subtree already descended at least as deep.
  local seeds = {}
  for i = 1, #R11.roots do
    local r = R11.roots[i]
    if R11.hint_of(r.id) ~= nil then
      seeds[#seeds + 1] = { uic = r.uic, path = tostring(r.id), depth = 1, below = 2 }
    end
  end
  for i = 1, #R11.children do
    local c = R11.children[i]
    if c.hint ~= nil then
      seeds[#seeds + 1] = { uic = c.uic, path = tostring(c.root_id) .. "/" .. tostring(c.id),
                            depth = 2, below = 2 }
    end
  end
  R11.out("STEP 3 seeds: " .. tostring(#seeds) .. " hinted node(s)")
  R11.desc_best = {}
  local function descend(uic, path, depth, below)
    if uic == nil then return end
    if R11.descend_count >= R11.descend_visits then return end
    if depth > R11.descend_depth then return end
    -- skip a subtree already descended at least as deep in this step
    local seen = R11.desc_best[path]
    if seen ~= nil and seen >= below then return end
    R11.desc_best[path] = below
    R11.descend_count = R11.descend_count + 1
    local id = R11.id_of(uic)
    R11.call("DESCEND " .. q(path) .. ":ChildCount()")
    local cn = R11.child_count(uic)
    R11.out("DESCEND path=" .. q(path) .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " children=" .. tostring(cn))
    if id ~= nil and R11.stat_ids[id] ~= nil and R11.located[id] == nil then
      R11.located[id] = { uic = uic, path = path }
      R11.located_order[#R11.located_order + 1] = id
    end
    if below <= 0 or depth >= R11.descend_depth then return end
    for i = 0, cn - 1 do
      if R11.descend_count >= R11.descend_visits then return end
      R11.call("DESCEND " .. q(path) .. ":Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ")")
      local ch = R11.child_at(uic, i)
      if ch ~= nil then
        local cid = R11.id_of(ch)
        if cid == nil or cid == "" then cid = "#" .. tostring(i) end
        descend(ch, path .. "/" .. cid, depth + 1, below - 1)
      end
    end
  end
  for i = 1, #seeds do
    local s = seeds[i]
    descend(s.uic, s.path, s.depth, s.below)
  end
  R11.out("STEP 3 done: visits=" .. tostring(R11.descend_count)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(R11.count_located()))
end

-- STEP 4 - read the located stat rows + the context ids (GetContextObjectId).
R11.steps[4] = function()
  R11.out("STEP 4 - read the located stat rows + the component context ids")
  R11.rows = {}
  R11.ctx = {}
  R11.ctx_from = {}
  if #R11.located_order == 0 then
    R11.out("STEP 4: the descent located NO panel component (dynamic_stats/template_stat/"
      .. "stat_name/value_holder/dy_value). Grep the DESCEND lines - the panel may sit deeper"
      .. " than depth " .. tostring(R11.descend_depth) .. " or under a non-hint root.")
  end
  -- find a child of `uic` whose Id() == want (bounded by child_max)
  local function child_named(uic, want)
    if uic == nil then return nil end
    local cn = R11.child_count(uic)
    local lim = cn
    if lim > R11.child_max then lim = R11.child_max end
    for i = 0, lim - 1 do
      R11.call("child " .. q(want) .. " under " .. q(R11.id_of(uic)) .. ":Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ")")
      local ch = R11.child_at(uic, i)
      if ch ~= nil and R11.id_of(ch) == want then return ch end
    end
    return nil
  end
  local function read_row(row, n)
    local sn = child_named(row, "stat_name")
    local vh = child_named(row, "value_holder")
    local dv = nil
    if vh ~= nil then dv = child_named(vh, "dy_value") end
    if dv == nil then dv = child_named(row, "dy_value") end
    local name_text, val_text = nil, nil
    if sn ~= nil then
      R11.call("stat_name:GetStateText()")
      name_text = R11.read_text(function() return sn:GetStateText() end)
    end
    if dv ~= nil then
      R11.call("dy_value:GetStateText()")
      val_text = R11.read_text(function() return dv:GetStateText() end)
    end
    R11.out("PANEL n=" .. tostring(n) .. " name=" .. q(name_text) .. " value=" .. q(val_text))
    R11.rows[#R11.rows + 1] = { n = n, name = name_text, value = val_text }
  end
  -- collect the stat rows: every template_stat child of a located dynamic_stats,
  -- else the located template_stat itself, else a lone located stat_name.
  local n = 0
  local ds = R11.located["dynamic_stats"]
  if ds ~= nil then
    local cn = R11.child_count(ds.uic)
    local lim = cn
    if lim > R11.child_max then lim = R11.child_max end
    for i = 0, lim - 1 do
      R11.call("dynamic_stats:Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ") looking for template_stat")
      local ch = R11.child_at(ds.uic, i)
      if ch ~= nil and R11.id_of(ch) == "template_stat" then
        n = n + 1
        read_row(ch, n)
      end
    end
  end
  if n == 0 and R11.located["template_stat"] ~= nil then
    n = n + 1
    read_row(R11.located["template_stat"].uic, n)
  end
  if n == 0 and R11.located["stat_name"] ~= nil then
    R11.call("stat_name:GetStateText()")
    local t = R11.read_text(function() return R11.located["stat_name"].uic:GetStateText() end)
    n = n + 1
    R11.out("PANEL n=" .. tostring(n) .. " name=" .. q(t) .. " value=" .. q(nil))
  end
  R11.out("STEP 4 rows=" .. tostring(#R11.rows))
  -- the context ids on every located component (a READ: GetContextObjectId)
  for k = 1, #R11.located_order do
    local id = R11.located_order[k]
    local rec = R11.located[id]
    if rec ~= nil then
      local cn = R11.child_count(rec.uic)
      R11.out("LOCATED " .. q(id) .. " path=" .. q(rec.path) .. " children=" .. tostring(cn))
      for t = 1, #R11.ctx_types do
        local tid = R11.ctx_types[t]
        R11.call(q(rec.path) .. " GetContextObjectId(" .. tid .. ")")
        local ok, raw = pcall(function() return rec.uic:GetContextObjectId(tid) end)
        local text = nil
        if ok then text = safe_text(raw) end
        R11.out("CTXID " .. q(rec.path) .. " " .. tid .. " -> " .. (ok and q(text) or "<ERR>"))
        if ok and text ~= nil and text ~= "" and R11.ctx[tid] == nil then
          R11.ctx[tid] = text
          R11.ctx_from[tid] = rec.path
        end
      end
    end
  end
  R11.out("STEP 4 done: items=" .. tostring(#R11.located_order)
    .. " ctx_ids=" .. tostring(R11.count_ctx()))
end

-- STEP 5 - ONE decisive query, run twice: the selected unit's context id, then a
-- NON-selected card's ui id. Vanilla shape, ZERO SetContextObject.
R11.steps[5] = function()
  local field = R11.fields[1]
  R11.out("STEP 5 - ONE decisive common.get_context_value (field=" .. field .. ")")
  local sel_tid, sel_id = nil, nil
  for i = 1, #R11.ctx_types do
    local tid = R11.ctx_types[i]
    if R11.ctx[tid] ~= nil then sel_tid = tid; sel_id = R11.ctx[tid]; break end
  end
  if sel_tid == nil then
    R11.out("STEP 5: no context id came out of step 4 - the decisive query is skipped")
    return
  end
  -- (a) the SELECTED unit's context id (read off the panel in step 4)
  R11.call("common.get_context_value(" .. sel_tid .. ", " .. q(sel_id) .. ", " .. q(field) .. ")")
  local ok1, v1 = pcall(function() return common.get_context_value(sel_tid, sel_id, field) end)
  local t1 = ok1 and text_of(v1, true) or "<ERR>"
  if t1 == nil then t1 = "<nil>" end
  R11.out("QUERY selected type=" .. sel_tid .. " id=" .. q(sel_id) .. " field=" .. field
    .. " -> " .. q(t1) .. " (from " .. tostring(R11.ctx_from[sel_tid]) .. ")")
  -- (b) a NON-selected card's ui id
  local cards, sel = nil, nil
  local cok, c1 = pcall(r5_read_cards)
  if cok then cards = c1 end
  local sok, s1 = pcall(r5_selected_set, cards)
  if sok then sel = s1 end
  if cards == nil or #cards == 0 then
    R11.out("QUERY nonsel: no unit cards found (review_DY) - keep the cards panel up with >=2 units")
    return
  end
  local nonsel_id, nonsel_ctx = nil, nil
  for i = 1, #cards do
    local c = cards[i]
    if c.uic ~= nil and c.vis == "true" and not (c.id ~= nil and sel ~= nil and sel[c.id] == true) then
      nonsel_id = c.id
      local ok_id, raw = pcall(function() return c.uic:GetContextObjectId("CcoBattleUnit") end)
      if ok_id then nonsel_ctx = safe_text(raw) end
      break
    end
  end
  if nonsel_id == nil then
    R11.out("QUERY nonsel: no visible NON-selected card (>=2 units needed)")
    return
  end
  R11.out("QUERY nonsel card ui id=" .. q(nonsel_id) .. " (its CcoBattleUnit ctx id="
    .. q(nonsel_ctx) .. ")")
  R11.call("common.get_context_value(\"CcoBattleUnit\", " .. q(nonsel_id) .. ", " .. q(field) .. ")")
  local ok2, v2 = pcall(function()
    return common.get_context_value("CcoBattleUnit", nonsel_id, field)
  end)
  local t2 = ok2 and text_of(v2, true) or "<ERR>"
  if t2 == nil then t2 = "<nil>" end
  R11.out("QUERY nonsel type=CcoBattleUnit id=" .. q(nonsel_id) .. " field=" .. field
    .. " -> " .. q(t2))
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the driver
function R11.advance()
  if R11.done then
    R11.out("step ignored: the run is done - zz_probe_r11() restarts it")
    return R11.step
  end
  R11.step = R11.step + 1
  local fn = R11.steps[R11.step]
  if fn == nil then
    R11.done = true
    R11.out("===== ROUND 11 RUN done (reads only; zero writes) =====")
    return R11.step
  end
  R11.out("")
  R11.out("===== R11 STEP " .. tostring(R11.step) .. " (t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. ") =====")
  local ok, err = pcall(fn)
  if not ok then
    R11.out("STEP " .. tostring(R11.step) .. " raised (swallowed): " .. truncate(err, 160))
  end
  return R11.step
end

function zz_probe_r11()
  R11.step = 0
  R11.done = false
  R11.roots = {}
  R11.children = {}
  R11.located = {}
  R11.located_order = {}
  R11.descend_count = 0
  R11.desc_best = {}
  R11.rows = {}
  R11.ctx = {}
  R11.ctx_from = {}
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R11 READY (step 0). In battle, open AND PIN the unit-info panel (keep the"
    .. " cards panel up with >=2 units), then call zz_probe_r11_step() ONE step at a time -"
    .. " after each step, if the game is still alive, type the next. Steps 1-2 are PROVEN SAFE."
    .. " Or zz_probe_r11_auto() to run to the cap. Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r11_step()
  if R11.step == 0 and (not R11.done) then
    R11.run_no = R11.run_no + 1
    R11.lines = 0
    R11.line_cap_spoken = false
    R11.out("")
    R11.out("===== ROUND 11 RUN #" .. tostring(R11.run_no)
      .. " (manual zz_probe_r11_step) t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. " =====")
    R11.out("FULL UI-root enumeration first (steps 1-2); then TWO-level descent below the hint"
      .. " nodes (step 3); then the stat rows + context ids (step 4) and ONE decisive"
      .. " common.get_context_value (step 5). Every native call is logged BEFORE it is made;"
      .. " ZERO SetContextObject; simhover DISARMED.")
  end
  local before = R11.step
  R11.advance()
  local nxt = R11.step + 1
  local nxt_name = R11.steps[nxt] ~= nil and ("step " .. tostring(nxt)) or "done"
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R11 step " .. tostring(R11.step) .. " done (was " .. tostring(before)
    .. "); next: " .. nxt_name .. " - call zz_probe_r11_step() again. log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r11_auto()
  if R11.step == 0 and (not R11.done) then zz_probe_r11() end
  R11.run_no = R11.run_no + 1
  R11.lines = 0
  R11.line_cap_spoken = false
  R11.out("")
  R11.out("===== ROUND 11 AUTO RUN #" .. tostring(R11.run_no) .. " t=" .. tostring(tick_count)
    .. " - runs every step until the cap; a fatal call dies here and the last R11 CALL names it =====")
  local guard = 0
  while (not R11.done) and guard < 40 do
    guard = guard + 1
    R11.advance()
  end
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R11 auto finished (step=" .. tostring(R11.step)
    .. (R11.done and ", done" or ", cap") .. "). log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r11_status()
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R11 run=" .. tostring(R11.run_no) .. " step=" .. tostring(R11.step)
    .. "/5 done=" .. tostring(R11.done) .. " lines=" .. tostring(R11.lines)
    .. "/" .. tostring(R11.max_lines)
    .. " | roots=" .. tostring(#(R11.roots or {}))
    .. " children=" .. tostring(#(R11.children or {}))
    .. " descend_visits=" .. tostring(R11.descend_count) .. "/" .. tostring(R11.descend_visits)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(R11.count_located())
    .. " rows=" .. tostring(#(R11.rows or {}))
    .. " ctx_ids=" .. tostring(R11.count_ctx())
    .. " | zz_probe_r11() to start/restart; log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r11_help()
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R11 COMPLETE-ENUMERATION + DESCENT: start a battle, open AND PIN the"
    .. " unit-info panel, and keep the cards panel up with >=2 units. Call zz_probe_r11() once,"
    .. " then zz_probe_r11_step() repeatedly (after each step, if the game is alive, call it"
    .. " again). Steps 1-2 are PROVEN SAFE (they only use core:get_ui_root() + ChildCount +"
    .. " Find(i) + Id): step 1 lists the top-level roots, step 2 lists EVERY root's children"
    .. " (budget " .. tostring(R11.child_max) .. ") and tags unit/panel/info/stat/card/left/right/"
    .. "tactical ids as HINTS. Step 3 descends two levels below every hint node (budget "
    .. tostring(R11.descend_visits) .. " visits, depth " .. tostring(R11.descend_depth)
    .. ") to FIND the panel (dynamic_stats/template_stat/stat_name/value_holder/dy_value)."
    .. " Step 4 reads the stat rows (stat_name -> value_holder/dy_value, GetStateText) and the"
    .. " CcoUnitDetails/CcoUnitStat/CcoBattleUnit context ids (GetContextObjectId). Step 5 makes"
    .. " ONE common.get_context_value(\"<type>\", \"<id>\", \"StatList.Size\") with the SELECTED"
    .. " unit's context id, then the same with a NON-selected card's ui id. The engine's"
    .. " name-lookup helper is BANNED from this file. ZERO writes. Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

-- ============================================================================
-- 16. ROUND 12 - FINISH THE PANEL HUNT: SEED THE DESCENT ON THE NUMERIC
--     UNIT-ID NODES UNDER unit_id_holder, DESCEND TO DEPTH 8 (800 VISITS),
--     PAIR THE STAT ROWS, READ THE CONTEXT IDS, THEN ASK EXACTLY TWO
--     common.get_context_value CALLS (the round-11 depth-cap post-mortem build).
--
--     WHY. Round 11's step 3 stopped at 88 of its 400 visits - the DEPTH cap
--     (4), not the budget, cut the hunt short. Its last node was
--         R11 DESCEND path="unit_id_holder/1001/modular_parent" id="modular_parent" children=10
--     i.e. the unit-info panel is PER-UNIT, under
--     unit_id_holder/<unit ui id>/modular_parent - and the stat rows sit at
--     DEPTH 5-8, one level past the round-11 cap. Round 12 re-seeds the
--     descent on the NUMERIC unit-id nodes (1001, 1002, ...) found under
--     unit_id_holder and descends to DEPTH 8 with an 800-visit budget.
--
--     R12 TOTAL STEPS 6 - you are done after step 6.
--
--     THE PLAN (all READ-ONLY; ZERO SetContextObject; simhover DISARMED; the
--     engine's name-lookup helper is BANNED from this file; ONE armed console
--     step at a time, every native call logged BEFORE it is made):
--       STEP 1 - enumerate the UI root's top-level children; keep unit_id_holder.
--       STEP 2 - list unit_id_holder's children; the NUMERIC ids (1001, 1002,
--                ...) are the per-unit seeds.
--       STEP 3 - descend EVERY unit-id subtree to DEPTH 8 (800 visits TOTAL),
--                logging R12 DOWN path/id/children/stext for every node inside.
--       STEP 4 - locate the stat-row nodes (health_and_stats / dynamic_stats /
--                template_stat / stat_name / value_holder / dy_value) and pair
--                every template_stat row's stat_name with its dy_value.
--       STEP 5 - read GetContextObjectId(CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat /
--                CcoBattleUnit) on the located row components (reads only).
--       STEP 6 - run EXACTLY TWO common.get_context_value calls: ONE with the
--                SELECTED unit's context id, ONE with a NON-selected unit's ui id.
--     Only proven-safe primitives: ChildCount, Find, Id, Visible,
--     VisibleFromRoot, CurrentState, GetStateText, GetContextObjectId.
-- ============================================================================

-- A GLOBAL table (not a local): the probe chunk already carries ~168 top-level
-- locals and Lua's 200-local ceiling is real - R12 must not spend one.
R12 = {
  run_no          = 0,
  step            = 0,          -- 0 = not started; +1 per armed step
  done            = false,
  total_steps     = 6,          -- R12 TOTAL STEPS 6 - you are done after step 6
  lines           = 0,
  max_lines       = 9000,       -- HARD CAP on R12 log lines
  line_cap_spoken = false,
  -- hard enumeration budgets
  root_max        = 60,         -- top-level roots logged (step 1)
  child_max       = 60,         -- children scanned per node (steps 2/4)
  descend_visits  = 800,        -- step 3 TOTAL visits
  descend_depth   = 8,          -- step 3 max depth FROM a unit-id seed
  locate_max      = 60,         -- most located components kept for step 4/5
  ctx_max         = 60,         -- most located components probed in step 5
  -- the panel ids the descent is hunting (SUBSTRING match on a lowercased id)
  locate_names = { "health_and_stats", "dynamic_stats", "template_stat",
                   "stat_name", "value_holder", "dy_value" },
  -- step-1 output
  roots        = {},            -- { id, uic }
  -- step-2 output
  children     = {},            -- { id, uic, numeric, stext }
  seeds        = {},            -- { id, uic, path } - the NUMERIC unit-id nodes
  -- step-3 output
  located       = {},           -- id -> first { id, uic, path }
  located_order = {},           -- ids in discovery order
  located_list  = {},           -- EVERY located node { id, uic, path }
  descend_count = 0,
  desc_seen     = {},           -- path -> true (repeat/cycle guard)
  -- step-4 output
  rows         = {},            -- { n, name, value, uic, path }
  -- step-5 output
  ctx_types    = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoUnitStat", "CcoBattleUnit" },
  ctx          = {},            -- type_id -> context id (non-nil, first kept)
  ctx_from     = {},            -- type_id -> path the id came from
  selected_ui  = nil,           -- the SELECTED unit's numeric ui id (from a path)
  sel_tid      = nil,           -- the type the selected context id came from
  sel_id       = nil,           -- the selected context id
  -- step-6
  fields       = { "StatList.Size" },   -- THE single decisive field
  gcv_calls    = 0,
}

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- R12 logging
function R12.out(msg)
  if R12.lines >= R12.max_lines then
    if not R12.line_cap_spoken then
      R12.line_cap_spoken = true
      log("R12 line cap reached (" .. tostring(R12.max_lines) .. ") - further R12 lines are not logged")
    end
    return
  end
  R12.lines = R12.lines + 1
  log("R12 " .. tostring(msg))
end

-- ALWAYS call this IMMEDIATELY before a native call: it is the line that names
-- the fatal call if the engine dies on the next statement.
function R12.call(desc)
  R12.out("CALL " .. tostring(R12.step) .. " " .. tostring(desc))
end

function R12.read_text(fn)
  local ok, v = pcall(fn)
  if not ok then return "<ERR>" end
  if v == nil then return nil end
  local s = safe_text(v)
  if s ~= nil then return s end
  return "<opaque>"
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------- proven-shape primitives
function R12.ui_root()
  R12.call("core:get_ui_root()")
  local ok, r = pcall(function() return core:get_ui_root() end)
  if not ok or r == nil then return nil end
  return r
end

function R12.child_count(uic)
  if uic == nil then return 0 end
  local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
  if lua_type(n) == "number" then return n end
  return 0
end

-- uic:Find(i) -> a child, or nil. The result is TRUTHINESS-guarded (never wrap a
-- boolean: the round-9 crash).
function R12.child_at(uic, i)
  if uic == nil then return nil end
  local ok, raw = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
  if not ok or raw == nil or raw == false then return nil end
  return wrap(raw)
end

function R12.id_of(uic)
  if uic == nil then return nil end
  return R12.read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
end

function R12.vis_of(uic)
  if uic == nil then return nil, nil end
  local vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end)
  local vfr = readb(function() return uic:VisibleFromRoot() end)
  return tostring(vis), tostring(vfr)
end

-- an id is a unit ui id when EVERY character is a digit
function R12.is_numeric(s)
  local str = safe_text(s)
  if str == nil or str == "" then return false end
  local len = string.len(str)
  for i = 1, len do
    local c = string.byte(str, i)
    if c == nil or c < 48 or c > 57 then return false end
  end
  return true
end

-- does an id name one of the panel nodes the hunt is after?
function R12.is_located_id(id)
  local str = safe_text(id)
  if str == nil then return false end
  local low = string.lower(str)
  for i = 1, #R12.locate_names do
    if contains_str(low, R12.locate_names[i]) then return true end
  end
  return false
end

function R12.count_ctx()
  local n = 0
  for _ in pairs(R12.ctx) do n = n + 1 end
  return n
end

-- Split helpers WITHOUT string.find (the probe bans it): plain byte scans.
function R12.first_segment(s)
  local str = safe_text(s)
  if str == nil then return nil end
  local len = string.len(str)
  for i = 1, len do
    if string.sub(str, i, i) == "/" then return string.sub(str, 1, i - 1) end
  end
  return str
end

function R12.strip_prefix(s, p)
  local str = safe_text(s)
  local pp = tostring(p)
  if str == nil then return nil end
  if string.len(str) >= string.len(pp)
     and string.sub(str, 1, string.len(pp)) == pp then
    return string.sub(str, string.len(pp) + 1)
  end
  return str
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the steps
R12.steps = {}

-- STEP 1 - enumerate the UI root's top-level children (find unit_id_holder).
R12.steps[1] = function()
  R12.out("STEP 1 - enumerate the UI root's top-level children (budget "
    .. tostring(R12.root_max) .. ")")
  local root = R12.ui_root()
  if root == nil then
    R12.out("STEP 1 aborted: core:get_ui_root() returned nil")
    return
  end
  local n = R12.child_count(root)
  R12.out("ROOTCOUNT " .. tostring(n))
  if n <= 0 then
    R12.out("STEP 1: the UI root has no children yet (battle not up?)")
    return
  end
  R12.roots = {}
  local lim = n
  if lim > R12.root_max then lim = R12.root_max end
  for i = 0, lim - 1 do
    R12.call("ui_root:Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ") + Id/ChildCount/Visible/VisibleFromRoot")
    local uic = R12.child_at(root, i)
    local id = R12.id_of(uic)
    local vis, vfr = R12.vis_of(uic)
    local cn = tostring(R12.child_count(uic))
    R12.out("ROOT " .. tostring(i) .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " vis=" .. tostring(vis)
      .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr) .. " children=" .. cn)
    R12.roots[#R12.roots + 1] = { uic = uic, id = id }
  end
  if n > lim then
    R12.out("ROOT ... (" .. tostring(n - lim) .. " more root(s) not listed; cap "
      .. tostring(R12.root_max) .. ")")
  end
end

-- STEP 2 - list unit_id_holder's children; the NUMERIC ids are the seeds.
R12.steps[2] = function()
  R12.out("STEP 2 - list unit_id_holder's children; the NUMERIC ids (1001, 1002,"
    .. " ...) are the per-unit seeds")
  R12.children = {}
  R12.seeds = {}
  if R12.roots == nil or #R12.roots == 0 then
    R12.out("STEP 2 aborted: no roots recorded by step 1")
    return
  end
  local holder = nil
  for i = 1, #R12.roots do
    local rid = R12.roots[i].id
    if rid ~= nil and safe_text(rid) == "unit_id_holder" then holder = R12.roots[i]; break end
  end
  if holder == nil then
    for i = 1, #R12.roots do
      local rid = R12.roots[i].id
      if rid ~= nil and contains_str(string.lower(tostring(rid)), "unit_id_holder") then
        holder = R12.roots[i]; break
      end
    end
  end
  if holder == nil then
    R12.out("STEP 2: NO unit_id_holder root among the " .. tostring(#R12.roots)
      .. " root(s) - keep the unit cards up in battle")
    return
  end
  local cn = R12.child_count(holder.uic)
  local lim = cn
  if lim > R12.child_max then lim = R12.child_max end
  R12.out("UNITIDHOLDER children=" .. tostring(cn) .. " listed=" .. tostring(lim))
  for j = 0, lim - 1 do
    R12.call("unit_id_holder:Find(" .. tostring(j) .. ") + Id/ChildCount/GetStateText")
    local ch = R12.child_at(holder.uic, j)
    local cid = R12.id_of(ch)
    local ccn = tostring(R12.child_count(ch))
    local st = nil
    if ch ~= nil then
      R12.call("unit_id child GetStateText()")
      st = R12.read_text(function() return ch:GetStateText() end)
    end
    local numeric = R12.is_numeric(cid)
    R12.out("UNITIDCHILD " .. tostring(j) .. " id=" .. q(cid) .. " children=" .. ccn
      .. " numeric=" .. tostring(numeric) .. " stext=" .. q(st))
    R12.children[#R12.children + 1] = { id = cid, uic = ch, numeric = numeric, stext = st }
    if numeric and ch ~= nil then
      R12.seeds[#R12.seeds + 1] = { uic = ch, path = "unit_id_holder/" .. tostring(cid), id = cid }
    end
  end
  R12.out("STEP 2 done: " .. tostring(#R12.children) .. " child(ren), "
    .. tostring(#R12.seeds) .. " numeric unit-id seed(s)")
end

-- STEP 3 - descend EVERY unit-id subtree to DEPTH 8 (800 visits TOTAL). Only
-- proven-safe primitives. Paths are RELATIVE to the unit-id seed (seed = depth 1).
R12.steps[3] = function()
  R12.out("STEP 3 - descend EVERY unit-id subtree (seeds=" .. tostring(#R12.seeds)
    .. ", budget " .. tostring(R12.descend_visits) .. " visits, depth "
    .. tostring(R12.descend_depth) .. ")")
  R12.located = {}
  R12.located_order = {}
  R12.located_list = {}
  R12.descend_count = 0
  R12.desc_seen = {}
  if R12.seeds == nil or #R12.seeds == 0 then
    R12.out("STEP 3 aborted: no numeric unit-id seed came out of step 2 - open AND PIN"
      .. " the unit-info panel and keep the cards panel up with >=2 units")
    return
  end
  local function descend(uic, path, depth)
    if uic == nil then return end
    if R12.descend_count >= R12.descend_visits then return end
    if depth > R12.descend_depth then return end
    -- repeat / cycle guard keyed on the COMPONENT (paths collide when sibling ids
    -- repeat - e.g. every stat row is id "template_stat")
    if R12.desc_seen[uic] ~= nil then return end
    R12.desc_seen[uic] = true
    R12.descend_count = R12.descend_count + 1
    local id = R12.id_of(uic)
    R12.call("DOWN " .. q(path) .. ":ChildCount()")
    local cn = R12.child_count(uic)
    R12.call("DOWN " .. q(path) .. ":GetStateText() + CurrentState() + Visible/VisibleFromRoot")
    local st = R12.read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
    local cs = R12.read_text(function() return uic:CurrentState() end)
    local vis, vfr = R12.vis_of(uic)
    R12.out("DOWN path=" .. q(path) .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " children=" .. tostring(cn)
      .. " stext=" .. q(st) .. " state=" .. q(cs)
      .. " vis=" .. tostring(vis) .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr))
    if id ~= nil and R12.is_located_id(id) and #R12.located_list < R12.locate_max then
      local rec = { id = id, uic = uic, path = path }
      R12.located_list[#R12.located_list + 1] = rec
      if R12.located[id] == nil then
        R12.located[id] = rec
        R12.located_order[#R12.located_order + 1] = id
      end
    end
    if depth >= R12.descend_depth then return end
    for i = 0, cn - 1 do
      if R12.descend_count >= R12.descend_visits then return end
      R12.call("DOWN " .. q(path) .. ":Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ")")
      local ch = R12.child_at(uic, i)
      if ch ~= nil then
        local cid = R12.id_of(ch)
        if cid == nil or cid == "" then cid = "#" .. tostring(i) end
        descend(ch, path .. "/" .. cid, depth + 1)
      end
    end
  end
  for i = 1, #R12.seeds do
    local s = R12.seeds[i]
    descend(s.uic, s.path, 1)
  end
  R12.out("STEP 3 done: visits=" .. tostring(R12.descend_count)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(#R12.located_order))
end

-- STEP 4 - locate the stat-row nodes (path + id) and pair every template_stat
-- row's stat_name with its dy_value.
R12.steps[4] = function()
  R12.out("STEP 4 - locate the stat-row nodes and pair each row's name with its value")
  R12.rows = {}
  if R12.located_order == nil or #R12.located_order == 0 then
    R12.out("STEP 4: the descent located NO stat-row node (health_and_stats / dynamic_stats /"
      .. " template_stat / stat_name / value_holder / dy_value). Grep the DOWN lines - the panel"
      .. " may sit deeper than depth " .. tostring(R12.descend_depth) .. " or under a non-unit-id node")
  end
  for k = 1, #(R12.located_order or {}) do
    local id = R12.located_order[k]
    local rec = R12.located[id]
    if rec ~= nil then
      R12.out("LOCATED path=" .. q(rec.path) .. " id=" .. q(id)
        .. " children=" .. tostring(R12.child_count(rec.uic)))
    end
  end
  -- find a child of `uic` whose Id() == want (bounded by child_max)
  local function child_named(uic, want)
    if uic == nil then return nil end
    local cn = R12.child_count(uic)
    local lim = cn
    if lim > R12.child_max then lim = R12.child_max end
    for i = 0, lim - 1 do
      R12.call("child " .. q(want) .. " under " .. q(R12.id_of(uic)) .. ":Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ")")
      local ch = R12.child_at(uic, i)
      if ch ~= nil and R12.id_of(ch) == want then return ch end
    end
    return nil
  end
  local function read_row(row_uic, n, row_path)
    local sn = child_named(row_uic, "stat_name")
    local vh = child_named(row_uic, "value_holder")
    local dv = nil
    if vh ~= nil then dv = child_named(vh, "dy_value") end
    if dv == nil then dv = child_named(row_uic, "dy_value") end
    local name_text, val_text = nil, nil
    if sn ~= nil then
      R12.call("stat_name:GetStateText()")
      name_text = R12.read_text(function() return sn:GetStateText() end)
    end
    if dv ~= nil then
      R12.call("dy_value:GetStateText()")
      val_text = R12.read_text(function() return dv:GetStateText() end)
    end
    R12.out("PANEL row=" .. tostring(n) .. " name=" .. q(name_text) .. " value=" .. q(val_text)
      .. " path=" .. q(row_path))
    R12.rows[#R12.rows + 1] = { n = n, name = name_text, value = val_text, uic = row_uic, path = row_path }
  end
  -- every located template_stat is one stat row
  local n = 0
  for k = 1, #(R12.located_list or {}) do
    local rec = R12.located_list[k]
    if rec.id == "template_stat" then
      n = n + 1
      read_row(rec.uic, n, rec.path)
    end
  end
  -- fallback: a located dynamic_stats whose template_stat children were not
  -- themselves located (defensive; the descent normally visits them)
  if n == 0 then
    local ds = R12.located["dynamic_stats"]
    if ds ~= nil then
      local cn = R12.child_count(ds.uic)
      local lim = cn
      if lim > R12.child_max then lim = R12.child_max end
      for i = 0, lim - 1 do
        R12.call("dynamic_stats:Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ") looking for template_stat")
        local ch = R12.child_at(ds.uic, i)
        if ch ~= nil and R12.id_of(ch) == "template_stat" then
          n = n + 1
          read_row(ch, n, ds.path .. "/template_stat[" .. tostring(i) .. "]")
        end
      end
    end
  end
  -- fallback: a lone located stat_name (+ a located dy_value, if any)
  if n == 0 and R12.located["stat_name"] ~= nil then
    R12.call("stat_name:GetStateText()")
    local t = R12.read_text(function() return R12.located["stat_name"].uic:GetStateText() end)
    local v = nil
    local dv = R12.located["dy_value"]
    if dv ~= nil then
      R12.call("dy_value:GetStateText()")
      v = R12.read_text(function() return dv.uic:GetStateText() end)
    end
    n = n + 1
    R12.out("PANEL row=" .. tostring(n) .. " name=" .. q(t) .. " value=" .. q(v)
      .. " path=" .. q(R12.located["stat_name"].path))
    R12.rows[#R12.rows + 1] = { n = n, name = t, value = v }
  end
  R12.out("STEP 4 done: rows=" .. tostring(#R12.rows)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(#(R12.located_order or {})))
end

-- STEP 5 - read GetContextObjectId (CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit)
-- on the located row components (READS only).
R12.steps[5] = function()
  R12.out("STEP 5 - read GetContextObjectId on the located row components (reads only)")
  R12.ctx = {}
  R12.ctx_from = {}
  R12.selected_ui = nil
  R12.sel_tid = nil
  R12.sel_id = nil
  if R12.located_list == nil or #R12.located_list == 0 then
    R12.out("STEP 5: nothing was located - no context id to read")
    return
  end
  local probed = 0
  for k = 1, #R12.located_list do
    if probed >= R12.ctx_max then break end
    local rec = R12.located_list[k]
    probed = probed + 1
    for t = 1, #R12.ctx_types do
      local tid = R12.ctx_types[t]
      R12.call(q(rec.path) .. " GetContextObjectId(" .. tid .. ")")
      local ok, raw = pcall(function() return rec.uic:GetContextObjectId(tid) end)
      local text = nil
      if ok then text = safe_text(raw) end
      R12.out("CTXID " .. q(rec.path) .. " " .. tid .. " -> " .. (ok and q(text) or "<ERR>"))
      if ok and text ~= nil and text ~= "" and R12.ctx[tid] == nil then
        R12.ctx[tid] = text
        R12.ctx_from[tid] = rec.path
      end
    end
  end
  -- the SELECTED unit's context id = the first non-nil one (a read off the panel)
  for i = 1, #R12.ctx_types do
    local tid = R12.ctx_types[i]
    if R12.ctx[tid] ~= nil then R12.sel_tid = tid; R12.sel_id = R12.ctx[tid]; break end
  end
  if R12.sel_tid == nil then
    R12.out("STEP 5: NO context id came back (all nil) - step 6 will have nothing to query")
    return
  end
  -- the SELECTED unit's ui id = the numeric segment right after unit_id_holder in
  -- the path the selected context id came from (recorded data only - no new read)
  local from = R12.ctx_from[R12.sel_tid]
  if from ~= nil then
    local rest = R12.strip_prefix(from, "unit_id_holder/")
    local seg = R12.first_segment(rest)
    if seg ~= nil and R12.is_numeric(seg) then R12.selected_ui = seg end
  end
  R12.out("STEP 5 done: ctx_ids=" .. tostring(R12.count_ctx())
    .. " selected_type=" .. tostring(R12.sel_tid) .. " selected_id=" .. q(R12.sel_id)
    .. " selected_ui=" .. q(R12.selected_ui))
end

-- STEP 6 - EXACTLY TWO common.get_context_value calls (vanilla shape, ZERO
-- SetContextObject): the SELECTED unit's context id, then a NON-selected ui id.
R12.steps[6] = function()
  local field = R12.fields[1]
  R12.out("STEP 6 - EXACTLY TWO common.get_context_value calls (vanilla shape, field="
    .. tostring(field) .. ")")
  R12.gcv_calls = 0
  if R12.sel_tid == nil or R12.sel_id == nil then
    R12.out("STEP 6: no context id came out of step 5 - both queries are skipped (0 calls made)")
    return
  end
  -- (a) the SELECTED unit's context id (read off the panel in step 5)
  R12.call("common.get_context_value(" .. R12.sel_tid .. ", " .. q(R12.sel_id) .. ", " .. q(field) .. ")")
  local ok1, v1 = pcall(function() return common.get_context_value(R12.sel_tid, R12.sel_id, field) end)
  R12.gcv_calls = R12.gcv_calls + 1
  local t1 = ok1 and text_of(v1, true) or "<ERR>"
  if t1 == nil then t1 = "<nil>" end
  R12.out("QUERY sel=" .. q(R12.sel_id) .. " type=" .. R12.sel_tid .. " field=" .. field
    .. " -> " .. q(t1) .. " (from " .. tostring(R12.ctx_from[R12.sel_tid]) .. ")")
  -- (b) a NON-selected unit's ui id (a numeric unit-id under unit_id_holder,
  --     other than the selected one) - the field-proven CcoBattleUnit ui-id shape
  local nonsel = nil
  for i = 1, #R12.children do
    local c = R12.children[i]
    if c.numeric and c.id ~= nil and tostring(c.id) ~= tostring(R12.selected_ui) then
      nonsel = tostring(c.id); break
    end
  end
  if nonsel == nil then
    R12.out("QUERY nonsel: no NON-selected numeric unit-id under unit_id_holder"
      .. " (keep the cards panel up with >=2 units)")
    return
  end
  R12.out("QUERY nonsel unit ui id=" .. q(nonsel) .. " (selected_ui=" .. q(R12.selected_ui) .. ")")
  R12.call("common.get_context_value(\"CcoBattleUnit\", " .. q(nonsel) .. ", " .. q(field) .. ")")
  local ok2, v2 = pcall(function() return common.get_context_value("CcoBattleUnit", nonsel, field) end)
  R12.gcv_calls = R12.gcv_calls + 1
  local t2 = ok2 and text_of(v2, true) or "<ERR>"
  if t2 == nil then t2 = "<nil>" end
  R12.out("QUERY nonsel=" .. q(nonsel) .. " type=CcoBattleUnit field=" .. field .. " -> " .. q(t2))
  R12.out("STEP 6 done: get_context_value calls=" .. tostring(R12.gcv_calls) .. " (want 2)")
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the driver
function R12.advance()
  if R12.done then
    R12.out("step ignored: the run is done (" .. tostring(R12.total_steps)
      .. " steps) - zz_probe_r12() restarts it")
    return R12.step
  end
  R12.step = R12.step + 1
  local fn = R12.steps[R12.step]
  if fn == nil then
    R12.done = true
    R12.out("===== ROUND 12 RUN done after " .. tostring(R12.total_steps)
      .. " steps (reads only; zero writes) - R12 TOTAL STEPS 6 - YOU ARE DONE =====")
    return R12.step
  end
  R12.out("")
  R12.out("===== R12 STEP " .. tostring(R12.step) .. "/" .. tostring(R12.total_steps)
    .. " (t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. ") =====")
  local ok, err = pcall(fn)
  if not ok then
    R12.out("STEP " .. tostring(R12.step) .. " raised (swallowed): " .. truncate(err, 160))
  end
  return R12.step
end

function zz_probe_r12()
  R12.step = 0
  R12.done = false
  R12.roots = {}
  R12.children = {}
  R12.seeds = {}
  R12.located = {}
  R12.located_order = {}
  R12.located_list = {}
  R12.descend_count = 0
  R12.desc_seen = {}
  R12.rows = {}
  R12.ctx = {}
  R12.ctx_from = {}
  R12.selected_ui = nil
  R12.sel_tid = nil
  R12.sel_id = nil
  R12.gcv_calls = 0
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R12 READY (step 0 of 6). R12 TOTAL STEPS 6 - you are done after step 6."
    .. " In battle, open AND PIN the unit-info panel and keep the cards panel up with >=2 units,"
    .. " then call zz_probe_r12_step() ONE step at a time (after each step, if the game is alive,"
    .. " type the next). Step " .. tostring(R12.total_steps) .. " is the LAST step - stop there."
    .. " log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r12_step()
  if R12.step == 0 and (not R12.done) then
    R12.run_no = R12.run_no + 1
    R12.lines = 0
    R12.line_cap_spoken = false
    R12.out("")
    R12.out("===== ROUND 12 RUN #" .. tostring(R12.run_no)
      .. " (manual zz_probe_r12_step) t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. " =====")
    R12.out("R12 TOTAL STEPS 6 - you are done after step 6. Seed the descent on the NUMERIC"
      .. " unit-id nodes under unit_id_holder; descend to DEPTH " .. tostring(R12.descend_depth)
      .. " with a " .. tostring(R12.descend_visits) .. "-visit budget; pair the stat rows;"
      .. " read the CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit context ids; then run EXACTLY"
      .. " TWO common.get_context_value calls. Every native call is logged BEFORE it is made;"
      .. " ZERO SetContextObject; simhover DISARMED; the name-lookup helper is BANNED.")
  end
  local before = R12.step
  R12.advance()
  local nxt
  if R12.done or R12.step >= R12.total_steps or R12.steps[R12.step + 1] == nil then
    nxt = "DONE - STOP (zz_probe_r12 finished after " .. tostring(R12.total_steps) .. " steps)"
  else
    nxt = "step " .. tostring(R12.step + 1) .. " of " .. tostring(R12.total_steps)
  end
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R12 step " .. tostring(R12.step) .. "/" .. tostring(R12.total_steps)
    .. " done (was " .. tostring(before) .. "); next: " .. nxt
    .. " - call zz_probe_r12_step() again. log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r12_auto()
  if R12.step == 0 and (not R12.done) then zz_probe_r12() end
  R12.run_no = R12.run_no + 1
  R12.lines = 0
  R12.line_cap_spoken = false
  R12.out("")
  R12.out("===== ROUND 12 AUTO RUN #" .. tostring(R12.run_no) .. " t=" .. tostring(tick_count)
    .. " - runs every step to the cap; a fatal call dies here and the last R12 CALL names it =====")
  local guard = 0
  while (not R12.done) and guard < 40 do
    guard = guard + 1
    R12.advance()
  end
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R12 auto finished (step=" .. tostring(R12.step)
    .. (R12.done and ", done" or ", cap") .. "). log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r12_status()
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R12 TOTAL STEPS " .. tostring(R12.total_steps) .. " - run="
    .. tostring(R12.run_no) .. " step=" .. tostring(R12.step) .. "/" .. tostring(R12.total_steps)
    .. " done=" .. tostring(R12.done) .. " lines=" .. tostring(R12.lines)
    .. "/" .. tostring(R12.max_lines)
    .. " | roots=" .. tostring(#(R12.roots or {}))
    .. " seeds=" .. tostring(#(R12.seeds or {}))
    .. " descend_visits=" .. tostring(R12.descend_count) .. "/" .. tostring(R12.descend_visits)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(#(R12.located_order or {}))
    .. " rows=" .. tostring(#(R12.rows or {}))
    .. " ctx_ids=" .. tostring(R12.count_ctx())
    .. " gcv_calls=" .. tostring(R12.gcv_calls)
    .. " | zz_probe_r12() to start/restart; log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r12_help()
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R12 FINISH THE PANEL HUNT. R12 TOTAL STEPS 6 - you are done after step 6."
    .. " Start a battle, open AND PIN the unit-info panel, and keep the cards panel up with >=2"
    .. " units. Call zz_probe_r12() once, then zz_probe_r12_step() SIX times ("
    .. tostring(R12.total_steps) .. " total; STOP after step " .. tostring(R12.total_steps) .. ")."
    .. " Step 1 lists the top-level roots; step 2 lists unit_id_holder's children and keeps the"
    .. " NUMERIC unit-id nodes (1001, 1002, ...) as seeds; step 3 descends EVERY unit-id subtree to"
    .. " depth " .. tostring(R12.descend_depth) .. " (budget " .. tostring(R12.descend_visits)
    .. " visits), logging R12 DOWN path/id/children/stext for every node; step 4 locates the panel"
    .. " nodes (health_and_stats/dynamic_stats/template_stat/stat_name/value_holder/dy_value) and"
    .. " pairs every row (R12 PANEL row=.. name=.. value=..); step 5 reads GetContextObjectId for"
    .. " CcoUnitDetails/CcoUnitStat/CcoBattleUnit on the located rows (R12 CTXID); step 6 runs"
    .. " EXACTLY TWO common.get_context_value calls - ONE with the SELECTED unit's context id, ONE"
    .. " with a NON-selected unit's ui id (R12 QUERY sel=/nonsel=). zz_probe_r12_auto() runs every"
    .. " step to the cap. ZERO writes; simhover DISARMED; the name-lookup helper is BANNED. Log: "
    .. LOG_FILE
end

-- ============================================================================
-- 17. ROUND 13 - THE PANEL IS NOT UNDER unit_id_holder (THAT SUBTREE IS THE
--     ON-FIELD CARD). DESCEND **EVERY** TOP-LEVEL UI ROOT THAT HAS CHILDREN
--     (PRIORITY: hud_battle, panel_manager, under_advisor_docker, left, right,
--     tactical_hud, menu_bar, THEN THE REST) TO DEPTH 8 WITH A 1200-VISIT
--     BUDGET, AND MATCH COMPONENTS BY THE STABLE id PREFIX **CcoUnitStat**
--     (CASE-INSENSITIVE) AS WELL AS BY THE STRUCTURAL NAMES. PAIR THE STAT
--     ROWS, READ THE CONTEXT IDS, THEN ASK EXACTLY TWO get_context_value CALLS.
--
--     WHY. Round 12's step 3 seeded the descent on the NUMERIC unit-id nodes
--     under unit_id_holder and walked 532 of its 800 visits straight into the
--     ON-FIELD UNIT CARD (character_portrait_parent, icon_rank_holder, cat_docker,
--     icon_leadership, icon_threat, script_ping_parent) - ZERO stat-row nodes
--     (LOCATED: 0), no panel, no context id, no query. The round-4 marker says
--     the stat components answer to ids that START WITH CcoUnitStat (e.g.
--     CcoUnitStat5974452864 'how fast a unit moves') - a STABLE PREFIX the round-11
--     hint-substring hunt never tested. So round 13 stops guessing the owning
--     subtree and descends EVERY top-level root that has children instead, hunting
--     the CcoUnitStat PREFIX and the structural names together.
--
--     R13 TOTAL STEPS 7 - you are done after step 7.
--
--     THE PLAN (all READ-ONLY; ZERO SetContextObject; simhover DISARMED; the
--     engine's name-lookup helper is BANNED from this file; ONE armed console
--     step at a time, every native call logged BEFORE it is made):
--       STEP 1 - enumerate the UI root's top-level children; keep EVERY root WITH
--                children and order them by the priority list above.
--       STEP 2 - descend the PRIORITY roots to DEPTH 8 (drop into the shared
--                1200-visit budget), logging R13 DOWN path/id/children/stext/vfr
--                for every node, and R13 HIT for every CcoUnitStat-prefixed or
--                structural node.
--       STEP 3 - descend the REMAINING roots with children, continuing the same
--                1200-visit budget.
--       STEP 4 - locate the stat-row nodes and pair each row's stat_name with its
--                value_holder/dy_value (R13 PANEL row=N name=.. value=..).
--       STEP 5 - read GetContextObjectId(CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat /
--                CcoBattleUnit) on the located components (R13 CTXID; reads only).
--       STEP 6 - QUERY 1 of 2: common.get_context_value with the LOCATED context
--                id, field StatList.Size.
--       STEP 7 - QUERY 2 of 2: common.get_context_value with a NON-selected
--                unit's ui id AS TEXT (CcoBattleUnit), field DisplayedValue if
--                query 1 returned a value, else StatList.Size - so EXACTLY TWO
--                get_context_value calls run in total.
--       Only proven-safe primitives: ChildCount, Find, Id, Visible,
--       VisibleFromRoot, CurrentState, GetStateText, GetTooltipText,
--       GetContextObjectId.
-- ============================================================================

-- A GLOBAL table (not a local): the probe chunk already carries ~168 top-level
-- locals and Lua's 200-local ceiling is real - R13 must not spend one.
R13 = {
  run_no          = 0,
  step            = 0,          -- 0 = not started; +1 per armed step
  done            = false,
  total_steps     = 7,          -- R13 TOTAL STEPS 7 - you are done after step 7
  lines           = 0,
  max_lines       = 12000,      -- HARD CAP on R13 log lines (1200 visits + CALL lines)
  line_cap_spoken = false,
  -- hard enumeration budgets
  root_max        = 80,         -- top-level roots logged (step 1)
  child_max       = 80,         -- children scanned per node (steps 1/4)
  descend_visits  = 1200,       -- steps 2-3 TOTAL visits (shared)
  descend_depth   = 8,          -- steps 2-3 max depth FROM a top-level root
  locate_max      = 120,        -- most located (hit) components kept for step 4/5
  ctx_max         = 120,        -- most located components probed in step 5
  unit_id_max     = 40,         -- most numeric unit-id candidates kept
  -- the stable PREFIX every stat component id starts with (case-insensitive)
  stat_prefix     = "ccounitstat",
  -- the structural ids the hunt also matches (SUBSTRING match on a lowercased id)
  locate_names    = { "health_and_stats", "dynamic_stats", "template_stat",
                      "stat_name", "value_holder", "dy_value",
                      "row_header_stats", "stats_toggle" },
  -- the priority order the top-level roots are descended in
  priority        = { "hud_battle", "panel_manager", "under_advisor_docker",
                      "left", "right", "tactical_hud", "menu_bar" },
  -- step-1 output
  roots        = {},            -- { id, uic, children, rank, keep }
  prio_roots   = {},            -- priority-ordered roots WITH children
  rest_roots   = {},            -- the rest of the roots WITH children
  -- collected during the descent: numeric unit-id candidates (the on-field cards)
  unit_ids     = {},            -- { id, path }
  unit_ids_seen = {},           -- id -> true
  -- steps 2-3 output
  located       = {},           -- id -> first { id, uic, path, stext, tip }
  located_order = {},           -- ids in discovery order
  located_list  = {},           -- EVERY located (hit) node
  hit_count     = 0,
  descend_count = 0,
  desc_seen     = {},           -- component -> true (repeat/cycle guard)
  descent_begun = false,
  -- step-4 output
  rows         = {},            -- { n, name, value, rowid, path }
  -- step-5 output
  ctx_types    = { "CcoUnitDetails", "CcoUnitStat", "CcoBattleUnit" },
  ctx          = {},            -- type_id -> context id (non-nil, first kept)
  ctx_from     = {},            -- type_id -> path the id came from
  selected_ui  = nil,           -- the SELECTED unit's numeric ui id (from a path)
  sel_tid      = nil,           -- the type the located context id came from
  sel_id       = nil,           -- the located context id
  -- steps 6-7
  query_sel    = nil,           -- query 1's returned text (drives query 2's field)
  gcv_calls    = 0,
}

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- R13 logging
function R13.out(msg)
  if R13.lines >= R13.max_lines then
    if not R13.line_cap_spoken then
      R13.line_cap_spoken = true
      log("R13 line cap reached (" .. tostring(R13.max_lines) .. ") - further R13 lines are not logged")
    end
    return
  end
  R13.lines = R13.lines + 1
  log("R13 " .. tostring(msg))
end

-- ALWAYS call this IMMEDIATELY before a native call: it is the line that names
-- the fatal call if the engine dies on the next statement.
function R13.call(desc)
  R13.out("CALL " .. tostring(R13.step) .. " " .. tostring(desc))
end

function R13.read_text(fn)
  local ok, v = pcall(fn)
  if not ok then return "<ERR>" end
  if v == nil then return nil end
  local s = safe_text(v)
  if s ~= nil then return s end
  return "<opaque>"
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------- proven-shape primitives
function R13.ui_root()
  R13.call("core:get_ui_root()")
  local ok, r = pcall(function() return core:get_ui_root() end)
  if not ok or r == nil then return nil end
  return r
end

function R13.child_count(uic)
  if uic == nil then return 0 end
  local n = read1(function() return uic:ChildCount() end)
  if lua_type(n) == "number" then return n end
  return 0
end

-- uic:Find(i) -> a child, or nil. The result is TRUTHINESS-guarded (never wrap a
-- boolean: the round-9 crash).
function R13.child_at(uic, i)
  if uic == nil then return nil end
  local ok, raw = pcall(function() return uic:Find(i) end)
  if not ok or raw == nil or raw == false then return nil end
  return wrap(raw)
end

function R13.id_of(uic)
  if uic == nil then return nil end
  return R13.read_text(function() return uic:Id() end)
end

function R13.vis_of(uic)
  if uic == nil then return nil, nil end
  local vis = readb(function() return uic:Visible() end)
  local vfr = readb(function() return uic:VisibleFromRoot() end)
  return tostring(vis), tostring(vfr)
end

-- an id is a unit ui id when EVERY character is a digit
function R13.is_numeric(s)
  local str = safe_text(s)
  if str == nil or str == "" then return false end
  local len = string.len(str)
  for i = 1, len do
    local c = string.byte(str, i)
    if c == nil or c < 48 or c > 57 then return false end
  end
  return true
end

-- does the lowercased id START WITH CcoUnitStat (the round-4 stable prefix)?
function R13.is_prefix_id(id)
  local str = safe_text(id)
  if str == nil or str == "" then return false end
  local low = string.lower(str)
  local p = R13.stat_prefix
  if string.len(low) < string.len(p) then return false end
  return string.sub(low, 1, string.len(p)) == p
end

-- does the lowercased id CONTAIN one of the structural names?
function R13.is_struct_id(id)
  local str = safe_text(id)
  if str == nil or str == "" then return false end
  local low = string.lower(str)
  for i = 1, #R13.locate_names do
    if contains_str(low, R13.locate_names[i]) then return true end
  end
  return false
end

-- a HIT is either a CcoUnitStat-prefixed id OR a structural name
function R13.is_hit_id(id)
  return R13.is_prefix_id(id) or R13.is_struct_id(id)
end

function R13.is_priority_id(id)
  local str = safe_text(id)
  if str == nil then return false end
  for i = 1, #R13.priority do
    if str == R13.priority[i] then return true end
  end
  return false
end

function R13.rank_of(id)
  local str = safe_text(id)
  if str == nil then return 100 end
  for i = 1, #R13.priority do
    if str == R13.priority[i] then return i end
  end
  return 100
end

function R13.count_ctx()
  local n = 0
  for _ in pairs(R13.ctx) do n = n + 1 end
  return n
end

-- the FIRST all-digit segment of a /-path (plain byte scans; no string.find)
function R13.first_numeric_segment(s)
  local str = safe_text(s)
  if str == nil then return nil end
  local len = string.len(str)
  local start = 1
  local i = 1
  while i <= len + 1 do
    local ch = (i <= len) and string.sub(str, i, i) or "/"
    if ch == "/" then
      if i > start then
        local seg = string.sub(str, start, i - 1)
        if R13.is_numeric(seg) then return seg end
      end
      start = i + 1
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  return nil
end

function R13.ids_join(list)
  local parts = {}
  for i = 1, #list do
    parts[#parts + 1] = tostring(list[i].id)
  end
  return table.concat(parts, ",")
end

-- record a numeric unit-id candidate (the on-field cards), de-duped by id
function R13.note_unit_id(id, path)
  local str = safe_text(id)
  if str == nil or str == "" then return end
  if R13.unit_ids_seen[str] ~= nil then return end
  if #R13.unit_ids >= R13.unit_id_max then return end
  R13.unit_ids_seen[str] = true
  R13.unit_ids[#R13.unit_ids + 1] = { id = str, path = path }
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the descent
-- Descend one root subtree to R13.descend_depth, charging the SHARED budget.
-- Paths are RELATIVE to the top-level root (root = depth 1).
function R13.descend(uic, path, depth)
  if uic == nil then return end
  if R13.descend_count >= R13.descend_visits then return end
  if depth > R13.descend_depth then return end
  -- repeat / cycle guard keyed on the COMPONENT (paths collide when sibling ids
  -- repeat - e.g. every stat row is id "template_stat")
  if R13.desc_seen[uic] ~= nil then return end
  R13.desc_seen[uic] = true
  R13.descend_count = R13.descend_count + 1
  local id = R13.id_of(uic)
  R13.call("DOWN " .. q(path) .. ":ChildCount()")
  local cn = R13.child_count(uic)
  R13.call("DOWN " .. q(path) .. ":GetStateText/CurrentState/Visible/VisibleFromRoot")
  local st = R13.read_text(function() return uic:GetStateText() end)
  local cs = R13.read_text(function() return uic:CurrentState() end)
  local vis, vfr = R13.vis_of(uic)
  R13.out("DOWN path=" .. q(path) .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " children=" .. tostring(cn)
    .. " stext=" .. q(st) .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr) .. " vis=" .. tostring(vis)
    .. " state=" .. q(cs))
  -- a numeric id is a unit card's ui id (kept as a NON-selected query candidate)
  if id ~= nil and R13.is_numeric(id) then R13.note_unit_id(id, path) end
  -- a HIT: CcoUnitStat prefix OR a structural name
  if id ~= nil and R13.is_hit_id(id) then
    R13.call("HIT " .. q(path) .. ":GetTooltipText()")
    local tip = R13.read_text(function() return uic:GetTooltipText() end)
    R13.hit_count = R13.hit_count + 1
    R13.out("HIT path=" .. q(path) .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " stext=" .. q(st) .. " tip=" .. q(tip))
    if #R13.located_list < R13.locate_max then
      local rec = { id = id, uic = uic, path = path, stext = st, tip = tip }
      R13.located_list[#R13.located_list + 1] = rec
      if R13.located[id] == nil then
        R13.located[id] = rec
        R13.located_order[#R13.located_order + 1] = id
      end
    end
  end
  if depth >= R13.descend_depth then return end
  for i = 0, cn - 1 do
    if R13.descend_count >= R13.descend_visits then return end
    R13.call("DOWN " .. q(path) .. ":Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ")")
    local ch = R13.child_at(uic, i)
    if ch ~= nil then
      local cid = R13.id_of(ch)
      if cid == nil or cid == "" then cid = "#" .. tostring(i) end
      R13.descend(ch, path .. "/" .. cid, depth + 1)
    end
  end
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the steps
R13.steps = {}

-- STEP 1 - enumerate the UI root's top-level children; keep EVERY root WITH
-- children, ordered by the priority list.
R13.steps[1] = function()
  R13.out("STEP 1 - enumerate the UI root's top-level children; keep every root WITH"
    .. " children, priority-ordered (budget " .. tostring(R13.root_max) .. ")")
  local root = R13.ui_root()
  if root == nil then
    R13.out("STEP 1 aborted: core:get_ui_root() returned nil")
    return
  end
  local n = R13.child_count(root)
  R13.out("ROOTCOUNT " .. tostring(n))
  if n <= 0 then
    R13.out("STEP 1: the UI root has no children yet (battle not up?)")
    return
  end
  R13.roots = {}
  R13.unit_ids = {}
  R13.unit_ids_seen = {}
  local lim = n
  if lim > R13.root_max then lim = R13.root_max end
  for i = 0, lim - 1 do
    R13.call("ui_root:Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ") + Id/ChildCount/Visible/VisibleFromRoot")
    local uic = R13.child_at(root, i)
    local id = R13.id_of(uic)
    local vis, vfr = R13.vis_of(uic)
    local cn = R13.child_count(uic)
    local rank = R13.rank_of(id)
    local keep = (cn > 0 and uic ~= nil)
    R13.out("ROOT " .. tostring(i) .. " id=" .. q(id) .. " vis=" .. tostring(vis)
      .. " vfr=" .. tostring(vfr) .. " children=" .. tostring(cn)
      .. " rank=" .. tostring(rank) .. " keep=" .. tostring(keep))
    R13.roots[#R13.roots + 1] = { uic = uic, id = id, children = cn, rank = rank, keep = keep }
  end
  if n > lim then
    R13.out("ROOT ... (" .. tostring(n - lim) .. " more root(s) not listed; cap "
      .. tostring(R13.root_max) .. ")")
  end
  -- the DESCEND PLAN: priority roots first (in the listed order), then the rest
  R13.prio_roots = {}
  for k = 1, #R13.priority do
    for j = 1, #R13.roots do
      local r = R13.roots[j]
      if r.keep and safe_text(r.id) == R13.priority[k] then
        R13.prio_roots[#R13.prio_roots + 1] = r
        break
      end
    end
  end
  R13.rest_roots = {}
  for j = 1, #R13.roots do
    local r = R13.roots[j]
    if r.keep and not R13.is_priority_id(r.id) then
      R13.rest_roots[#R13.rest_roots + 1] = r
    end
  end
  -- keep a NON-selected unit-id candidate even if the budget never reaches
  -- unit_id_holder: scan that root's DIRECT children for numeric ids (reads only)
  for j = 1, #R13.roots do
    local r = R13.roots[j]
    if r.uic ~= nil and r.id ~= nil and contains_str(string.lower(tostring(r.id)), "unit_id_holder") then
      local cn = R13.child_count(r.uic)
      local clim = cn
      if clim > R13.child_max then clim = R13.child_max end
      for c = 0, clim - 1 do
        R13.call("unit_id_holder:Find(" .. tostring(c) .. ") + Id")
        local ch = R13.child_at(r.uic, c)
        local cid = R13.id_of(ch)
        if cid ~= nil and R13.is_numeric(cid) then R13.note_unit_id(cid, "unit_id_holder/" .. tostring(cid)) end
      end
      break
    end
  end
  R13.out("DESCEND PLAN prio=" .. tostring(#R13.prio_roots) .. " : " .. R13.ids_join(R13.prio_roots))
  R13.out("DESCEND PLAN rest=" .. tostring(#R13.rest_roots) .. " : " .. R13.ids_join(R13.rest_roots))
  R13.out("STEP 1 done: roots=" .. tostring(#R13.roots) .. " with_children="
    .. tostring(#R13.prio_roots + #R13.rest_roots) .. " unit_id_candidates="
    .. tostring(#R13.unit_ids))
end

-- STEP 2 - descend the PRIORITY roots (the shared budget begins here).
R13.steps[2] = function()
  R13.out("STEP 2 - descend the PRIORITY roots (" .. tostring(#R13.prio_roots)
    .. ") to depth " .. tostring(R13.descend_depth) .. ", budget "
    .. tostring(R13.descend_visits) .. " visits (shared with step 3)")
  R13.located = {}
  R13.located_order = {}
  R13.located_list = {}
  R13.hit_count = 0
  R13.descend_count = 0
  R13.desc_seen = {}
  if #R13.prio_roots == 0 then
    R13.out("STEP 2: no PRIORITY root has any children - step 3 covers the rest")
  end
  for k = 1, #R13.prio_roots do
    local r = R13.prio_roots[k]
    if R13.descend_count >= R13.descend_visits then
      R13.out("STEP 2: budget exhausted before root " .. q(r.id))
      break
    end
    R13.out("STEP 2 root " .. tostring(k) .. " id=" .. q(r.id)
      .. " children=" .. tostring(r.children) .. " (visits so far "
      .. tostring(R13.descend_count) .. ")")
    R13.descend(r.uic, tostring(r.id), 1)
  end
  R13.descent_begun = true
  R13.out("STEP 2 done: visits=" .. tostring(R13.descend_count) .. "/"
    .. tostring(R13.descend_visits) .. " hits=" .. tostring(R13.hit_count)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(#R13.located_order))
end

-- STEP 3 - descend the REMAINING roots with children (same shared budget).
R13.steps[3] = function()
  R13.out("STEP 3 - descend the REMAINING roots with children (" .. tostring(#R13.rest_roots)
    .. "), continuing the " .. tostring(R13.descend_visits)
    .. "-visit budget (used so far " .. tostring(R13.descend_count) .. ")")
  if not R13.descent_begun then
    R13.located = {}
    R13.located_order = {}
    R13.located_list = {}
    R13.hit_count = 0
    R13.descend_count = 0
    R13.desc_seen = {}
  end
  if #R13.rest_roots == 0 then
    R13.out("STEP 3: no further root with children was listed by step 1")
  end
  for k = 1, #R13.rest_roots do
    local r = R13.rest_roots[k]
    if R13.descend_count >= R13.descend_visits then
      R13.out("STEP 3: budget exhausted before root " .. q(r.id))
      break
    end
    R13.out("STEP 3 root " .. tostring(k) .. " id=" .. q(r.id)
      .. " children=" .. tostring(r.children) .. " (visits so far "
      .. tostring(R13.descend_count) .. ")")
    R13.descend(r.uic, tostring(r.id), 1)
  end
  R13.out("STEP 3 done: visits=" .. tostring(R13.descend_count) .. "/"
    .. tostring(R13.descend_visits) .. " hits=" .. tostring(R13.hit_count)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(#R13.located_order))
end

-- STEP 4 - log every located (hit) component and pair each stat ROW's stat_name
-- with its value_holder/dy_value. A row is a template_stat OR a CcoUnitStat* node.
R13.steps[4] = function()
  R13.out("STEP 4 - locate the stat rows and pair each row's name with its value")
  R13.rows = {}
  if R13.located_order == nil or #R13.located_order == 0 then
    R13.out("STEP 4: the descent located NO HIT (no CcoUnitStat prefix and no"
      .. " structural id). Grep the DOWN lines - the panel may sit deeper than depth "
      .. tostring(R13.descend_depth) .. " or under a root step 1 skipped")
  end
  for k = 1, #(R13.located_order or {}) do
    local id = R13.located_order[k]
    local rec = R13.located[id]
    if rec ~= nil then
      R13.out("LOCATED path=" .. q(rec.path) .. " id=" .. q(id)
        .. " children=" .. tostring(R13.child_count(rec.uic)))
    end
  end
  -- find a child of `uic` whose Id() == want (bounded by child_max)
  local function child_named(uic, want)
    if uic == nil then return nil end
    local cn = R13.child_count(uic)
    local lim = cn
    if lim > R13.child_max then lim = R13.child_max end
    for i = 0, lim - 1 do
      R13.call("child " .. q(want) .. " under " .. q(R13.id_of(uic)) .. ":Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ")")
      local ch = R13.child_at(uic, i)
      if ch ~= nil and R13.id_of(ch) == want then return ch end
    end
    return nil
  end
  local function read_row(row_uic, n, row_path, row_id)
    local sn = child_named(row_uic, "stat_name")
    local vh = child_named(row_uic, "value_holder")
    local dv = nil
    if vh ~= nil then dv = child_named(vh, "dy_value") end
    if dv == nil then dv = child_named(row_uic, "dy_value") end
    local name_text, val_text = nil, nil
    if sn ~= nil then
      R13.call("stat_name:GetStateText()")
      name_text = R13.read_text(function() return sn:GetStateText() end)
    end
    if dv ~= nil then
      R13.call("dy_value:GetStateText()")
      val_text = R13.read_text(function() return dv:GetStateText() end)
    end
    R13.out("PANEL row=" .. tostring(n) .. " name=" .. q(name_text) .. " value=" .. q(val_text)
      .. " path=" .. q(row_path) .. " rowid=" .. q(row_id))
    if R13.is_prefix_id(row_id) then
      R13.out("ROWCTX " .. q(row_path) .. " prefix=CcoUnitStat id=" .. q(row_id))
    end
    R13.rows[#R13.rows + 1] = { n = n, name = name_text, value = val_text,
                                rowid = row_id, uic = row_uic, path = row_path }
  end
  -- every located template_stat OR CcoUnitStat* node is one stat row
  local n = 0
  for k = 1, #(R13.located_list or {}) do
    local rec = R13.located_list[k]
    if rec.id == "template_stat" or R13.is_prefix_id(rec.id) then
      n = n + 1
      read_row(rec.uic, n, rec.path, rec.id)
    end
  end
  -- fallback: a located dynamic_stats whose template_stat children were not
  -- themselves located (defensive; the descent normally visits them)
  if n == 0 then
    local ds = R13.located["dynamic_stats"]
    if ds ~= nil then
      local cn = R13.child_count(ds.uic)
      local lim = cn
      if lim > R13.child_max then lim = R13.child_max end
      for i = 0, lim - 1 do
        R13.call("dynamic_stats:Find(" .. tostring(i) .. ") looking for template_stat")
        local ch = R13.child_at(ds.uic, i)
        if ch ~= nil and (R13.id_of(ch) == "template_stat" or R13.is_prefix_id(R13.id_of(ch))) then
          n = n + 1
          read_row(ch, n, ds.path .. "/" .. tostring(R13.id_of(ch)), R13.id_of(ch))
        end
      end
    end
  end
  -- fallback: a lone located stat_name (+ a located dy_value, if any)
  if n == 0 and R13.located["stat_name"] ~= nil then
    R13.call("stat_name:GetStateText()")
    local t = R13.read_text(function() return R13.located["stat_name"].uic:GetStateText() end)
    local v = nil
    local dv = R13.located["dy_value"]
    if dv ~= nil then
      R13.call("dy_value:GetStateText()")
      v = R13.read_text(function() return dv.uic:GetStateText() end)
    end
    n = n + 1
    R13.out("PANEL row=" .. tostring(n) .. " name=" .. q(t) .. " value=" .. q(v)
      .. " path=" .. q(R13.located["stat_name"].path) .. " rowid=" .. q("stat_name"))
    R13.rows[#R13.rows + 1] = { n = n, name = t, value = v, rowid = "stat_name" }
  end
  R13.out("STEP 4 done: hits=" .. tostring(R13.hit_count) .. " rows=" .. tostring(#R13.rows)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(#(R13.located_order or {})))
end

-- STEP 5 - read GetContextObjectId (CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit)
-- on the located components (READS only).
R13.steps[5] = function()
  R13.out("STEP 5 - read GetContextObjectId on the located components (reads only)")
  R13.ctx = {}
  R13.ctx_from = {}
  R13.selected_ui = nil
  R13.sel_tid = nil
  R13.sel_id = nil
  if R13.located_list == nil or #R13.located_list == 0 then
    R13.out("STEP 5: nothing was located - no context id to read")
    return
  end
  local probed = 0
  for k = 1, #R13.located_list do
    if probed >= R13.ctx_max then break end
    local rec = R13.located_list[k]
    probed = probed + 1
    for t = 1, #R13.ctx_types do
      local tid = R13.ctx_types[t]
      R13.call(q(rec.path) .. " GetContextObjectId(" .. tid .. ")")
      local ok, raw = pcall(function() return rec.uic:GetContextObjectId(tid) end)
      local text = nil
      if ok then text = safe_text(raw) end
      R13.out("CTXID " .. q(rec.path) .. " " .. tid .. " -> " .. (ok and q(text) or "<ERR>"))
      if ok and text ~= nil and text ~= "" and R13.ctx[tid] == nil then
        R13.ctx[tid] = text
        R13.ctx_from[tid] = rec.path
      end
    end
  end
  -- the located context id = the first non-nil one (a read off a hit component)
  for i = 1, #R13.ctx_types do
    local tid = R13.ctx_types[i]
    if R13.ctx[tid] ~= nil then R13.sel_tid = tid; R13.sel_id = R13.ctx[tid]; break end
  end
  if R13.sel_tid == nil then
    R13.out("STEP 5: NO context id came back (all nil) - the query steps make no call")
    return
  end
  -- the SELECTED unit's ui id = the FIRST numeric segment of the path the located
  -- context id came from (recorded data only - no new read)
  local from = R13.ctx_from[R13.sel_tid]
  if from ~= nil then R13.selected_ui = R13.first_numeric_segment(from) end
  R13.out("STEP 5 done: ctx_ids=" .. tostring(R13.count_ctx()) .. " selected_type="
    .. tostring(R13.sel_tid) .. " selected_id=" .. q(R13.sel_id)
    .. " selected_ui=" .. q(R13.selected_ui))
end

-- STEP 6 - QUERY 1 of 2: the LOCATED context id, field StatList.Size.
R13.steps[6] = function()
  R13.out("STEP 6 - QUERY 1 of 2: the LOCATED context id (vanilla shape, field StatList.Size)")
  R13.gcv_calls = 0
  R13.query_sel = nil
  if R13.sel_tid == nil or R13.sel_id == nil then
    R13.out("STEP 6: no context id came out of step 5 - query 1 is skipped (0 calls so far)")
    return
  end
  local field = "StatList.Size"
  R13.call("common.get_context_value(" .. R13.sel_tid .. ", " .. q(R13.sel_id) .. ", " .. q(field) .. ")")
  local ok1, v1 = pcall(function() return common.get_context_value(R13.sel_tid, R13.sel_id, field) end)
  R13.gcv_calls = R13.gcv_calls + 1
  local t1 = ok1 and text_of(v1, true) or "<ERR>"
  if t1 == nil then t1 = "<nil>" end
  if ok1 and v1 ~= nil then R13.query_sel = t1 end
  R13.out("QUERY sel=" .. q(R13.sel_id) .. " type=" .. R13.sel_tid .. " field=" .. field
    .. " -> " .. q(t1) .. " (from " .. tostring(R13.ctx_from[R13.sel_tid]) .. ")")
  R13.out("STEP 6 done: get_context_value calls=" .. tostring(R13.gcv_calls) .. " (want 2 total)")
end

-- STEP 7 - QUERY 2 of 2: a NON-selected unit's ui id AS TEXT (CcoBattleUnit),
-- field DisplayedValue if query 1 returned a value, else StatList.Size.
R13.steps[7] = function()
  R13.out("STEP 7 - QUERY 2 of 2: a NON-selected unit's ui id as text (field"
    .. " DisplayedValue if query 1 returned, else StatList.Size)")
  if R13.sel_id == nil then
    R13.out("STEP 7: no context id came out of step 5 - query 2 is skipped,"
      .. " get_context_value calls=" .. tostring(R13.gcv_calls) .. " (want 2)")
    return
  end
  local nonsel = nil
  for i = 1, #(R13.unit_ids or {}) do
    local u = R13.unit_ids[i]
    if u.id ~= nil and tostring(u.id) ~= tostring(R13.selected_ui) then
      nonsel = tostring(u.id)
      break
    end
  end
  if nonsel == nil then
    R13.out("QUERY nonsel: no NON-selected unit ui id was collected (keep the"
      .. " cards panel up with >=2 units) - query 2 skipped, calls="
      .. tostring(R13.gcv_calls) .. " (want 2)")
    return
  end
  local returned = (R13.query_sel ~= nil and R13.query_sel ~= "<nil>" and R13.query_sel ~= "<ERR>")
  local field = returned and "DisplayedValue" or "StatList.Size"
  R13.out("QUERY nonsel unit ui id=" .. q(nonsel) .. " (selected_ui=" .. q(R13.selected_ui)
    .. ") field=" .. field)
  R13.call("common.get_context_value(\"CcoBattleUnit\", " .. q(nonsel) .. ", " .. q(field) .. ")")
  local ok2, v2 = pcall(function() return common.get_context_value("CcoBattleUnit", nonsel, field) end)
  R13.gcv_calls = R13.gcv_calls + 1
  local t2 = ok2 and text_of(v2, true) or "<ERR>"
  if t2 == nil then t2 = "<nil>" end
  R13.out("QUERY nonsel=" .. q(nonsel) .. " type=CcoBattleUnit field=" .. field .. " -> " .. q(t2))
  R13.out("STEP 7 done: get_context_value calls=" .. tostring(R13.gcv_calls) .. " (want 2)")
end

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the driver
function R13.advance()
  if R13.done then
    R13.out("step ignored: the run is done (" .. tostring(R13.total_steps)
      .. " steps) - zz_probe_r13() restarts it")
    return R13.step
  end
  R13.step = R13.step + 1
  local fn = R13.steps[R13.step]
  if fn == nil then
    R13.done = true
    R13.out("===== ROUND 13 RUN done after " .. tostring(R13.total_steps)
      .. " steps (reads only; zero writes) - R13 TOTAL STEPS 7 - YOU ARE DONE =====")
    return R13.step
  end
  R13.out("")
  R13.out("===== R13 STEP " .. tostring(R13.step) .. "/" .. tostring(R13.total_steps)
    .. " (t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. ") =====")
  local ok, err = pcall(fn)
  if not ok then
    R13.out("STEP " .. tostring(R13.step) .. " raised (swallowed): " .. truncate(err, 160))
  end
  return R13.step
end

function zz_probe_r13()
  R13.step = 0
  R13.done = false
  R13.roots = {}
  R13.prio_roots = {}
  R13.rest_roots = {}
  R13.unit_ids = {}
  R13.unit_ids_seen = {}
  R13.located = {}
  R13.located_order = {}
  R13.located_list = {}
  R13.hit_count = 0
  R13.descend_count = 0
  R13.desc_seen = {}
  R13.descent_begun = false
  R13.rows = {}
  R13.ctx = {}
  R13.ctx_from = {}
  R13.selected_ui = nil
  R13.sel_tid = nil
  R13.sel_id = nil
  R13.query_sel = nil
  R13.gcv_calls = 0
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R13 READY (step 0 of 7). R13 TOTAL STEPS 7 - you are done after step 7."
    .. " In battle, open AND PIN the unit-info panel and keep the cards panel up with >=2 units,"
    .. " then call zz_probe_r13_step() ONE step at a time (after each step, if the game is alive,"
    .. " type the next). Step 7 is the LAST step - stop there. log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r13_step()
  if R13.step == 0 and (not R13.done) then
    R13.run_no = R13.run_no + 1
    R13.lines = 0
    R13.line_cap_spoken = false
    R13.out("")
    R13.out("===== ROUND 13 RUN #" .. tostring(R13.run_no)
      .. " (manual zz_probe_r13_step) t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. " =====")
    R13.out("R13 TOTAL STEPS 7 - you are done after step 7. Descend EVERY top-level root"
      .. " that has children (priority: hud_battle, panel_manager, under_advisor_docker,"
      .. " left, right, tactical_hud, menu_bar, then the rest) to DEPTH "
      .. tostring(R13.descend_depth) .. " with a " .. tostring(R13.descend_visits)
      .. "-visit budget; match the CcoUnitStat* PREFIX (case-insensitive) AND the structural"
      .. " names; pair the stat rows; read the CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit"
      .. " context ids; then run EXACTLY TWO common.get_context_value calls (the located id,"
      .. " then a NON-selected unit's ui id as text). Every native call is logged BEFORE it is"
      .. " made; ZERO SetContextObject; simhover DISARMED; the name-lookup helper is BANNED.")
  end
  local before = R13.step
  R13.advance()
  local nxt
  if R13.done or R13.step >= R13.total_steps or R13.steps[R13.step + 1] == nil then
    nxt = "DONE - STOP (zz_probe_r13 finished after " .. tostring(R13.total_steps) .. " steps)"
  else
    nxt = "step " .. tostring(R13.step + 1) .. " of " .. tostring(R13.total_steps)
  end
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R13 step " .. tostring(R13.step) .. "/" .. tostring(R13.total_steps)
    .. " done (was " .. tostring(before) .. "); next: " .. nxt
    .. " - call zz_probe_r13_step() again. log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r13_auto()
  if R13.step == 0 and (not R13.done) then zz_probe_r13() end
  R13.run_no = R13.run_no + 1
  R13.lines = 0
  R13.line_cap_spoken = false
  R13.out("")
  R13.out("===== ROUND 13 AUTO RUN #" .. tostring(R13.run_no) .. " t=" .. tostring(tick_count)
    .. " - runs every step to the cap; a fatal call dies here and the last R13 CALL names it =====")
  local guard = 0
  while (not R13.done) and guard < 40 do
    guard = guard + 1
    R13.advance()
  end
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R13 auto finished (step=" .. tostring(R13.step)
    .. (R13.done and ", done" or ", cap") .. "). log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r13_status()
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R13 TOTAL STEPS " .. tostring(R13.total_steps) .. " - run="
    .. tostring(R13.run_no) .. " step=" .. tostring(R13.step) .. "/" .. tostring(R13.total_steps)
    .. " done=" .. tostring(R13.done) .. " lines=" .. tostring(R13.lines)
    .. "/" .. tostring(R13.max_lines)
    .. " | roots=" .. tostring(#(R13.roots or {}))
    .. " prio=" .. tostring(#(R13.prio_roots or {}))
    .. " rest=" .. tostring(#(R13.rest_roots or {}))
    .. " unit_ids=" .. tostring(#(R13.unit_ids or {}))
    .. " descend_visits=" .. tostring(R13.descend_count) .. "/" .. tostring(R13.descend_visits)
    .. " hits=" .. tostring(R13.hit_count)
    .. " located=" .. tostring(#(R13.located_order or {}))
    .. " rows=" .. tostring(#(R13.rows or {}))
    .. " ctx_ids=" .. tostring(R13.count_ctx())
    .. " gcv_calls=" .. tostring(R13.gcv_calls)
    .. " | zz_probe_r13() to start/restart; log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_r13_help()
  return PROBE_TAG .. "R13 DESCEND EVERY ROOT. R13 TOTAL STEPS 7 - you are done after step 7."
    .. " Start a battle, open AND PIN the unit-info panel, and keep the cards panel up with"
    .. " >=2 units. Call zz_probe_r13() once, then zz_probe_r13_step() SEVEN times ("
    .. tostring(R13.total_steps) .. " total; STOP after step " .. tostring(R13.total_steps) .. ")."
    .. " Step 1 enumerates every top-level root and keeps the ones WITH children, priority-ordered"
    .. " (hud_battle, panel_manager, under_advisor_docker, left, right, tactical_hud, menu_bar,"
    .. " then the rest); step 2 descends the priority roots to depth " .. tostring(R13.descend_depth)
    .. " (budget " .. tostring(R13.descend_visits) .. " visits), logging R13 DOWN"
    .. " path/id/children/stext/vfr for every node and R13 HIT for every CcoUnitStat*-prefixed or"
    .. " structural node; step 3 descends the remaining roots with children; step 4 pairs the rows"
    .. " (R13 PANEL row=N name=.. value=..); step 5 reads GetContextObjectId"
    .. " (CcoUnitDetails/CcoUnitStat/CcoBattleUnit) on the located components (R13 CTXID); steps"
    .. " 6-7 run EXACTLY TWO common.get_context_value calls - query 1 with the LOCATED context id"
    .. " (field StatList.Size), query 2 with a NON-selected unit's ui id as text (CcoBattleUnit,"
    .. " field DisplayedValue if query 1 returned, else StatList.Size) (R13 QUERY sel=/nonsel=)."
    .. " zz_probe_r13_auto() runs every step to the cap. ZERO writes; simhover DISARMED; the"
    .. " name-lookup helper is BANNED. Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

-- ============================================================================
-- 8. WINDOW LIFECYCLE + THE POLL (mouse-armed primary, no auto windows, manual)

-- ============================================================================

local function start_window(why, seconds, hover_id, hover_reason, hover_addr)
	window_index = window_index + 1
	window_active = true
	window_why = why
	window_hover_id = hover_id
	window_hover_reason = hover_reason
	window_arm_addr = hover_addr
	window_ends_tick = tick_count + math.floor((seconds * 1000) / POLL_MS)
	window_header_pending = true
	cap_spoken = false
	polls_in_window = 0
	lines_in_window = 0
	mouse_off_tick = nil
	log("---- capture window " .. tostring(window_index) .. " armed (" .. tostring(why) .. ")"
		.. (hover_id ~= nil and (", hover=" .. q(hover_id)) or "")
		.. ", " .. tostring(seconds) .. " s -> ends at tick " .. tostring(window_ends_tick)
		.. " ----")
end

local function end_window()
	window_active = false
	log("---- capture window " .. tostring(window_index) .. " (" .. tostring(window_why)
		.. ") ended at t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. ": " .. tostring(polls_in_window)
		.. " poll(s) with content, " .. tostring(lines_in_window) .. " log line(s) ----")
	log("---- window closed - a hover still arms a " .. tostring(MOUSE_SECONDS)
		.. " s capture; manual re-run: zz_probe_ui_arm(60) BEFORE hovering ----")
end

-- A battle is running when the engine says it is in the conflict phase, or (the
-- deployment fallback) hud_battle is already populated with children.
local function battle_started()
	local ok, conflict = pcall(function() return bm:is_conflict_phase() end)
	if ok and conflict == true then return true end
	local hud = find_by_name(DEFAULT_ROOT)
	if hud ~= nil then
		local n = read1(function() return hud:ChildCount() end)
		if lua_type(n) == "number" and n > 0 then return true end
	end
	return false
end

local function zz_probe_ui_tick()
	local ok, err = pcall(function()
		tick_count = tick_count + 1

		-- close a finished window
		if window_active and tick_count >= window_ends_tick then
			end_window()
		end

		-- a MouseOff on the arming card closes the MOUSE window early, after a
		-- short grace so the tooltip's first poll always lands
		if window_active and window_why == "mouse" and mouse_off_tick ~= nil
			and (tick_count - mouse_off_tick) >= MOUSE_OFF_GRACE_TICKS then
			end_window()
		end

		-- a manual arm request (console hook) is honoured first
		if not window_active and manual_arm_seconds ~= nil then
			local s = manual_arm_seconds
			manual_arm_seconds = nil
			manual_windows_started = manual_windows_started + 1
			start_window("manual", s, "manual", "console arm", nil)
		end

		-- the MOUSE arm: a hover landed on a card (recorded by the listener).
		-- A pending arm is consumed either way, so it can never fire late.
		if mouse_arm_pending then
			mouse_arm_pending = false
			if not window_active then
				if mouse_captures_started < MAX_MOUSE_CAPTURES then
					mouse_captures_started = mouse_captures_started + 1
					start_window("mouse", MOUSE_SECONDS, mouse_arm_id, mouse_arm_reason, mouse_arm_addr)
				elseif not mouse_cap_spoken then
					mouse_cap_spoken = true
					log("---- mouse capture cap reached (" .. tostring(MAX_MOUSE_CAPTURES)
						.. ") - no more hover captures; manual: zz_probe_ui_arm(seconds) ----")
				end
			end
		end

		-- ROUND 7: no automatic windows here - the mouse arm above and the
		-- manual hook are the only window sources.

		-- outside a window, keep the card reporters fresh (a light sweep)
		if not window_active and (tick_count % PANEL_SWEEP_TICKS) == 0 then
			pcall(arm_panel_reporters)
		end

		-- ROUND 4: the targeted stat watch + automatic full dump. It runs
		-- OUTSIDE capture windows too, because the pinned unit-details panel is
		-- the normal trigger and needs no mouse. A non-empty visible-stat set
		-- that CHANGES since the last scan fires ONE full dump; a change of the
		-- set (a different stat became visible) re-dumps.
		if (tick_count % STAT_WATCH_EVERY) == 0 then
			local ok_scan, sig = pcall(stat_watch_scan)
			if ok_scan and sig ~= nil then
				r5.sig_now = sig   -- ROUND 5: the stat panel's visibility tell
				r6.sig_now = sig   -- ROUND 6: its own copy of the same tell
				if sig ~= stat_visible_sig then
					stat_visible_sig = sig
					if sig ~= "" then
						pcall(stat_do_dump,
							"auto: visible stat set changed, sig=[" .. tostring(sig) .. "]",
							stat_scan_seeds, stat_scan_cards)
					end
				end
			end
		end

		-- ROUND 5: advance a queued experiment run. Each stage performs ONE
		-- bounded action per tick and logs every write IMMEDIATELY BEFORE it
		-- happens. A run only ever starts when the stat panel is visible.
		if r5.active and tick_count >= r5.next_at then
			pcall(r5_step)
		end

		-- ROUND 5 auto trigger: the stat panel first became visible (the
		-- visible-stat signature carries dynamic_stats) -> queue ONE automatic
		-- run; the manual hooks can still queue more (all cap-limited).
		if (not r5.active) and (not r5.auto_done)
			and r5.sig_now ~= nil and contains_str(r5.sig_now, "dynamic_stats") then
			if r5.auto_attempts < R5.auto_attempts then
				r5.auto_attempts = r5.auto_attempts + 1
				local ok_start, started = pcall(r5_start, "auto", "full")
				if not ok_start or not started then
					r5.auto_done = true   -- refused (e.g. the run cap): never re-queue automatically
				end
			else
				r5.auto_done = true
				r5_out("auto: the stat panel is visible but the automatic-run attempts ("
					.. tostring(R5.auto_attempts) .. ") are spent - manual: zz_probe_r5()")
			end
		end

		-- ROUND 6: the ONE-write-per-pass context ladder. Pass 1 arms itself
		-- ONCE when the stat panel becomes visible; every later pass needs the
		-- console (zz_probe_r6_next()). A pass in flight performs exactly one
		-- write, then settles, then stops - it never auto-advances.
		if (not r6.done) and (not r6.auto_done) and (not r6.active)
			and r6.armed_pass == 0 and (not r5.active)
			and r6.sig_now ~= nil and contains_str(r6.sig_now, R6.target_name) then
			r6.auto_attempts = r6.auto_attempts + 1
			R6.arm(1, "auto")
		end
		if (not r6.active) and r6.armed_pass ~= 0 then
			pcall(R6.try_begin)
		end
		if r6.active and tick_count >= r6.next_at then
			pcall(R6.step)
		end

		-- ROUND 7: the zero-write read experiment. A bounded sweep every
		-- R7.every ticks while the stat panel is visible (or during a hover
		-- capture): both cards' CcoBattleUnit fields via common.get_context_value
		-- + the panel's compared rows. All reads, change-only, ZERO writes.
		if (tick_count % R7.every) == 0 then
			pcall(r7_tick_sweep)
		end

		-- ROUND 9: ONE automatic name-lookup + context read run, as soon as the
		-- stat panel (dynamic_stats) is seen visible. READ ONLY; the round-8
		-- simhover ladder is disarmed, so nothing else writes.
		-- ROUND 11: the R9 auto-run stays DISARMED; only the hardened manual
		-- zz_probe_r9() can run now.
		if R9.auto_enabled and (not R9.ran) and (not R9.active) then
			local panel_now = (r5.sig_now ~= nil and contains_str(r5.sig_now, "dynamic_stats"))
			if panel_now then
				R9.active = true
				R9.origin = "auto: stat panel visible"
			elseif (not R9.wait_spoken) and battle_started() then
				R9.wait_spoken = true
				log("R9 armed: waiting for the stat panel (dynamic_stats) - then ONE"
					.. " name-lookup + context-read run; manual: zz_probe_r9()")
			end
		end
		if R9.active and (not R9.ran) then
			R9.active = false
			R9.ran = true
			pcall(R9.run, R9.origin or "auto")
		end

		if not window_active then return end

		local root = find_by_name(DEFAULT_ROOT)
		if capture_poll(DEFAULT_ROOT, root) then
			polls_in_window = polls_in_window + 1
		end
	end)
	if not ok then
		log("PROBE ERROR (swallowed - engine callbacks stay alive): " .. truncate(err, 160))
	end
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 8b. THE MOUSE EVENT BODIES (run in the engine's event context: tiny, pcall-
--     walled, and they only record a pending arm - the tick does the work)
-- ============================================================================

-- Pull the component id and address out of an event context. context.string is
-- the component's id (the main mod's proven field); context.component is the
-- component address string ("Pointer<Component> (0x...)"). If string is empty,
-- fall back to Id() on the component.
local function event_id_and_addr(context)
	local id_text = nil
	local addr_text = nil
	if context == nil then return nil, nil end
	if context.string ~= nil then id_text = safe_text(context.string) end
	if context.component ~= nil then addr_text = safe_text(context.component) end
	if (id_text == nil or id_text == "") and context.component ~= nil then
		local c = wrap(context.component)
		if c ~= nil then
			local ok_i, raw = pcall(function() return c:Id() end)
			id_text = text_of(raw, ok_i)
		end
	end
	return id_text, addr_text
end

local function mouse_on_body(context)
	local id_text, addr_text = event_id_and_addr(context)
	local reason = mouse_event_is_card(id_text, addr_text)
	if reason == nil then return end
	mouse_arm_id = id_text or addr_text or "?"
	mouse_arm_addr = addr_text
	mouse_arm_reason = reason
	mouse_arm_pending = true
	mouse_off_tick = nil                 -- a fresh hover cancels a pending close
end

local function mouse_off_body(context)
	if not window_active or window_why ~= "mouse" then return end
	local id_text, addr_text = event_id_and_addr(context)
	if window_arm_addr ~= nil and addr_text == window_arm_addr then
		mouse_off_tick = tick_count
	elseif window_arm_id ~= nil and id_text == window_arm_id then
		mouse_off_tick = tick_count
	elseif mouse_event_is_card(id_text, addr_text) ~= nil then
		mouse_off_tick = tick_count
	end
end


-- ============================================================================
-- 9. START IT UP (mouse listeners + registration + console hooks)
-- ============================================================================

-- The mouse listeners. The registration idiom is copied from the main mod
-- (core:add_listener(name, event, condition, callback, true)); the condition is
-- unfiltered ON PURPOSE (the label is taken from the event), and each body runs
-- behind a pcall - an error escaping a listener can break the battle.
local mouse_on_registered = false
local mouse_off_registered = false

local ok_lon, err_lon = pcall(function()
	core:add_listener(
		"zz_probe_ui_mouse_on",
		"ComponentMouseOn",
		function(context) return true end,
		function(context)
			local ok, err = pcall(mouse_on_body, context)
			if not ok then
				log("mouse-on handler error (swallowed - the battle stays alive): "
					.. truncate(err, 160))
			end
		end,
		true
	)
end)
mouse_on_registered = ok_lon

local ok_loff, err_loff = pcall(function()
	core:add_listener(
		"zz_probe_ui_mouse_off",
		"ComponentMouseOff",
		function(context) return true end,
		function(context)
			local ok, err = pcall(mouse_off_body, context)
			if not ok then
				log("mouse-off handler error (swallowed - the battle stays alive): "
					.. truncate(err, 160))
			end
		end,
		true
	)
end)
mouse_off_registered = ok_loff

function zz_probe_ui(root_name)
	local ok, ran = pcall(one_shot, root_name)
	if not ok then
		return PROBE_TAG .. "error: " .. tostring(ran)
	end
	if not ran then
		return PROBE_TAG .. "no walk (root absent or childless) - see " .. LOG_FILE
	end
	return PROBE_TAG .. "one-shot walk done - see " .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_ui_arm(seconds)
	local s = tonumber(seconds) or 60
	if s < 5 then s = 5 end
	if s > 300 then s = 300 end
	manual_arm_seconds = s
	return PROBE_TAG .. "capture window armed for " .. tostring(s) .. " s - hover the unit card NOW"
		.. " (capture starts within " .. tostring(POLL_MS) .. " ms). Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_ui_status()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "windows used=" .. tostring(window_index)
		.. " mouse=" .. tostring(mouse_captures_started) .. "/" .. tostring(MAX_MOUSE_CAPTURES)
		.. " manual=" .. tostring(manual_windows_started)
		.. " active=" .. tostring(window_active)
		.. " polls=" .. tostring(tick_count)
		.. " log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_ui_help()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "HOVER a unit card: ComponentMouseOn arms a " .. tostring(MOUSE_SECONDS)
		.. " s capture, polling every " .. tostring(POLL_MS) .. " ms; only new/changed text is logged."
		.. " MANUAL re-run: zz_probe_ui_arm(60) BEFORE hovering."
		.. " ROUND 7: NO automatic windows - a hover or the manual hook only."
		.. " One-shot: zz_probe_ui('hud_battle'). Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

-- ROUND 4 manual hooks: the targeted stat dump. Call with the unit-details
-- panel pinned open. zz_probe_stat_dump() rescans and dumps every seed root;
-- zz_probe_stat_dump('root id') dumps one named root.
function zz_probe_stat_dump(root_name)
	local ok, res = pcall(function()
		if root_name ~= nil and root_name ~= "" then
			local name = tostring(root_name)
			local root, how = resolve_root(name)
			if root == nil then root, how = find_by_id_under_hud(name) end
			if root == nil then
				log("===== STAT DUMP (manual: zz_probe_stat_dump('" .. name
					.. "')) ROOT NOT FOUND =====")
				return PROBE_TAG .. "stat dump: root '" .. name
					.. "' not found (Find / FindByScriptTag / SequentialFind / hud search) - see "
					.. LOG_FILE
			end
			log("")
			log("===== STAT DUMP (manual: zz_probe_stat_dump('" .. name
				.. "')) found via " .. tostring(how) .. " t=" .. tostring(tick_count) .. " =====")
			local ref = { [1] = 0 }
			stat_dump_visit(root, 0, name, ref)
			log("--- manual root done: " .. tostring(ref[1]) .. " component(s) visited ---")
			return PROBE_TAG .. "stat dump done (" .. tostring(ref[1]) .. " components) - see " .. LOG_FILE
		end
		local sig = stat_watch_scan()
		if sig ~= nil then stat_visible_sig = sig end
		stat_do_dump("manual: zz_probe_stat_dump()", stat_scan_seeds, stat_scan_cards)
		return PROBE_TAG .. "stat dump done (" .. tostring(#stat_scan_seeds)
			.. " seed + " .. tostring(#stat_scan_cards) .. " card roots) - see " .. LOG_FILE
	end)
	if not ok then return PROBE_TAG .. "stat dump error: " .. tostring(res) end
	return res
end

function zz_probe_stat_status()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "stat dumps=" .. tostring(stat_dump_count) .. "/" .. tostring(STAT_DUMP_MAX)
		.. " last visible-set=" .. q(stat_visible_sig)
		.. " seeds=" .. tostring(#stat_scan_seeds) .. " cards=" .. tostring(#stat_scan_cards)
		.. " | seed roots: CcoUnitStat*, dynamic_stats, template_stat,"
		.. " health_and_stats_parent, row_header_stats, stats_toggle (fallback: unit card)"
		.. " | log=" .. LOG_FILE
end

function zz_probe_stat_help()
	return PROBE_TAG .. "TARGETED STAT DUMP: open AND PIN the unit-details panel;"
		.. " when a stat becomes visible the probe dumps the whole stat subtree"
		.. " (depth " .. tostring(STAT_MAX_DEPTH) .. ", " .. tostring(STAT_MAX_VISITS)
		.. " visits TOTAL per dump, text/stat rows only). Manual: zz_probe_stat_dump()"
		.. " or zz_probe_stat_dump('root id'). Grep the log for 'STAT DUMP' and"
		.. " '***STAT-LIKE***'. Log: " .. LOG_FILE
end

-- APPEND-ONLY ROUND HEADER on load (a new session is always marked).
log("loaded from script/battle/mod/ (auto-load proof). Log file: " .. LOG_FILE
	.. " | MOUSE-ARMED: hovering a unit card arms a " .. tostring(MOUSE_SECONDS)
	.. " s capture (poll every " .. tostring(POLL_MS) .. " ms, logs ONLY new/changed text)"
	.. " | NO automatic windows (round 7)"
	.. " | cap " .. tostring(MAX_VISITS) .. " visits, depth " .. tostring(MAX_DEPTH)
	.. " | manual: zz_probe_ui_arm(60)")

log("ROUND 4: targeted stat dump armed - seeds CcoUnitStat* / dynamic_stats /"
	.. " template_stat / health_and_stats_parent / row_header_stats / stats_toggle"
	.. " (fallback: the unit card); a NON-EMPTY visible-stat set triggers ONE full"
	.. " dump (ROUND 7 SLIM: depth " .. tostring(STAT_MAX_DEPTH) .. ", "
	.. tostring(STAT_MAX_VISITS) .. " visits TOTAL, text/stat rows only); manual: zz_probe_stat_dump() /"
	.. " zz_probe_stat_dump('root id'); status: zz_probe_stat_status()")

log("ROUND 5 (its AUTO ladder is DISARMED by round 6 - the manual hooks below remain):"
	.. " cross-unit experiment - when the stat panel becomes visible"
	.. " (dynamic_stats) ONE automatic run of 4 labelled tests QUEUED in round 5: R5.1"
	.. " GetContextObject reads (read-only), R5.2 SetContextObject candidates"
	.. " (selected AND non-selected units), R5.3 select_in_ui on a non-selected"
	.. " unit, R5.4 SimulateMouseOn on another card (released with SimulateMouseOff);"
	.. " caps: " .. tostring(R5.max_runs) .. " runs / " .. tostring(R5.max_sets) .. " sets / "
	.. tostring(R5.max_selects) .. " selects / " .. tostring(R5.max_sims) .. " sims;"
	.. " manual: zz_probe_r5() / zz_probe_r5_context() / zz_probe_r5_setctx() /"
	.. " zz_probe_r5_select() / zz_probe_r5_hover(); status: zz_probe_r5_status()")

log("ROUND 7: zero-write read experiment ready - every ~2.5 s (and during hover"
	.. " captures) the probe reads BOTH cards' CcoBattleUnit contexts via"
	.. " common.get_context_value (" .. tostring(#R7.fields) .. " fields; the non-selected"
	.. " card included - its id comes from GetContextObjectId) and the stat panel's"
	.. " compared rows (label_compare); change-only, pcall-walled, and ZERO writes:"
	.. " every former SetContextObject / select_in_ui / SimulateMouseOn call site is"
	.. " REMOVED (the R5/R6 ladders log R7-SKIP; R6's auto pass is disarmed)."
	.. " Manual: zz_probe_r7(); status: zz_probe_r7_status(); log: " .. LOG_FILE)

log("ROUND 9: resolve the stat panel BY NAME first, then read its context objects -"
	.. " LOOKUP unit_information / health_and_stats_parent / dynamic_stats / template_stat /"
	.. " stats_toggle / row_header_stats (one bounded 2000-visit / depth-20 walk ONLY for a"
	.. " name that fails), log the REAL component ids under the panel (stat / dy_value /"
	.. " template / value_holder / bar / label_compare), read GetContextObjectId +"
	.. " GetContextObject (CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit) on the components"
	.. " genuinely FOUND, then run common.get_context_value for StatList.Size / DisplayedValue"
	.. " / Name / Value / ValueBase / ComparisonValue with the selected unit's context id AND"
	.. " with a NON-selected card's ui id. ZERO SetContextObject; the round-8 simhover ladder"
	.. " is DISARMED by default (manual hook only). Manual: zz_probe_r9(); status:"
	.. " zz_probe_r9_status(); log: " .. LOG_FILE)

log("ROUND 8: the DECISIVE EXPERIMENT is ready - PART 1 the ground-truth table"
	.. " (pin the stat panel and click each unit in turn -> 'R8 TRUTH <id>"
	.. " <stat>=<value> ...'); PART 2 the SIMULATED-HOVER LADDER (DISARMED by round 9 -"
	.. " manual only; was SimulateMouseOn"
	.. " then SimulateMouseOff at " .. tostring(R8.holds[1]) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.holds[2])
	.. "/" .. tostring(R8.holds[3]) .. "/" .. tostring(R8.holds[4]) .. " ms holds, polled every "
	.. tostring(R8.poll_ms) .. " ms; one 'R8 SIMHOVER card=.. hold=.. comparison_seen=..'"
	.. " verdict per pass; holds below " .. tostring(R8.visible_ms) .. " ms are invisible=yes);"
	.. " PART 4 the ONE manual select_in_ui test (R8 DESELECT-TEST, OFF by default,"
	.. " zz_probe_r8_toggle_select_test()). ZERO SetContextObject writes. Manual:"
	.. " zz_probe_r8() / zz_probe_r8_status(); log: " .. LOG_FILE)

log("ROUND 6: one-write-per-pass context ladder ready - 3 passes: (1) the selected"
	.. " unit's own cco (CONTROL, auto-runs once when the panel opens), (2) the"
	.. " non-selected unit's cco, (3) the raw battle_unit userdata; ONE SetContextObject"
	.. " write per pass, target dynamic_stats; the probe STOPS after every pass - advance"
	.. " with zz_probe_r6_next() from the console (shift+F3); real type ids: CcoUnitDetails /"
	.. " CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit; the R5 auto ladder is disarmed; status: zz_probe_r6_status();"
	.. " log: " .. LOG_FILE)

log("ROUND 11: COMPLETE UI-root enumeration + hint descent - call zz_probe_r11() once and then"
	.. " zz_probe_r11_step() repeatedly (each call = ONE native call, logged BEFORE it runs, so a"
	.. " crash names its last R11 CALL line). STEP 1-2 are PROVEN SAFE: list the global UI root's"
	.. " top-level children AND every root's children (budget "
	.. "40 each; unit/panel/info/stat/card/left/right/tactical ids tagged as HINTS). STEP 3 descends"
	.. " two levels below every hint node (budget 400 visits, depth 4) to FIND the panel"
	.. " (dynamic_stats/template_stat/stat_name/value_holder/dy_value). STEP 4 reads the stat rows"
	.. " (stat_name -> value_holder/dy_value) and the CcoUnitDetails/CcoUnitStat/CcoBattleUnit"
	.. " context ids (GetContextObjectId). STEP 5 makes ONE common.get_context_value('StatList.Size')"
	.. " with the SELECTED unit's context id, then the same with a NON-selected card's ui id."
	.. " The engine's name-lookup helper is BANNED from this file. zz_probe_r11_auto() runs to the"
	.. " cap. ZERO SetContextObject. log: " .. LOG_FILE)

log("R13 TOTAL STEPS 7 - you are done after step 7. ROUND 13: descend EVERY top-level root"
	.. " that has children (priority hud_battle, panel_manager, under_advisor_docker, left, right,"
	.. " tactical_hud, menu_bar, then the rest) to DEPTH 8 (1200 visits), matching the CcoUnitStat*"
	.. " PREFIX (case-insensitive) AND the structural names; pair the stat rows; read"
	.. " GetContextObjectId (CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat / CcoBattleUnit); then run EXACTLY TWO"
	.. " common.get_context_value calls - query 1 with the LOCATED context id, query 2 with a"
	.. " NON-selected unit's ui id as text. Call zz_probe_r13() once, then zz_probe_r13_step()"
	.. " SEVEN times (STOP after step 7). Only proven-safe primitives; ZERO SetContextObject;"
	.. " simhover DISARMED; the name-lookup helper is BANNED. zz_probe_r13_auto() runs to the cap."
	.. " log: " .. LOG_FILE)

log("R12 TOTAL STEPS 6 - you are done after step 6. ROUND 12: seed the descent on the"
	.. " NUMERIC unit-id nodes under unit_id_holder, descend to DEPTH 8 (800 visits), locate"
	.. " and pair the stat rows, read GetContextObjectId (CcoUnitDetails / CcoUnitStat /"
	.. " CcoBattleUnit) on the located rows, then run EXACTLY TWO common.get_context_value"
	.. " calls - ONE with the SELECTED unit's context id, ONE with a NON-selected unit's ui id."
	.. " Call zz_probe_r12() once, then zz_probe_r12_step() SIX times (STOP after step 6)."
	.. " Only proven-safe primitives; ZERO SetContextObject; simhover DISARMED; the name-lookup"
	.. " helper is BANNED. zz_probe_r12_auto() runs to the cap. log: " .. LOG_FILE)

if mouse_on_registered then
	log("mouse listener registered: ComponentMouseOn / ComponentMouseOff -> a hover on a unit card"
		.. " arms a " .. tostring(MOUSE_SECONDS) .. " s capture (reporters are subscribed on card-like"
		.. " components + the cards panel)")
else
	log("mouse listener registration FAILED: " .. truncate(err_lon, 160)
		.. " - the manual hook zz_probe_ui_arm(60) still works (hover capture needs the listener)")
end

-- ROUND 8: the decisive-experiment ladder's OWN 50 ms poll. It is registered
-- BEFORE the main poll so the main poll stays the primary callback.
local ok_reg8, err_reg8 = pcall(function()
	bm:repeat_callback(r8_poll, R8.poll_ms, R8_POLL_NAME)
end)
if ok_reg8 then
	log("R8 poll registered: " .. R8_POLL_NAME .. " every " .. tostring(R8.poll_ms)
		.. " ms (round 8: the ground-truth table + the simulated-hover ladder)")
else
	log("R8 poll registration FAILED: " .. truncate(err_reg8, 160)
		.. " - the ladder cannot run without it")
end

local ok_reg, err_reg = pcall(function()
	bm:repeat_callback(zz_probe_ui_tick, POLL_MS, POLL_NAME)
end)
if ok_reg then
	log("poll registered: " .. POLL_NAME .. " every " .. tostring(POLL_MS)
		.. " ms (walks only inside an armed window)")
else
	log("poll registration FAILED: " .. truncate(err_reg, 160)
		.. " - use the console: zz_probe_ui_arm(60)")
end
